{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten","id":506852,"title":"Sidereals, how much is forgotten","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-07T08:34:43-07:00","id":506852,"title":"Sidereals, how much is forgotten","content":"You know, i never got how much is it that a person forgets when the sids leave the area.<br /> My main concern was, does the lessons taugth bys the sidreal would also be forgotten. For example if one goes all christmas ghost on someone will the person continue to be kind and leave behind his greedy self forever or after 2 months he goes back to normal and the town belive him being nice was just a bout of insanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:41:59-07:00","id":506884,"title":"","content":"Lessons taught or information shared is not forgotten. The Sidereal who did the teaching is forgotten. Most of the time you simply don't remember who taught you. Other times, someone else will fill in the gap in the memory.<br /> <br /> You are basically an unsung hero as a Sidereal. You do all these great things, but no one remembers it was you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:57:53-07:00","id":506903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=506884#post506884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are basically an unsung hero as a Sidereal. You do all these great things, but no one remembers it was you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you skip out on bar tabs, leave a string of broken hearts behind you, and ignore jury summons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T09:11:15-07:00","id":506911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=506903#post506903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you skip out on bar tabs, leave a string of broken hearts behind you, and ignore jury summons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was Flynn, my Chosen of Serenity, before...things happened. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T10:37:23-07:00","id":506978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=506884#post506884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are basically an unsung hero as a Sidereal. You do all these great things, but no one remembers it was you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can murder thousands or millions of people with no consequences whatsoever. Which was the whole point of Arcane Fate after all. Never again being accountable for any actions, no matter how extreme, unless they anger the Bureau of Destiny higher ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T10:55:25-07:00","id":506983,"title":"","content":"The Bureau of Destiny is not well portrayed if everyone ranking above &quot;field agent&quot; is an apathetic or sociopathic shitbird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T11:04:20-07:00","id":507001,"title":"","content":"The Bureau of Destiny didn't not-care that the Sidereals instigated the Usurpation; they just couldn't prove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T12:07:52-07:00","id":507085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507001#post507001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bureau of Destiny didn't not-care that the Sidereals instigated the Usurpation; they just couldn't prove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, no accountability unless you anger a more powerful Sidereal enough that they actually bother to take it out on you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:02:21-07:00","id":507102,"title":"","content":"That is the beauty of being a Siddie. You show up. Do stuff. Go home. Then get forgotten. If that stuff ostensibly helps Creation? Yay for you. If not, then someone will eventually find out about it. When that person does, if they have a moral code, then you are in trouble. If they do not? You are golden until someone else finds out. Similar to any agency in Creation. As the 11th Commandment states: Thou shalt not get caught.<br /> With Sidereals, it is difficult but not impossible for them to get caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:21:12-07:00","id":507111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=506978#post506978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can murder thousands or millions of people with no consequences whatsoever. Which was the whole point of Arcane Fate after all. Never again being accountable for any actions, no matter how extreme, unless they anger the Bureau of Destiny higher ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. No.<br /> <br /> Arcane Fate is an <i>unintended consequence</i>. The Sidereals were not planning to break the Mask. That just happened because the need to avoid being purged in the wake of the Usurpation caused them to overstress it. It was <i>supposed</i> to be a one-off.<br /> <br /> Second of all, there are other organs of the Heavenly Bureaucracy aside from the Bureau of Destiny, and they have just as much power to hold Sidereals accountable for crimes against their specific society. It is true that at this point Heaven is so corrupt that that isn't much of a guarantee of justice being served... but the Sidereals didn't know that was going to happen (they don't see <i>everything</i>, after all) and they are not happy about it. At the time of the Usurpation Heaven was still <i>functional </i>and they had every expectation it would remain that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In that case, no accountability unless you anger a more powerful Sidereal enough that they actually bother to take it out on you. </div> </div> </div>Also not true. The Sidereals have political enemies who love to move against them, and having actual, for-real dirt on the Sids just makes that even easier.<br /> <br /> Example: in 2E, the head of the Convention of Air was executed for criminal activity. It is implied that they weren't actually guilty, although they were probably guilty of something, but a powerful, veteran Sidereal, in good standing with the Bronze Faction, with lots of hard-to-replace experience, was hauled in front of a censor and <i>killed</i>, and Kejak couldn't do shit about it.<br /> <br /> That's not precisely justice, but it is a form of accountability that comes outside of the Bureau of Destiny. If a Sidereal rolls around committing all kinds of crimes, well, there are interested parties in holding them accountable, not necessarily because of BURNING JUSTICE, but because they want the Sids taken down a peg.<br /> <br /> It is worth noting: when I speak of &quot;crimes&quot; I mean &quot;crimes from the <i>perspective of Heaven</i>.&quot; Heaven doesn't necessarily care that you killed and raped your way across An-Teng; they care if you didn't fill out the proper forms to do that or trespassed in the rightful sphere of influence of a god or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:28:59-07:00","id":507114,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind Arcane Fate isn't a perfect affect by any means. There are a lot of gods, including Celestial Lions, who can trivially make the roll to remember Sids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:38:16-07:00","id":507117,"title":"","content":"2e really did swing too far the other way in its portrayal of Sidereals and the rest of heaven having only a terrible relationship. A better balance is needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T13:44:59-07:00","id":507137,"title":"","content":"I think a comic in the Sidereal Corebook portrayed this beautifully. It was a woman and her two daughters arguing the details about a guy who came through and killed a monster in the forest.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, she likes him but she can't even remember his name.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;... I'm drawing a blank.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Remember? He had red hair?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, his hair was gray, like his beard.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, you mean that soldier who killed that beast in the forest?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;*Grumbles* He didn't have a beard.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, what happened is remembered, its just that for most common folk they'll have trouble remembering the small things. They seem to remember that he was a male, and that he used the story of &quot;I got lost from my troop, hold on let me take care of that thing in the forest-&quot;, but beyond that things get murky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:48:17-07:00","id":507238,"title":"","content":"The idea that the Sidereals are using Arcane Fate to avoid punishment for the Usurpation assumes that Yu-Shan officially follows &quot;innocent until proven guilty&quot; which just seems odd given that Heaven's laws are presented as being so unfair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:56:34-07:00","id":507247,"title":"","content":"The general consensus is people forget exactly as much as they need to for it to be a pain for the Sidereal, no less, no more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:57:51-07:00","id":507250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507238#post507238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that the Sidereals are using Arcane Fate to avoid punishment for the Usurpation assumes that Yu-Shan officially follows &quot;innocent until proven guilty&quot; which just seems odd given that Heaven's laws are presented as being so unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> There are plenty of countries, both right now and historically, in the real world that have legal systems that simultaneously use an &quot;innocent until proven guilty&quot; rubric for judicial proceedings and are chock full of laws that are brutally unfair and unjust, with corruption layered on top for good measure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:09:13-07:00","id":507257,"title":"","content":"My opinion, the breaking of the Mask and Arcane was pretty much absolutely intended by the Sidereal to allow them to murder 300 very dangerous people (the Solars), then avoid being themselves murdered by their 300 (or more) dangerous allies (the Lunars). <br /> <br /> (I think it was mostly the Lunars, because I don't think anyone else really would've been keen to avenge the Solars by that point (surely not Heaven, for whom &quot;Solars all gone, suddenly no one living in Creation can remember much about Sidereals... Huh, what?&quot; would lead to some level of putting two and two together, you would think).)<br /> <br /> If the Lunars know all about the Sidereals in the new edition, enough to be waging a war against them, I'm not sure it does this very well, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:20:35-07:00","id":507268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507257#post507257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion, the breaking of the Mask and Arcane was pretty much absolutely intended by the Sidereal to allow them to murder 300 very dangerous people (the Solars), then avoid being themselves murdered by their 300 (or more) dangerous allies (the Lunars).<br /> <br /> (I think it was mostly the Lunars, because I don't think anyone else really would've been keen to avenge the Solars by that point (surely not Heaven, for whom &quot;Solars all gone, suddenly no one living in Creation can remember much about Sidereals... Huh, what?&quot; would lead to some level of putting two and two together, you would think).)<br /> <br /> If the Lunars know all about the Sidereals in the new edition, enough to be waging a war against them, I'm not sure it does this very well, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Breaking of the Mask was, again, not intentional, and the working that resulted in the Breaking of the Mask wasn't aimed at Lunars. Most Lunars have sufficient scores in the relevant statistics to auto-succeed on the roll to remember Sidereals, and it is important to note that Arcane Fate provides no protection for generalized knowledge of the Sidereals, only specific ones.<br /> <br /> It was aimed at the fact that the Sidereals stormed Lytek's office and held him prisoner for days and days on end while hoovering up all the Solar Exaltations coming to him for maintenance. This would be the rough equivalent of the Delta Force storming the Pentagon, holding the Joint Chiefs hostage, and sinking all of the the U.S's nuclear carriers... and then <i>expecting to go back to their normal jobs</i> afterwards.<br /> <br /> They had to figure out a way for the entire Bronze Faction to not end up rounded up and executed by literally thousands of pissed-off gods, and their crazy-ass Mask working was a way to do it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:29:14-07:00","id":507277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507268#post507268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane Fate provides no protection for generalized knowledge of the Sidereals, only specific ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm talking about personal accountability for personally committed acts, not being opposed by somebody who just hates Sidereals in general, and you happened to be one.<br /> <br /> What are the actual circumstances under which a non-Sidereal can remember a Sidereal's face and name and deeds, and connect those three together, and also know they're a Sidereal? This isn't explained in the corebook, so my understanding is vague beyond &quot;nobody inside Fate remembers them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-07-2015, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:37:56-07:00","id":507288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507268#post507268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Breaking of the Mask was, again, not intentional, and the working that resulted in the Breaking of the Mask wasn't aimed at Lunars. Most Lunars have sufficient scores in the relevant statistics to auto-succeed on the roll to remember Sidereals, and it is important to note that Arcane Fate provides no protection for generalized knowledge of the Sidereals, only specific ones</div> </div> </div> </div>Memory might be off on this, do you wanna chuck some First Edition Sidereals cites on that at me? I haven't got the books to hand either or the time to look through them either though, so no probs if that's not possible for you either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:05:24-07:00","id":507480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507277#post507277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm talking about personal accountability for personally committed acts, not being opposed by somebody who just hates Sidereals in general, and you happened to be one.<br /> <br /> What are the actual circumstances under which a non-Sidereal can remember a Sidereal's face and name and deeds, and connect those three together, and also know they're a Sidereal? This isn't explained in the corebook, so my understanding is vague beyond &quot;nobody inside Fate remembers them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually super simple, and the mechanics are very similar across editions. I'm going to use the 2E ones, but the 1E ones are pretty similar.<br /> <br /> First of all, four categories of beings automatically are immune to Arcane Fate:<ul><li>Other Sidereals</li> <li>All Celestial gods and all beings outside of Fate</li> <li>Any official or functionary of the Bureau of Destiny</li> <li>Acquaintances and Familiars of the Sidereal in question</li> </ul><br /> So damn near anyone in Yu-Shan a Sidereal is likely to meet doesn't give a shit about Arcane Fate.<br /> <br /> For everyone else? Wits + Integrity roll, difficulty 1, -3 dice pool penalty. You have to make this roll every time you try and remember the Sidereal as a Sidereal until you fulfill one of three conditions:<ul><li>You succeed with more successes than the Sids Essence rating on a single roll. From then on you remember them and don't need to roll.</li> <li>You succeed on a number of rolls equal to the Sids Essence rating. From then on you remember them and don't need to roll.</li> <li>You fail. You forget them.</li> </ul><br /> The thing is, it is not hard to do that for a lot of Exalts. A lot of Lunars are going to have a dice pool that lets them take an auto-success on that roll. Hell, it's possible for a mortal to have a dice pool that lets them take an auto-success on that roll, with appropriate specialties. The rules explicitly allow Excellencies to be invoked and Willpower to be spent on this roll.<br /> <br /> Extras are gonna forget about a Sidereals en masse real real quick. Other people? Not so much. This is why they stooge around wearing Resplendencies and assumed identities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507288#post507288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Memory might be off on this, do you wanna chuck some First Edition Sidereals cites on that at me? I haven't got the books to hand either or the time to look through them either though, so no probs if that's not possible for you either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mechanically or fluff-wise?<br /> <br /> Mechanically it's substantially similar to 2E. There are some differences (it's Wits + Occult, not Integrity, and the intervals for rolling are different) but basically the same roll.<br /> <br /> Fluff-wise, the breaking of the Mask in 1e was very hand-wavey. There isn't an explicit reason given for it, it's just sort of stated &quot;the Sidereals were withdrawing from the world after the Solar Purge, and they used the Mask so much in such a short period of time they busted it.&quot; That's on page 120-121 of the 1e Sids core. However, it is explicitly in 1e still an accident. They didn't mean for it to happen, and it is an inconvenience to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:26:24-07:00","id":507498,"title":"","content":"Alright, so it affects most mortals and lower-power Terrestrial spirits, and really slow-witted Exalted, and nobody else?<br /> (I've only glanced into the Arcane Fate section of the 1e book on one occasion, but IIRC it said gods also forget them.)<br /> <br /> So if it provides them no legal immunity for abducting Lytek or whatever, and it was purely an accident, and is pure downside, why has nobody tried to fix it in 1500 years? I remember a thread about this idea earlier, and the consensus I remember was that the Bronze Faction leaders had deliberately broken the Mask and wanted to keep it that way to protect themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-07-2015, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:47:17-07:00","id":507512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507498#post507498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so it affects most mortals and lower-power Terrestrial spirits, and really slow-witted Exalted, and nobody else?<br /> (I've only glanced into the Arcane Fate section of the 1e book on one occasion, but IIRC it said gods also forget them.)<br /> <br /> So if it provides them no legal immunity for abducting Lytek or whatever, and it was purely an accident, and is pure downside, why has nobody tried to fix it in 1500 years? I remember a thread about this idea earlier, and the consensus I remember was that the Bronze Faction leaders had deliberately broken the Mask and wanted to keep it that way to protect themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Arcane Fate by itself doesn't provide them legal immunity, but the working they did of which Arcane Fate is a side effect does; they fucked up that specific period of their history so badly nobody can prove a damn thing. Even the Sidereals who were actually involved in it don't really remember what happened or who was responsible for doing what anymore.<br /> <br /> As for trying to reverse it... well, it was only Jupiter's personal intervention that saved the Mask from disintegrating entirely. So it would be a major, risky undertaking. And maybe if it works, it not only undoes Arcane Fate, but it undoes the obfuscation around the Usurpation and a bunch of Bronzies end up executed. And given their already hectic schedules, can you blame them for not being too interested in trying?<br /> <br /> Undoing Arcane Fate would be a Big Fucking Deal. Not quite &quot;remove the Great Curse&quot; but up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:53:59-07:00","id":507514,"title":"","content":"If they almost destroyed the entire constellation, why didn't even the Maidens hold them responsible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T20:35:05-07:00","id":507574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507514#post507514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they almost destroyed the entire constellation, why didn't even the Maidens hold them responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>That I can't answer. The Maidens are the Maidens, they're both functionally insane and inscrutable. The only real explanation I have is &quot;if the non-Sol Incarnae had reacted to the various levels of bullshit that happened to/because of their Exalted during the Usurpation by intervening in productive ways, we wouldn't have a setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> (This is the point where the discussion usually segues into the degree to which the Incarnae's disengagement from the setting and the degree to which they allow their Exalted to run wild and free is believable or not. I enjoy the hell out of that discussion, but sometimes it is productive and sometimes it is not.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T20:38:51-07:00","id":507577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507514#post507514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they almost destroyed the entire constellation, why didn't even the Maidens hold them responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, as with virtually every question involving why the Maidens do or do not do anything, there's a plausible answer in, &quot;Because that wasn't what the Maidens foresaw themselves doing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T20:38:57-07:00","id":507578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507514#post507514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they almost destroyed the entire constellation, why didn't even the Maidens hold them responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows?<br /> <br /> Murcushio's pretty much laid out <i>everything</i> the books in both editions say about Arcane Fate. It's the result of the Breaking of the Mask, the Breaking was accidental,* the point of the Breaking was to cover up the Usurpation,** the Maidens had to fix it and it has a very weak mechanical effect but a profound narrative impact.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the mechanics of Arcane Fate do essentially allow Sidereal players to join a circle without a Resplendent Destiny and have all of the other Exalted easily remember them. Arcane Fate is a thing which happens to NPCs, by and large.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Or, as people who don't like Sidereals would rejoin, the book says that <i>most Sidereals</i> think it was an accident.<br /> **2e Sidereals specifies that it was to cover up the attack on Lytek's office, because that was way more important to Heaven than murdering all of the Solars and destroying civilization. As much as I know the author must have enjoyed dissing the Celestial Bureaucracy like that, most gods were way more hurt in the end by the destruction of the Old Realm than Lytek being terrorized for a bit. Not that I'm saying they wouldn't care, just that they should <i>also</i> care about the other thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:09:36-07:00","id":507608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507578#post507578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> **2e Sidereals specifies that it was to cover up the attack on Lytek's office, because that was way more important to Heaven than murdering all of the Solars and destroying civilization. As much as I know the author must have enjoyed dissing the Celestial Bureaucracy like that, most gods were way more hurt in the end by the destruction of the Old Realm than Lytek being terrorized for a bit. Not that I'm saying they wouldn't care, just that they should <i>also</i> care about the other thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, personally, chalk that up to a failure of presentation rather than a failure of concept.<br /> <br /> Nuking the Old Realm from orbit may not have actually been a crime; I think the Bureau of Destiny could make a plausible case for &quot;we're doing our jobs; it is explicitly in our ambit to pick and choose amongst possible Destinies and then make them happen when we deem it appropriate for the good of Creation. We picked this one. Our bosses have signaled at least a form of assent by refusing to get involved; you got a problem with that, the Jade Pleasure Dome is right over there.&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of the Celestial Bureacracy would have been really upset by that, but they wouldn't necessarily have had the chops to do anything about it, especially since at the time Heaven was still mostly functional instead of mostly not. But assaulting Lytek... that's something they can do something about, an actual crime. Also, it's important to remember that Lytek wasn't just some random Important God, he was the Left Hand of Power, the highest-ranking god in Heaven who isn't an Incarnae. If the Sidereals can slap him around, they can slap anyone around. <i>Nobody is safe</i>.<br /> <br /> That's an avenue for the gods of the Celestial Bureaucracy who were royally honked off about the Sidereals destroying the Realm to get their own back. That, in my opinion, is how it should have been portrayed. Instead it comes off as &quot;the gods don't really give a fuck about the Usurpation, just that one of their own was violated.&quot; And it really should be both, as you said, Mercury.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T22:22:42-07:00","id":507685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507608#post507608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I, personally, chalk that up to a failure of presentation rather than a failure of concept.<br /> <br /> Nuking the Old Realm from orbit may not have actually been a crime</div> </div> </div> </div>You're fucking with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T00:13:37-07:00","id":507768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507111#post507111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example: in 2E, the head of the Convention of Air was executed for criminal activity. It is implied that they weren't actually guilty, although they were probably guilty of something, but a powerful, veteran Sidereal, in good standing with the Bronze Faction, with lots of hard-to-replace experience, was hauled in front of a censor and <i>killed</i>, and Kejak couldn't do shit about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals being executed by Heaven is also something hatewheel has explictly said is going away in 3e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hatewheel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that there have been problems with the way Sidereals have been depicted, especially in how they operate mindlessly and without question, and especially in how the gods seethe with hatred and resentment for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Q: Can you talk a bit about what you mean by &quot;dropping the negative context of their entire presentation from 2e&quot;? <b>(ADamiani)</b></i> A: Negative elements I'm dropping: the gods hate the Sidereals, Venus signed off on the Usurpation (UGH), Sidereals being executed by Heaven (what) and others that I can't recall off the top of my head. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fluff-wise, the breaking of the Mask in 1e was very hand-wavey. There isn't an explicit reason given for it, it's just sort of stated &quot;the Sidereals were withdrawing from the world after the Solar Purge, and they used the Mask so much in such a short period of time they busted it.&quot; That's on page 120-121 of the 1e Sids core. However, it is explicitly in 1e still an accident. They didn't mean for it to happen, and <b>it is an inconvenience to them.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine, but you seem to have misspelled &quot;best thing ever&quot; there.<br /> As usual, Big Boss can demonstrate why Arcane Fate is the best and most fun thing in the entire game:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img537/9499/cq2hvx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507514#post507514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they almost destroyed the entire constellation, why didn't even the Maidens hold them responsible?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maidens really do have a lid on it. The current theory is that they use mellow jazz, bongo drums, and a huge bag of weed to relax.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507578#post507578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the mechanics of Arcane Fate do essentially allow Sidereal players to join a circle without a Resplendent Destiny and have all of the other Exalted easily remember them. Arcane Fate is a thing which happens to NPCs, by and large.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also technically no rule against making a Resplendant Destiny of what is essentially yourself to use for talking to people, so long as you observe the rules that you can't imitate a specific person and can't use the same identity twice (and also that it takes up one of your slots and Paradox, but that's an entirely different rant). Most games I've been involved in allowed slightly different spellings or pronounciations of the name to be enough to count as a &quot;seperate&quot; identity (which also helps in that any given Sidereal is probably going to be carrying a few burner resplendencies for the powers and thus doesn't have to waste time coming up with names or backgrounds for them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T00:22:45-07:00","id":507786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507111#post507111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example: in 2E, the head of the Convention of Air was executed for criminal activity. It is implied that they weren't actually guilty, although they were probably guilty of something, but a powerful, veteran Sidereal, in good standing with the Bronze Faction, with lots of hard-to-replace experience, was hauled in front of a censor and <i>killed</i>, and Kejak couldn't do shit about it.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never really understood why this sort of thing can happen. It seems to me that the Sids are powerful enough that if they just banded together, the gods would all be too scared to actually do anything to them. If I'm some Essence 7 lesser elemental dragon Censor, do I really want to kill somebody who's friends and allies with the Essence 10 master-of-every-SMA-in-existence most powerful Exalt alive? Sounds like a good way to get turned into a rock or something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T00:42:48-07:00","id":507802,"title":"","content":"To be fair, this Essence 7 Censor is, firstly, extremely powerful, more than most Sidereals, he's hardly lowly (there are a total of 5 Censors in Creation, they're a big deal), and secondly he's probably got a whole bunch of contacts and friends himself.<br /> <br /> And Kejak certainly wouldn't punch a Dragon and turn it into a rock. That's crass. The Sidereals would much rather use the corrupt legal system to have him officially banished to the Pole of Water or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T01:11:10-07:00","id":507808,"title":"","content":"The idea that the astrology that broke the Mask was to keep the Sidereals from being prosecuted in Heaven for plotting against the Solars and that they <i>actually wrote the notion that everybody in Yu-Shan</i> knows <i>they did it but there's no punishment because nobody has hard evidence</i> is so fucking stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T01:11:56-07:00","id":507809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507480#post507480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fluff-wise, the breaking of the Mask in 1e was very hand-wavey. There isn't an explicit reason given for it, it's just sort of stated &quot;the Sidereals were withdrawing from the world after the Solar Purge, and they used the Mask so much in such a short period of time they busted it.&quot; That's on page 120-121 of the 1e Sids core. However, it is explicitly in 1e still an accident. They didn't mean for it to happen, and it is an inconvenience to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> The wording there on p120, in exact terms is <i>&quot;Since the Usurpation, the Sidereals have worked to hide themselves and their manipulations of the world's destiny from the eyes of others. So great, in fact, were their early efforts that the Chosen of Fate have forever twisted that aspect of their own destinies&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Under glossary it is <i>&quot;Arcane Fate: Prolonged manipulation of the Tapestry in the precincts of the constellation known as the Mask has left the destinies of the Sidereal Exalted permanently obscured behind a haze of forgetfulness&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> p62 is likewise <i>&quot;In the time of the Usurpation, the Sidereals used a great deal of powerful Sidereal Astrology to hide themselves from history. This was a wildly improbably (sic) event, as they had been an open part of the apparatus of the Solar Deliberative until then. The succeeded, but only at the cost of permanently damaging that part of the Tapestry - now, it is virtually impossible to remember the Sidereals exist at all&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> It does make sense to read that as unintentional, in part. <br /> <br /> I do feel a little nonplussed though.<br /> <br /> The early books are all like, from the First Edition Core, first mention of Sidereals - &quot;<i>Shortly after the Solars' destruction, the Sidereal Exalted made a concerted effort to fade from view. Texts mentioning them were destroyed, and memories of them were allowed to vanish over mortal lifetimes, until they were only a legend</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I then sort of expected the Sidereal book to be all like &quot;Yes, and that may make us seem like a shadowy conspiracy but this isn't just evil and was unfortunately from our perspective necessary and here's why (another day, another stock trope subverted in favour of a bit more complex humanity - Exalted life)&quot;.<br /> <br /> I didn't really expect the Sidereal book to go &quot;Er... Right. That. Well, honestly, yeah, that was all just a big mistake. Uh.. Frankly we just weren't going for that at all. We didn't really want to disappear from view permanently and manipulate the Immaculate Order behind the scenes, just.. lol, well you know, accidents happen right? When life gives you lemons, Sparkling Beverage Atemi!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T03:19:27-07:00","id":507901,"title":"","content":"Kejack has like three SMAs. If you were going by the (admittedly stupid) experience-by-age rules in 2e, no Sidereal could live long enough <i>to</i> master all the SMAs because they were absurdly pricey.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Guesstimating there, I obviously haven't done the math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-08-2015, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T04:53:53-07:00","id":507944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're fucking with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It seems like there's a case to be made. Heaven interferes with how Earth is run all the time. There are tons of gods whose entire job is &quot;decide how things are gonna be down there and then make it happen.&quot; That's an enormous part of what of the Bureau of Destiny does; sure, the Loom does the heavy lifting, but they do a lot of the work themselves. And once they decide on a course of action, they don't really give a damn about what people outside Yu-Shan think except to the extent that they need to do so for practical reasons.<br /> <br /> The difference between &quot;this Kingdom is fated to fall; thus it has been written. (By us.) Go and ensure this fate comes to pass, Sidereals&quot; and &quot;the Old Realm is fated to fall; thus it has been written. (By us.) Go forth and ensure this fate comes to pass, Sidereals!&quot; seems to be one of degree, rather than kind.<br /> <br /> This doesn't necessarily mean it was a <i>good idea</i>. It just might not (emphasis on might) have actually been in illegal <i>in Yu-Shan</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507768#post507768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sidereals being executed by Heaven is also something hatewheel has explictly said is going away in 3e.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that, and I'd like some context, really, because the incredulity he expressed seems out of line with how... banal the idea that Heaven will occasionally execute a Sidereal is.<br /> <br /> The Realm executes Dragon-Blooded for doin' crimes all the time. The Lunars execute other Lunars for going all chimera and needing to be put down. When you form a society, you generally speaking need to police yourself. That doesn't necessarily mean executions, but in the cultural context of Creation going with something like life imprisonment in the hope of rehabilitation seems like it would make Heaven... surprisingly progressive. Especially given how Exaltations work. I mean, if the Sidereals get their hands on Rakan Thulio, who has declared war on HEaven and created a whole new kind of Exalted to prosecute that war, they're NOT gonna execute him? They're gonna... what? Lock him in a cage for the rest of his natural life? That would be very ethical of them; it would also tie up an Exaltation that could be put to better use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really understood why this sort of thing can happen. It seems to me that the Sids are powerful enough that if they just banded together, the gods would all be too scared to actually do anything to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are 100 Sidereals, of whom at any given time a bunch are unavailable due to the Exaltation being dormant, Ronin, etc. There are literally millions of gods, even the weakest of whom have Charms and are essence-wielders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really expect the Sidereal book to go &quot;Er... Right. That. Well, honestly, yeah, that was all just a big mistake. Uh.. Frankly we just weren't going for that at all. We didn't really want to disappear from view permanently and manipulate the Immaculate Order behind the scenes, just.. lol, well you know, accidents happen right? When life gives you lemons, Sparkling Beverage Atemi!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. No. It... doesn't say that at all.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals DID want to disappear from view permanently, manipulate the Immaculate Order behind the scenes, all that stuff. That was on their agenda!<br /> <br /> What they didn't want to do was turn into beings who vanish from the minds of the vast majority of the people of Creation the second they're no longer in their presence. That's what Arcane Fate does. That's ALL Arcane Fate does. It was not intended. The other stuff was. That specifically? Was not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T05:33:35-07:00","id":507950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507809#post507809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really expect the Sidereal book to go &quot;Er... Right. That. Well, honestly, yeah, that was all just a big mistake. Uh.. Frankly we just weren't going for that at all. We didn't really want to disappear from view permanently and manipulate the Immaculate Order behind the scenes, just.. lol, well you know, accidents happen right? When life gives you lemons, Sparkling Beverage Atemi!&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, &quot;When life gives you murderous carnivore lemons, use Juice Beverage Atemi&quot; is kind of a Sidereal's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T06:08:27-07:00","id":507960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507944#post507944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that, and I'd like some context, really, because the incredulity he expressed seems out of line with how... banal the idea that Heaven will occasionally execute a Sidereal is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The context is the question given, since I'm fairly sure that was from the first &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; question over on rpg.net . The stupidly antagonistic attitude towards Sidereals (and Dragon-Blooded) that Yu-Shan was given in 2e has been discussed several times since then, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't necessarily mean executions, but in the cultural context of Creation going with something like life imprisonment in the hope of rehabilitation seems like it would make Heaven... surprisingly progressive. </div> </div> </div>I doubt it's as much progressive as practical. Generally speaking, what's to be gained from executing Sidereals? Let's see, you remove a valuable agent of Heaven from active duty for 15 - 20 years or so, which is a great idea when everything is going to shit and the Yozi and Malfeans are actively rattling their cages and going around sticking their dicks in people's Cheerios. Every other Sidereal will be gunning for your ass, even if they didn't like the one who got executed, because executing Sidereals is extremely bad precedent as far as they're concerned; even if you're not punched into a duck and then spit roasted, expect to be politically ruined because the entire political capital that the Bureau of Destiny can muster (which given that they're the only bureau that actually still works, largely due to the efforts of the Sidereals, is <i>a fucking lot</i>) will fall directly on your ass.<br /> <br /> I'm actually just tempted to dig up that thread from a few months ago about why Lytek doesn't just piss in the Sidereals' collective Cheerios and say &quot;Pretty much that.&quot;<br /> <br /> From a gameplay perspective, saying that Heaven can and does execute Sidereals is also shit, because that makes Sidereals the only splat with <i>two</i> punishment mechanics that can outright kill them. Paradox can outright do enough damage to kill them, of course (and that's usually my go-to for explaining why that's complete shit), but don't forget that they also had a large section of the 2e book devoted to lovingly detailed trial and penalty mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially given how Exaltations work. I mean, if the Sidereals get their hands on Rakan Thulio, who has declared war on HEaven and created a whole new kind of Exalted to prosecute that war, they're NOT gonna execute him? They're gonna... what? Lock him in a cage for the rest of his natural life? That would be very ethical of them; it would also tie up an Exaltation that could be put to better use. </div> </div> </div>No, I think Raken would get <i>his</i> ass executed. But he's guilty of high treason, sediition and war crimes. The other guy...umm...fuck, I can't even remember what he did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are 100 Sidereals, of whom at any given time a bunch are unavailable due to the Exaltation being dormant, Ronin, etc. There are literally millions of gods, even the weakest of whom have Charms and are essence-wielders. </div> </div> </div>Okay. So how many of them are combatants? How many of them are Essence 1 or 2 scrubs who can't do shit against an Exalt? Perhaps most importantly, how many of them are willing to be the first ones through the door at the Crimson Panoply? How many of them are willing to go up against Terminal Sanction, let alone some of the scarier shit Sidereals who've been around the block can do?<br /> <br /> Now that's not to suggest that I feel the Sidereals are invincible. Far from it. But when you get down to it, what god is going to be suicidal enough to be the example the Sidereals make? Since I've already paraphrased Iron Man, there's no throne there. There's no scenario where they come out on top. <i>Maybe</i> they attack the Sidereals, politically or physically, and <i>maybe</i> it's too much for them, but then it's all on them.<br /> <br /> Seriously, gods fucking with Sidereals in any sort of major or organized fashion is pyrrhic at best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T07:00:04-07:00","id":508010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507250#post507250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the presumption of innocence is a Roman idea (you don't have a girlfriend whose a lawyer without picking up a few facts), but the way it's presented here gives the impression that a modern American author made a pretty big assumption about how Yu-Shan's legal system worked rather than consciously rejecting certain aspects of Traditional Chinese Law because they thought it'd make a better story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T07:13:34-07:00","id":508015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507944#post507944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that, and I'd like some context, really, because the incredulity he expressed seems out of line with how... banal the idea that Heaven will occasionally execute a Sidereal is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know of only one reference to Sidereals being executed; in Kingdom of Halta, in which there's the idea that the circle of Sidereals who destroyed a city using Cantata of Empty Voices were tried on charges of war crimes, found guilty, and executed for that.<br /> <br /> The idea that Yu-Shan even has a concept of war crimes, let alone that they would prosecute Sidereals for that, let alone that Sidereals involved would go along with such proceedings... none of it fits.<br /> <br /> I would say that Sidereals can get punished for crimes in Heaven, but more likely in the manner of services or debts or loss of privileges over execution. It just seems more... practical.<br /> <br /> And those are more likely going to be about breaches of protocol than killing a large number of people.<br /> <br /> There might be deadly intentions towards Rakan Thulio, but I'd say they're closer to assassination than judicially validated execution. Maybe the best he can hope for is a show trial in the manner of what Nazis brought back to Israel got, but that's still distinct from the idea of being charged with a crime and sentenced to death within your own society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm executes Dragon-Blooded for doin' crimes all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem right...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T07:26:54-07:00","id":508023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507960#post507960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The context is the question given, since I'm fairly sure that was from the first &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; question over on rpg.net . The stupidly antagonistic attitude towards Sidereals (and Dragon-Blooded) that Yu-Shan was given in 2e has been discussed several times since then, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the in-setting context. As I said: all the other Exalts who have formed societies have &quot;execution&quot; as an option for sufficiently heinous crimes against their societies, as defined by the rules of said societies. Why should the Sidereals be any different?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt it's as much progressive as practical. Generally speaking, what's to be gained from executing Sidereals? Let's see, you remove a valuable agent of Heaven from active duty for 15 - 20 years or so, which is a great idea when everything is going to shit and the Yozi and Malfeans are actively rattling their cages and going around sticking their dicks in people's Cheerios. Every other Sidereal will be gunning for your ass, even if they didn't like the one who got executed, because executing Sidereals is extremely bad precedent as far as they're concerned; even if you're not punched into a duck and then spit roasted, expect to be politically ruined because the entire political capital that the Bureau of Destiny can muster (which given that they're the only bureau that actually still works, largely due to the efforts of the Sidereals, is <i>a fucking lot</i>) will fall directly on your ass. </div> </div> </div>Except that quite a lot of the time, if a Sidereal has committed sufficient crimes to warrant being executed, the Bureau of Destiny will presumably be part of the group pressing charges, or at least stand aside, no? I mean, there will, logically, be times when the BoD decides &quot;this asshole has had every chance there is; he pisses off the other Bureau's constantly, has ignored reprimands and attempts and remediation, and we keep having to burn boatloads of political capital to keep him out of Torment Cage or from being straight-up killed. He is a liability. The next time someone presses charges, we aren't lifting a finger. Perhaps the next bearer of his Exaltation will be better at this job.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a gameplay perspective, saying that Heaven can and does execute Sidereals is also shit, because that makes Sidereals the only splat with <i>two</i> punishment mechanics that can outright kill them. Paradox can outright do enough damage to kill them, of course (and that's usually my go-to for explaining why that's complete shit), but don't forget that they also had a large section of the 2e book devoted to lovingly detailed trial and penalty mechanics. </div> </div> </div>Wait, what?<br /> <br /> No, they aren't. The Realm can execute Dragon-Blooded for completely spurious reasons! Dragon-Blooded can end up executed or having to flee into exile because they were bad at politics, which is something that won't happen to a Sidereal unless they are also bad at their jobs. Is that a &quot;punishment mechanic&quot; for the Dragon-Blooded? Lunars are executed by the Silver Pact if they fall too far towards chimerism; is that a &quot;punishment mechanic&quot; for the Lunars?<br /> <br /> Part of being part of the Celestial Bureaucracy is needing to play by the rules. A group of PCs playing Dragon-Blooded officers in a Legion would be expected to play by the rules or be subject to discipline; why shouldn't Sidereals?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay. So how many of them are combatants? How many of them are Essence 1 or 2 scrubs who can't do shit against an Exalt? Perhaps most importantly, how many of them are willing to be the first ones through the door at the Crimson Panoply? How many of them are willing to go up against Terminal Sanction, let alone some of the scarier shit Sidereals who've been around the block can do? </div> </div> </div>I dunno. How many Realm soldiers, armed with a pretty good spear and pretty decent armor, you know, for mortals, are willing to be the first one through the door when the time comes to throw an army at a Solar or Lunar warlord? The Realm seems to have no trouble recruiting them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously, gods fucking with Sidereals in any sort of major or organized fashion is pyrrhic at best. </div> </div> </div>So basically, you posit that the faction that is all about heavenly politics... shouldn't have any heavenly politics in it.<br /> <br /> Because politics is the definition of fucking with other people in major, organized fashions. Gods can and should be fucking with the Sidereals in major, organized ways all the time. By getting dirt on the guy who has been doing faction business on company time. By befriending Sidereals who share a political agenda and trading favors. By gaining political leverage over the gods who are the Sidereals bosses (remember, only the highest-ranking Sidereals are management; many of them answer directly to gods) and having those gods give the Sidereals orders that are congenial to your agenda.<br /> <br /> And the Sidereals should be fucking back! They should be <i>playing the political game</i>. If you cut that out you cut out the most interesting bits of them. This isn't even something unique to Heaven or the Realm; this is how all politics have worked, forever. You use the agreed upon conventions and mechanisms of power to ruin your enemies and enact your agenda, and your enemies do the same to you, and the reason the knives don't come out is because it has been tacitly agreed upon that the political process is a better way of doing things than naked force. (The generally lasts until a group decides that naked force needs to be tried, but even so.)<br /> <br /> You seem to be arguing that the gods should be meek little supplicants at the altar of Sidereal power, because any god that messes with them is going to end up regretting it. That's boring. It means the Sidereals can swagger around heaven and fuck up as much as they want and step on the toes of all the gods they want and nobody will say boo. Well, the gods will say boo. Lots of gods are very powerful. Lots of those very powerful gods have friends. They're going to deploy the politics of heaven against those who Done Them Wrong, and one of the consequences Doing Gods Wrong too many times should be you get your ass killed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T07:37:51-07:00","id":508027,"title":"","content":"One might abstract hypothetical scenarios in which a Sidereal conducts themselves in a manner that would warrant some kind of officially sanctioned murder, but inserting that into the context of how small the sample group is and how relatively controlled the selection criteria are and it doesn't really feel very likely.<br /> <br /> Rakan Thulio seems to be a lot more than a Sidereal who conducted himself in a criminal manner or went rogue, he doesn't really seem like he should be used as a baseline for anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:31:18-07:00","id":508185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507786#post507786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never really understood why this sort of thing can happen. It seems to me that the Sids are powerful enough that if they just banded together, the gods would all be too scared to actually do anything to them. If I'm some Essence 7 lesser elemental dragon Censor, do I really want to kill somebody who's friends and allies with the Essence 10 master-of-every-SMA-in-existence most powerful Exalt alive? Sounds like a good way to get turned into a rock or something...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of demongraphics. There are one million celestial lions, which means they outnumber the Sidereals 10,000/1. Throw in lion dogs, the Aerial Legion, censors, and various fighty gods impressed for this purpose and the balance of essence levels, motes, and ability to wreak things is massively in the gods favor. An open war between them is something no one wins but that the Sids lose worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:42:27-07:00","id":508194,"title":"","content":"Seems like the two editions are inconsistent on the breaking of the Mask, and whether Sidereals are held accountable for their actions. But you all seem to agree that the Celestial Bureaucracy doesn't care about murder or destroying a town or whatever, and Sidereals who do that &quot;for the greater good&quot; are mostly immune to Terrestrial consequences.<br /> <br /> I'm not in favor of all gods everywhere disliking Sidereals, but I'm not sure how they could swing all the way to the other side, to never resenting Sidereals, without saying all the gods of Heaven agree on supporting the Usurpation and the Realm, and also don't mind being shoved around or forced to do their jobs by nosy Exalts. I hope 3e presents it in a balanced and plausible manner in between the two extremes, instead of giving the gods one monolithic agenda.<br /> <br /> I do wonder about &quot;every&quot; god knowing that the Sidereals caused the Usurpation and assaulted Lytek and forged the Jade Prison. I feel like the Usurpation connection should at least be pretty clearly plausible to gods who pay attention, since the dominant Sidereal faction is openly anti-Solar, anti-Lunar, and pro-Immaculate. But I think the part about Lytek and the Jade Prison isn't something most Celestial gods could easily find out. Aside from the way the Bronzes messed up that period of history in the Tapestry, the Jade Prison isn't the sort of thing that gets advertised. The Solars mostly stopped reincarnating, and it's really weird, and it obviously has something to do with the Usurpation, and thus maybe with Sol Invictus turning his back on humanity, or maybe with the Sidereals, or who knows!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507768#post507768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maidens really do have a lid on it. The current theory is that they use mellow jazz, bongo drums, and a huge bag of weed to relax.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what that means, it looks like total nonsense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This thread does make me want to write silly, exaggerated taglines for each type of Exalted, starting with Sidereals:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Congratulations! You have been selected to receive Cosmic Power. Your job sucks and nobody will thank you for it. If you fuck up, reality will have a hernia. Even if you have personal time (HAHAHA) say goodbye to a normal social life. Be in the office 5 am sharp tommorow.</i>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-08-2015, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T12:31:59-07:00","id":508282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508185#post508185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are one million celestial lions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cite please? Because that sounds absolutely insane.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T12:37:23-07:00","id":508287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how they could swing all the way to the other side, to never resenting Sidereals, without saying all the gods of Heaven agree on supporting the Usurpation and the Realm, and also don't mind being shoved around or forced to do their jobs by nosy Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div> It makes me think of the HBO Rome series, in which several characters attend one another's parties and make great shows of cordiality and respect, even while lacing those statements with innuendo and implications of contempt, and they're all basically plotting to murder and violate one another. It's not even two-faced, really, it's just all part of the game; the one who breaks decorum and openly attacks first loses, even if they kill the other person, because they let somebody get under their skin, and that means a loss of face. I feel as though that social standard would apply very well to Yu-Shan; the Sidereals and gods respecting one another in a lot of ritual and protocol and acknowledgement of how useful and dutiful they all are, but that doesn't necessarily mean they like each other and aren't plotting for advantages (although I would say that murder is highly uncommon in the Heavenly social scene).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T13:07:44-07:00","id":508359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508282#post508282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cite please? Because that sounds absolutely insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mistaken. Its 10,000. Compass of Celestial Directions Yu-Shan p. 13. Perhaps I was confused with the Million Dragons in the First Age or something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508287#post508287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It makes me think of the HBO Rome series, in which several characters attend one another's parties and make great shows of cordiality and respect, even while lacing those statements with innuendo and implications of contempt, and they're all basically plotting to murder and violate one another. It's not even two-faced, really, it's just all part of the game; the one who breaks decorum and openly attacks first loses, even if they kill the other person, because they let somebody get under their skin, and that means a loss of face. I feel as though that social standard would apply very well to Yu-Shan; the Sidereals and gods respecting one another in a lot of ritual and protocol and acknowledgement of how useful and dutiful they all are, but that doesn't necessarily mean they like each other and aren't plotting for advantages (although I would say that murder is highly uncommon in the Heavenly social scene).</div> </div> </div> </div>As well as being very difficult since all the gods can come back from it and if they don't it will be very obvious that one of the vanishingly small number of people with Ghost Eating Technique or Terminal Sanction was responsible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T15:33:57-07:00","id":508510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508359#post508359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well as being very difficult since all the gods can come back from it and if they don't it will be very obvious that one of the vanishingly small number of people with Ghost Eating Technique or Terminal Sanction was responsible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not quite. A spirit who kills another spirit can destroy it, so if a god dies in Yu-Shan it is probably <i>not</i> the work of the Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T16:00:26-07:00","id":508533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508287#post508287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It makes me think of the HBO Rome series, in which several characters attend one another's parties and make great shows of cordiality and respect, even while lacing those statements with innuendo and implications of contempt, and they're all basically plotting to murder and violate one another. It's not even two-faced, really, it's just all part of the game; the one who breaks decorum and openly attacks first loses, even if they kill the other person, because they let somebody get under their skin, and that means a loss of face. I feel as though that social standard would apply very well to Yu-Shan; the Sidereals and gods respecting one another in a lot of ritual and protocol and acknowledgement of how useful and dutiful they all are, but that doesn't necessarily mean they like each other and aren't plotting for advantages (although I would say that murder is highly uncommon in the Heavenly social scene).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, politics. If corrupt politics doesn't cause simmering resentment, hatred, and backstabbing, then what's going on? Folks in Yu-Shan probably have lots of reasons to resent each other that aren't related to Factions or the Usurpation. Or at least they should probably be presented that way.<br /> <br /> But I also think there should be more than one opinion about the Usurpation itself among Celestial gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T16:54:29-07:00","id":508551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507944#post507944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. It seems like there's a case to be made. Heaven interferes with how Earth is run all the time. There are tons of gods whose entire job is &quot;decide how things are gonna be down there and then make it happen.&quot; That's an enormous part of what of the Bureau of Destiny does; sure, the Loom does the heavy lifting, but they do a lot of the work themselves. And once they decide on a course of action, they don't really give a damn about what people outside Yu-Shan think except to the extent that they need to do so for practical reasons.<br /> <br /> The difference between &quot;this Kingdom is fated to fall; thus it has been written. (By us.) Go and ensure this fate comes to pass, Sidereals&quot; and &quot;the Old Realm is fated to fall; thus it has been written. (By us.) Go forth and ensure this fate comes to pass, Sidereals!&quot; seems to be one of degree, rather than kind.<br /> <br /> This doesn't necessarily mean it was a <i>good idea</i>. It just might not (emphasis on might) have actually been in illegal <i>in Yu-Shan</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so you subscribe tot the theory that the law in Yu Shan is absolutely fucking batshit. Okay, carry on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:13:12-07:00","id":508565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508023#post508023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. How many Realm soldiers, armed with a pretty good spear and pretty decent armor, you know, for mortals, are willing to be the first one through the door when the time comes to throw an army at a Solar or Lunar warlord? The Realm seems to have no trouble recruiting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those people are either motivated by religious belief or conscripts who don't get a choice, likely. Neither really applies in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T01:42:08-07:00","id":508821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508194#post508194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread does make me want to write silly, exaggerated taglines for each type of Exalted, starting with Sidereals:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Congratulations! You have been selected to receive Cosmic Power. Your job sucks and nobody will thank you for it. If you fuck up, reality will have a hernia. Even if you have personal time (HAHAHA) say goodbye to a normal social life. Be in the office 5 am sharp tommorow.</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot &quot;Look on the bright side, at least you get paid three boatloads of money! You can't use it anywhere that matters without incurring massive criminal offenses, though, you just <i>have </i>the money&quot; :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T02:09:03-07:00","id":508840,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that your entire family will forget you ever existed, and you can never again build any kind of serious relationship with any humans who aren't your co-workers. Do not expect to have a happy love life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T04:32:55-07:00","id":508858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508840#post508840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that your entire family will forget you ever existed, and you can never again build any kind of serious relationship with any humans who aren't your co-workers. Do not expect to have a happy love life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, what about acquitances? Sidereals can be recognized and remembered by those that have been repeatedly exposed to them, afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T04:45:55-07:00","id":508861,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but they don't remember them very well. It requires loads of work to get them to remember you well. It's a level 4 background just to get a close relationship with a normal, regular mortal.<br /> Consider the comic at the beginning of the traits section of MoEP: Sidereals. May Blossom goes to see a man that she claims to have met many times, and kisses him, implying that they have a pretty serious relationship. But he didn't even recognise her when she came into his shop. When she tells him her name, he vaguely remembers, but still forgets that he's her lover (I assume).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T07:55:22-07:00","id":508970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508840#post508840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that your entire family will forget you ever existed, and you can never again build any kind of serious relationship with any humans who aren't your co-workers. Do not expect to have a happy love life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I covered that with giving up hope of a social life.<br /> <br /> Seriously Sidereals have shot off both feet when it comes to being isolated from the humans they supposedly protect and rule, and having any capacity to interact with them at all normally or understand what they need. At least they grow up in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T08:04:14-07:00","id":508976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508970#post508970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously Sidereals have shot off both feet when it comes to being isolated from the humans they supposedly protect and rule, and having any capacity to interact with them at all normally or understand what they need. At least they grow up in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dispute that Sidereals &quot;rule&quot; anything. Even if their made-up history props up the Immaculate Order, they don't <i>rule</i> it.<br /> <br /> Also, like...Sidereals aren't sociopaths. Sidereals can interact with people. That people don't remember them does not mean that Sidereals are all socially stunted or working on abstract levels rather than being able to concretely know what people need.<br /> <br /> And not all of them grow up in Creation either :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508194#post508194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread does make me want to write silly, exaggerated taglines for each type of Exalted, starting with Sidereals:<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Congratulations! You have been selected to receive Cosmic Power. Your job sucks and nobody will thank you for it. If you fuck up, reality will have a hernia. Even if you have personal time (HAHAHA) say goodbye to a normal social life. Be in the office 5 am sharp tommorow.</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>These are the kinds of awful memes that stick and really should not be perpetuated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T09:05:45-07:00","id":509035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't use it anywhere that matters</div> </div> </div> </div> Do your games depict some kind of curiously impoverished and drab Heaven?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T11:48:50-07:00","id":509166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=509035#post509035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do your games depict some kind of curiously impoverished and drab Heaven?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they just mostly depict Heaven as not the place where things actually happen. Sidereals or not, a minimum of 80% of every game I've been in happens in Creation, with Creation people, and Creation stuff, and commerce is done almost unanimously between Creation parties with Creation merchandise. Heaven is more kind of the place the Sidereal heads off for a few hours every now and then. It's the MI6 building for James Bond - a place visited at the beginning of the movie for the briefing and the place where the jobs come from, but I've never been in a game where it was a legitimately utilized setting.<br /> <br /> I don't think it helps that for a hell of a lot of people, the idea that Heaven might not, in fact, be <i>completely </i>filled with &quot;useless assholes&quot; doesn't even come to mind. I've legitimately had to spend nearly an hour arguing for it, once, and even then the table agreed that yeah, it would be cooler, so let's do it, &quot;even if it's noncanon&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I kinda hope Heaven gets a better depiction in 3E books, in case it wasn't noticeable :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 05-09-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T12:17:54-07:00","id":509176,"title":"","content":"The whole idea of breaking the mask to hide proof of your crimes despite everyone knowing you did it irks me. It reminds me of why court drama TV shows bother me so much. Judge and jury aren't stupid nor will the system allow an obviously guilty person go free due to a technicality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T12:22:55-07:00","id":509179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=509176#post509176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole idea of breaking the mask to hide proof of your crimes despite everyone knowing you did it irks me. It reminds me of why court drama TV shows bother me so much. Judge and jury aren't stupid nor will the system allow an obviously guilty person go free due to a technicality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of proof isn't much of a technicality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:19:42-07:00","id":509211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=509176#post509176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nor will the system allow an obviously guilty person go free due to a technicality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so very incorrect* there are not words for it.<br /> <br /> *in most Western countries at least, or judicial systems which are not effectively kangaroo courts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:09:54-07:00","id":509287,"title":"","content":"Does one have any examples of a criminal getting off on a &quot;technicality&quot; that aren't fictional, were things in which the judiciary was actually motivated, and weren't retried afterwards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:32:10-07:00","id":509293,"title":"","content":"Yes. Look up George Zimmerman. The jury did not want to acquit him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:41:03-07:00","id":509300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The jury did not want to acquit him.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then... why did they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:47:55-07:00","id":509303,"title":"","content":"Technicality. They were required because he technically didn't break a law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2015, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T18:35:30-07:00","id":509368,"title":"","content":"That's not really a technicality; that's just the law very intentionally not forbidding what Zimmerman did (ie, start a fight with an unarmed teen while armed himself, then escalate to using his gun when he started to lose).<br /> <br /> &quot;Getting off on a technicality&quot; is when a guilty man is released because the police used improper means to get their hands on evidence or something like that. And yes, it does happen. That's why the rules allow it, because not letting police convict people they built cases against improperly is one of the only effective ways to force them to follow the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T02:24:39-07:00","id":509745,"title":"","content":"I don't think proper due process is really a technicality. Seems more foundational and intrinsic. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were required because he technically didn't break a law.</div> </div> </div> </div> More that there was insufficient evidence that he had broken a law, from what I can gather. There was some, but not enough to fully overcome the possibility that he had acted in (an unfortunately sanctioned form of) self-defence. That being said, acquitting somebody if there is concluded to be insufficient proof that they broke the law seems to be the entire point of juries. Really, if this was a case in which the jury consisted of persons who would not have wanted somebody to get off, but had to acquit on the basis of the evidence and the legal arguments, that's an instance of the trial-by-jury system working; conviction based on the evidence and the principle that you need to prove wrongdoing rather than innocence rather than personal feelings (even if they're fairly valid feelings) is not a technicality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T06:28:04-07:00","id":509822,"title":"","content":"But how is it different from the Sidereals getting away with what is widely considered criminal, because of insufficient evidence? Or because &quot;technically&quot; Exalted all have the Mandate of Heaven and gods aren't supposed to intervene in their internal power struggles? That was the point of bringing up the example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-10-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:03:23-07:00","id":510250,"title":"","content":"Because even if certain evidence cannot be used in court (as in there being no physical record of it) you can still be convicted if eye witnesses and circumstantial evidence supports it. The Zimmerman case is not an accurate analogy. This is the equivalent of someone plotting to murder all the world leaders, making thinly veiled references to it to those that would be the jury and judges later, assisting the military in killing said leaders, breaking into a secure location to completely screw over the succession of government to force its collapse, then after all that getting away with it simply because they destroyed all the surveillance footage.<br /> <br /> If all it took to get away with murder was a lack of physical evidence than how do you think we convicted people before DNA evidence and photography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:06:26-07:00","id":510252,"title":"","content":"Arcane fate also ruined the eyewitness testimony, I think, based on what others have explained in this thread. If it's true that even the Sidereals can't remember what they did or who was involved, how could witnesses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-10-2015, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T19:05:51-07:00","id":510309,"title":"","content":"Alright quick clarification on the debate of Sidereal crime and trial issues, please. Now I think we're all basically in agreement that the Sidereals are guilty of some crime that they were never canonically punished for* even though it is generally known they were heavily involved if not responsible. What I'm questioning is which part are we arguing they're getting away with that they shouldn't be? Is it the Usurpation, the shattering of Mask, the assault and robbery of Lytek, or some combination?<br /> <br /> <br /> *ie It is possible the Sids did get punished, but nothing was ever said about it since at least in 2nd there is a grand total if 1 person left from the crime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T19:17:34-07:00","id":510310,"title":"","content":"Chejop Kejak is seriously the only surviving 1st Age Bronze? That's not at all what I thought/expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T19:48:13-07:00","id":510332,"title":"","content":"There are other First Age Sidereals, but the oldest of these are about a hundred years younger than Chejop Kejak. They are part of his inner circle and were all students of Kejak at one point or another.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals got away with the Usurpation, the Breaking of the Mask, and locking all the Solar Exaltations away due to lack of evidence. However, there was obviously some supernatural cover up shenanigans going on, so I bet they got some sort of punishment for that. Kejak probably got charged with Contempt of Court, Obstructing Justice, etc. The punishment was probably a slap on the wrist compared to what the Sidereals actually got away with, but better than nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-10-2015, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T19:48:14-07:00","id":510333,"title":"","content":"I think so. I mean my information is strictly 2E, so if there are others in 1E I would have missed them entirely. But checking the book* on it Ayesha Ura was born during the Usurpation. It looks like Lupo exalted in a similar time frame to Ayesha Ura. Nazri the Independent apparently exalted at the end of the Usurpation. I have no clue how old the Green Lady is, so she might be, but I couldn't find a time frame for her.<br /> <br /> *Scroll of Exalts chapter 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:06:13-07:00","id":510346,"title":"","content":"Lupo exalted before the Usurpation. It's part of why his philosophy regarding the Solars is quite different from that of Ayesha Ura: he actually remembers them, and while he thinks Creation needs them, he knows that there were serious problems with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:18:08-07:00","id":510376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=510346#post510346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lupo exalted before the Usurpation. It's part of why his philosophy regarding the Solars is quite different from that of Ayesha Ura: he actually remembers them, and while he thinks Creation needs them, he knows that there were serious problems with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright like I said I'm just going with the stuff said in &quot;Scroll of Exalts&quot; and that says Lupo's predecessor died trying to stop the Usurpation and he was brought up by the remnants of the gold faction who &quot;raised him to remain loyal to a cause that seemed lost.*&quot; So that's where I got that idea.<br /> <br /> *pg 70 if anyone wants to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:20:06-07:00","id":510378,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I was going by 1st ed Cult of the Illuminated.<br /> I guess that 2nd ed is more canonical though(for about the next 2 months, anyway).<br /> <br /> Scroll of Exalts was weird about quite a few Exalts' backgrounds. Quite a few of them got made younger. IIRC, Swims-in-Shadows got turned into a starting character whereas before he was an elder with thousands of sharkmen descendants.<br /> I'm not sure if this was deliberate, or the writers just didn't read the old material properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:34:15-07:00","id":510395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=510378#post510378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I was going by 1st ed Cult of the Illuminated.<br /> I guess that 2nd ed is more canonical though(for about the next 2 months, anyway).<br /> <br /> Scroll of Exalts was weird about quite a few Exalts' backgrounds. Quite a few of them got made younger. IIRC, Swims-in-Shadows got turned into a starting character whereas before he was an elder with thousands of sharkmen descendants.<br /> I'm not sure if this was deliberate, or the writers just didn't read the old material properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's why I said my knowledge is strictly 2E. I figured with my luck 1E has like a dozen Sidereals listed who have their bloody notes from when they made the case that the Solars were going nuts.<br /> Funnily if we bring 3E into this I think somewhere it was mentioned that Rakan Thulio is a survivor of the Primordial War. I could be wrong on that I can't remember where it was said,but I'm pretty sure he's at least around Kejack's age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:37:02-07:00","id":510408,"title":"","content":"Rakan Thulio was Exalted in the early Primordial War, or even before it. I expect that he's the oldest living human. Saturn tried to kill him personally with her Sign and he <b><i>parried</i></b> it with his &quot;blasphemous&quot; powers.<br /> <br /> So he's past his expiration date and using methods nobody else is likely to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-12-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T20:44:51-07:00","id":510416,"title":"","content":"In 2nd ed, Chejop was the oldest human, because he exalted just after the Primordial War. So if Rakan exalted during it, chances are he's older than Chejop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:51:30-07:00","id":510548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508551#post508551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so you subscribe tot the theory that the law in Yu Shan is absolutely fucking batshit. Okay, carry on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's necessarily &quot;batshit&quot; for Heavenly law to mostly only cover Heaven, not Creation. Writing and enforcing the law in Creation was the Deliberative's job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T13:28:31-07:00","id":511071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508551#post508551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so you subscribe tot the theory that the law in Yu Shan is absolutely fucking batshit. Okay, carry on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive the long lapse in replying; I was at the Toronto Comic Arts Festival all weekend.<br /> <br /> And... hmm, maybe? I do think the law in Yu-shan is batshit, but not in <i>this</i> specific case. Rather, in the context of this discussion, I think that it, like most bodies of law, doesn't cover edge cases.<br /> <br /> Let me toss out some examples. Nazri convenes the Convention of Fire for their once-a-month staff meeting. The third item on the agenda is that there's a guy in the Lap who is alive when he isn't supposed to be; his thread in the Loom ran its course and was duly snipped, but he's still walking around and breathing and suchly. The Pattern Spiders are worried that random orphan destinies are going to start attaching themselves to him, and would like it &quot;taken care of.&quot; Dude is just a mortal, so this is the equivalent of paperwork for the Sidereals; one of them will simply knife him the next time they're in Gem and the body will never be found.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals have committed a series of rather serious crimes here, up to and including murder, but I don't think Heaven is going to hold them all that responsible for it, because they're doing the job they were given. It would be illegal for them to just randomly kill people without orders, in the same way Her Majesty's Government would be okay with James Bond blowing away a British industrialist they'd specifically tasked him to assassinate because he was going to hold the world hostage with his space lasers but would be less cool if he killed the same guy because he just didn't like his hair.<br /> <br /> Let's scale that up. Would you say the Sidereals are permitted under their ambit to do things like rig the outcome of battles? That probably involves ensuring hundreds of people die. Would you say they're permitted to actually arrange the fall of entire kingdoms and noble houses if all the paperwork is in order and word comes down from on high in the Bureau of Destiny that the time has come?<br /> <br /> Because, if so, then the Usurpation may very well have been entirely legal. Remember, the higher echelons of the Bureau of Destiny have a fair number of Sidereals in actual planning, as opposed to simply execution, roles. The law codes of Yu-Shan probably were not ever written to consider the possibility the Sidereals would decide that the time had come for the Old Realm to perish in fiery destruction, so when they did that, there wasn't a legal venue of recourse available, because the Sidereals can just piously say &quot;we had a planning session, it generated a number of possible destinies, we picked the best one. We do that all the time. That is our job. You got a problem, talk to our bosses.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not saying this is canon. I am saying that this seems like a reasonable explanation to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:15:42-07:00","id":511203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508023#post508023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically, you posit that the faction that is all about heavenly politics... shouldn't have any heavenly politics in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, and I think that\u2019s a pretty uncharitable read of what I posted. Hell:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now that's not to suggest that I feel the Sidereals are invincible. Far from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point, more than anything, is that Sidereals have a nuclear option when it comes to heavenly politics. Maybe they can only use it once or twice before their political capital is spent, but it\u2019s there, and only the most suicidal of gods is going to try do something like get a Sidereal executed because they <i>will</i> close ranks and they <i>will</i> make an example of the offending party, because you don\u2019t survive in a cutthroat environment like Yu-Shan by employing half-measures. Letting a Sidereal get executed in any but the most egregious circumstances (ie Raken Thulio) sets a bad precedent, after all.<br /> <br /> I think the disconnect here is I\u2019m thinking macro scale political action against the Sidereals as a whole (ie execution, mass censure, that sort of thing) and you\u2019re thinking micro scale. Kejak isn\u2019t going to cash in any markers because a newbie Sidereal spilled wine on a minor god\u2019s floor and they\u2019re now in a tiff. That\u2019s for the newbie to sort out, and maybe learn a valuable lesion (and, if they seem really over their head, become indebted to one of their elders). If Ahlat or Ryzala gets it into their little pea brains to try and start having Sidereals executed, though\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508821#post508821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You forgot &quot;Look on the bright side, at least you get paid three boatloads of money! You can't use it anywhere that matters without incurring massive criminal offenses, though, you just <i>have </i>the money&quot; :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that you can make ambrosia and quintessence into basically <i>anything</i> in Yu-Shan, though, saying that you can't spend it on the streets of Nexus isn't that big of a limitation.<br /> <br /> And it's not even so much that you can't use it. It's more that you just can't wreck economies for funsies.<br /> <br /> Hell, since you can make ambrosia aspected to the Maidens into starmetal, I always assumed that there were Completely Voluntary Compulsory Mandatory Collection of Ambrosia for the Good of the Bureau as a Whole You Greedy Fucks a few times a year at the Bureau.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=508840#post508840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that your entire family will forget you ever existed, and you can never again build any kind of serious relationship with any humans who aren't your co-workers. Do not expect to have a happy love life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img407/6939/arcanefate.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm fine with keeping on posting Big Boss goodness every time this topic comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:04:06-07:00","id":511275,"title":"","content":"That's a valid and well-argued counterpoint, and I accept it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T22:09:27-07:00","id":511672,"title":"","content":"For that matter, how does the Bureau of Destiny's gods planning Creation's future interact with the Creation-Ruling Mandate, which is all about gods not messing with Creation &amp; leaving that to the Exalted? Wouldn't it make more sense if the Sidereals, not the gods, were the heads of the Bureau of Destiny?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T00:57:53-07:00","id":511787,"title":"","content":"IIRC, at least nominally, the things the Bureaus are doing, they're doing at the behest of the Exalted who rule Creation. Since the throne's currently empty, that complicates things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T01:15:09-07:00","id":511794,"title":"","content":"To be honest, the empty throne probably makes it simpler.<br /> The Sidereals can just claim that whatever they want is what the Exalted want. They are Exalted, and no other Exalted are coming and contradicting them.<br /> Now, if a bunch of Solars turned up and said that the Sidereals lacked authority to do this, it might be a problem.<br /> <br /> Also, of course, in the 1st age the Sidereals were, in terms of the Bureau, doing exactly what they're doing now. They just presumably had to make sure that what they did went along with what the Deliberative wanted. Now they can work without interference. So it's not like they've stopped doing what they were told to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:19:12-07:00","id":511883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=511672#post511672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, how does the Bureau of Destiny's gods planning Creation's future interact with the Creation-Ruling Mandate, which is all about gods not messing with Creation &amp; leaving that to the Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Planning Destiny&quot; is supposed to mean figuring out the logical consequences of actions and motivations that people are taking, bound within the Sidereal conjunctions of the constellations, and instructing the pattern spiders to weave in those processes and outcomes.<br /> <br /> A god who plans the day and the moment when some mortal dies isn't really interfering in anything, because somebody writing out the day and cause of your death is just how things die, and that person is mortal.<br /> <br /> It becomes interference when it becomes about not sticking to operational procedures and instead inserting personal agendas.<br /> <br /> Which gods have probably always done to some extent, possibly even by necessity to keep things actually running smoothly, because it's not actually possible to have a complex system consisting of large numbers of individuals follow the rules all of the time, both in the sense of &quot;people won't be so rigid&quot; and &quot;there are too many unpredictable variables that people will need to break rules to fix&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Although the need for improvisation and cheating when things aren't going by the book is probably largely supervised by Sidereal Exalted, at least for the important things)<br /> <br /> People talk up &quot;Creation-Ruling Mandate&quot; a lot, and many books don't help, but Games of Divinity was clear that even before the Usurpation there were various levels of gods not following the rules.<br /> <br /> But yeah, non-interference is supposed to mean things like Ahlat not favouring the side that makes the biggest cattle sacrifice and not taking the souls of fallen warriors to adorn his cloak, not that he never contributes to the overall essence of how certain kinds of battles and wars play out. At least that's how I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:42:24-07:00","id":511893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=511794#post511794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, the empty throne probably makes it simpler.<br /> The Sidereals can just claim that whatever they want is what the Exalted want. They are Exalted, and no other Exalted are coming and contradicting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. The meta plot is that Sidereals are overworked Agents of F.A.T.E., not <i>de facto</i> rulers of Creation.<br /> <br /> After the Usurpation, the gods (and elementals) proclaimed that the Mandate of Heaven was granted exclusively to the Solar Host; not to the Sidereals or Terrestrials --- and the Incarnae didn't contradict <i>them</i> on this point. <br /> <br /> That is ostensibly why a lot of First Age infrastructure collapsed; when elementals bound to onerous tasks tested their bonds and <i>found </i>that their service had indeed ended with the Solars.<br /> <br /> Likewise, in Yu Shan, the Fivescore Fellowship didn't just become the new the Deliberative after overthrowing the Solars; and the Bureaus were able to somewhat reduce their authority with nary an objection from the Maidens. Unable to actually punish the Sidereals (for <i>reasons</i>) the gods settled for acting snooty and obstructionist.<br /> <br /> And such like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:59:07-07:00","id":511903,"title":"","content":"I like to think that at least part (if a big part) of why gods of various sorts were extremely uncooperative with the Shogunate was because one of the major consequences of the need to appropriate massive amounts of labour in an effort to restore and expand the infrastructure, as well as the general sense among the Dragon Blooded that a firm hand of control was needed, was the widespread disruption of festivals and temples and other practices that had entertained and enriched the gods, and some of them were simply angry on that count and others felt a need to start acting more directly to gather dedicated cults to themselves, and it created all kinds of tensions and lack of cooperation.<br /> <br /> The idea that it's all just a matter of semantic and ultra-legalistic argument is dissatisfying to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:39:08-07:00","id":511924,"title":"","content":"Well, yes, there was <i>definitely </i>petty-vindictive self-interest behind the legal fiction that the Mandate only applied to the Solar Host.<br /> <br /> That's why, now that they've <i>gotten used </i>to the Immaculate Calendar and such, the Celestial Gods <i>aren't </i>falling over themselves haling the returned Solars as holders of the Mandate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:29:29-07:00","id":511984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=510332#post510332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are other First Age Sidereals, but the oldest of these are about a hundred years younger than Chejop Kejak. They are part of his inner circle and were all students of Kejak at one point or another.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The only Bronze Faction IC members we have the names of are Holok and Anys Syn; the Chair holder of the Northern Convention just recently died, and there's a big political scramble to replace him. <br /> <br /> I believe that Leviathan was originally intended to be the oldest Exalt, as 1E calls him &quot;ancient even in the First Age&quot;, but the 2E writers admitted to missing that line and rewrote him as considerably younger...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:47:26-07:00","id":511988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=509166#post509166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they just mostly depict Heaven as not the place where things actually happen. Sidereals or not, a minimum of 80% of every game I've been in happens in Creation, with Creation people, and Creation stuff, and commerce is done almost unanimously between Creation parties with Creation merchandise. Heaven is more kind of the place the Sidereal heads off for a few hours every now and then. It's the MI6 building for James Bond - a place visited at the beginning of the movie for the briefing and the place where the jobs come from, but I've never been in a game where it was a legitimately utilized setting.<br /> <br /> I don't think it helps that for a hell of a lot of people, the idea that Heaven might not, in fact, be <i>completely </i>filled with &quot;useless assholes&quot; doesn't even come to mind. I've legitimately had to spend nearly an hour arguing for it, once, and even then the table agreed that yeah, it would be cooler, so let's do it, &quot;even if it's noncanon&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I kinda hope Heaven gets a better depiction in 3E books, in case it wasn't noticeable :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a perfectly good and usable depiction now, in the Yu-Shan compass (although there's always room for improvement). There's PLENTY to do and be involved in, *in games actually set there*. Just because one table's games mostly take place in Creation doesn't make all the canonical coolness there go away! <br /> <br /> It's like reducing ALL of London, with all its history and places to go and things to see and do, to &quot;that one MI6 building&quot;, because that's all you ever see in the Bond movies before he goes oversees. <br /> <br /> Canonically, Sidereals do get time off, and their salaries are quite useful in enjoying themselves in the many, many pastimes that Heaven offers. Many Viziers are regulars at various heavenly casinos, brothels, workshops, theaters, dojos, restaurants, etc, all of which have the added draw of being places where everyone actually knows their name!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:56:30-07:00","id":511992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=506978#post506978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can murder thousands or millions of people with no consequences whatsoever. Which was the whole point of Arcane Fate after all. Never again being accountable for any actions, no matter how extreme, unless they anger the Bureau of Destiny higher ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall a trio of Sidereals who got killed by Oversight because of pulling shenanigans like that. I don't think that wanton genocide can be considered &quot;Aceeptable losses&quot; especially since Heaven needs mortals to pay for their opulent lifestyles with prayer, so to speak. <br /> <br /> I've always played with Sidereals being the unsung heroes to mortals and any Exalted NPCs who didn't pay attention, but never tried to pull a &quot;And then the stranger leaves, and you forget about him, WHOOOO~&quot; on any players. Sidereals have enough weird esoteric powers to pull off disappearing without needing to resort to Arcane Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:06:16-07:00","id":511994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=507111#post507111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Example: in 2E, the head of the Convention of Air was executed for criminal activity. It is implied that they weren't actually guilty, although they were probably guilty of something, but a powerful, veteran Sidereal, in good standing with the Bronze Faction, with lots of hard-to-replace experience, was hauled in front of a censor and <i>killed</i>, and Kejak couldn't do shit about it.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of correction: The Air Chair died of old age. The one who was executed was one of the Sids who sorcerously destroyed an entire city as punishment for allying with the Bull of the North. His partner was killed by the Bull, and both of them were the Chair's chosen successors, meaning that that position is now up for grabs. <br /> <br /> I never thought Heaven executed that guy because &quot;mass killing was wrong&quot; so much as that unscheduled snuffing out that many lives is bound to have a bad effect on the Loom (if not creating a massive new Shadowland), necessitating LOTS of extra work on the part of the B. of Destiny...so it's maybe not a surprise that they didn't lift a finger to save him (&quot;Sorry, we'd love to help you out, but can't because of all this overtime due to <i>some jackass</i> who couldn't find a subtler way to deal with his problems!&quot;). It also deprives the Gods of a sizable amount of worship...<br /> <br /> Really, it was a very stupid thing for those Sids to do, which is more implausible than Heaven's reaction to it.<br /> <br /> Seeing that his execution also freed up the Chair for possible Gold possession, I'm also inclined to give it the benefit of the doubt that the Gold Faction may have used some influence to ensure a worse sentence than could have been expected. This would be in keeping with the escalation of their factional rivalry as a Bronze agent had recently killed a Gold Star, so many of them could also see this as payback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:25:39-07:00","id":512007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=511203#post511203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point, more than anything, is that Sidereals have a nuclear option when it comes to heavenly politics. Maybe they can only use it once or twice before their political capital is spent, but it\u2019s there, and only the most suicidal of gods is going to try do something like get a Sidereal executed because they <i>will</i> close ranks and they <i>will</i> make an example of the offending party, because you don\u2019t survive in a cutthroat environment like Yu-Shan by employing half-measures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why doesn't this go the other way around, though? Why aren't the Sidereals worried about using political manipulation to get a god executed because the gods friends and allies will close ranks and make an example of the offending party, because &quot;you don't survive in a cutthroat environment like Yu-shan by employing half-measures.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the disconnect here is I\u2019m thinking macro scale political action against the Sidereals as a whole (ie execution, mass censure, that sort of thing) and you\u2019re thinking micro scale. Kejak isn\u2019t going to cash in any markers because a newbie Sidereal spilled wine on a minor god\u2019s floor and they\u2019re now in a tiff. That\u2019s for the newbie to sort out, and maybe learn a valuable lesion (and, if they seem really over their head, become indebted to one of their elders). If Ahlat or Ryzala gets it into their little pea brains to try and start having Sidereals executed, though\u2026 </div> </div> </div>That might be it, yes. It's just... part of the point of a cutthroat political environment, in my mind, is that the mechanisms of the state can be turned against you even unto the point of death. Having your political rivals killed is a logical endgame and removing the danger of &quot;if you fuck up badly enough you gonna die&quot; removes a lot of the tension and drama.<br /> <br /> It's like... if there's a Sidereal who is a political and personal enemy of Ahlat, and who in fact has dedicated himself to taking Ahlat down or at least forcing him to do his fuckin' job properly, why the hell wouldn't Ahlat respond in kind by trying to take that Sidereal down, employing methods up to and including trying to get them killed, <i>because that's what the Sidereal is doing to Ahlat</i>, and that's how the game is played?<br /> <br /> I dislike the idea that the Sidereals are &quot;exempt&quot; from the normal consequences of politics, and that they're so damn powerful the gods just have to accept that the political weapons they would deploy against a god doing the precise same things a Sidereal does to them somehow don't apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that you can make ambrosia and quintessence into basically <i>anything</i> in Yu-Shan, though, saying that you can't spend it on the streets of Nexus isn't that big of a limitation.<br /> <br /> And it's not even so much that you can't use it. It's more that you just can't wreck economies for funsies. </div> </div> </div>This. You can live at Resources 3 in Creation without fear of audit, and Resources 3 is pretty damn comfortable.<br /> <br /> And hell, that limitation only applies to your personal lifestyle. The rules don't speak to this one way or the other, but I've always assumed if you're on the clock, the normal rules don't apply <i>and</i> you can expense everything. &quot;Ayesha, this Resplendency I'm using really demands that I hire a company of mercs as my personal guards; it isn't believable otherwise, and frankly if I'm going to be spending two months crawling around the jungle that close to Rathess, I'd feel better with the meatshield.&quot; &quot;Yeah, okay, approved. Keep your receipts, tho.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm fine with keeping on posting Big Boss goodness every time this topic comes up. </div> </div> </div>I think you intended that as a threat, Coik, but I interpreted it as a <i>promise</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, how does the Bureau of Destiny's gods planning Creation's future interact with the Creation-Ruling Mandate, which is all about gods not messing with Creation &amp; leaving that to the Exalted? Wouldn't it make more sense if the Sidereals, not the gods, were the heads of the Bureau of Destiny?</div> </div> </div> </div>The heads of the Bureau of Destiny are the Maidens, who are Incarnae. The normal rules do not apply to the Incarnae and those they specifically designate, because the Creation-Ruling Mandate was bestowed with their imprimatur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that it's all just a matter of semantic and ultra-legalistic argument is dissatisfying to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's always been the case that the semantics and legal arguments are just a veneer, right?<br /> <br /> The gods didn't have a long history of having to do anything the Dragon-Blooded said, and as the First Age wore on the Dragon-Blooded were reduced more and more to &quot;ornaments of the Solars.&quot; The Terrestrial gods and elementals saw the Dragon-Blooded a lot, sure, but the Celestial gods rarely interacted with them and certainly not as equals. So when the chance came for the gods to start calling their own shots, well, why not take it? They don't have to obey the Dragon-Blooded in the same way they had to obey the Solars... and the Solars might have been capable of storming Heaven, but the Dragon-Blooded Host doesn't seem to be... the Sidereals would like them to cooperate with the Dragon-Blooded, but there are plenty of gods of who don't much care for the Sidereals anyway and the Sidereals requests to cooperate with the Terrestrials is more &quot;personal favor&quot; than it is &quot;legally binding, Celestial Lion's gonna come for you if you refuse.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, the part I don't care for is how... abrupt it seems. Heaven's slide into corruption would have been slow, for inertia reasons if nothing else, even after such an upheaval as the Usurpation was. So it seems likely that at the dawn of the Shogunate, said Shogunate would have been able to get quite a lot of help out of Heaven.<br /> <br /> And then, as time went on... less help. And the Sidereals step in to the extent they can, but getting the gods to cooperate takes a lot of political capital, especially as the Immaculate Philosophy, which gods of all stripes are going to see as both inaccurate and offensive, takes hold.<br /> <br /> So then after awhile you get no help at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:13:30-07:00","id":512039,"title":"","content":"Very well put, Mercushio.<br /> <br /> That's the thing I think with gods' positions about the Usurpation, the Immaculate Order, and the Sidereals: the ones who preferred the First Age order are going to resent the current order. The ones who prefer the current order... are more likely to be corrupt, and resent the Sidereals who try to interfere with their corruption. There will be gods who like the Immaculate Order because they can get cushy stuff out of it, but mostly the Immaculate Order doesn't give them cushy stuff, whereas corruption does. There will be gods who prefer to just do their jobs because they consider them important, and aren't necessarily strongly opinionated about who's specifically running Creation. There will be gods who owe favors to or are owed favors by this or that Sidereal, or have specific goals in common with them. There will be gods who are cooperative or favorable towards Sidereals as an institution or particular Sidereals personally. But I can't imagine a Yu-Shan in which there aren't a great number of resentful and uncooperative gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T15:04:11-07:00","id":512358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=511994#post511994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Point of correction: The Air Chair died of old age. The one who was executed was one of the Sids who sorcerously destroyed an entire city as punishment for allying with the Bull of the North. His partner was killed by the Bull, and both of them were the Chair's chosen successors, meaning that that position is now up for grabs.<br /> <br /> I never thought Heaven executed that guy because &quot;mass killing was wrong&quot; so much as that unscheduled snuffing out that many lives is bound to have a bad effect on the Loom (if not creating a massive new Shadowland), necessitating LOTS of extra work on the part of the B. of Destiny...so it's maybe not a surprise that they didn't lift a finger to save him (&quot;Sorry, we'd love to help you out, but can't because of all this overtime due to <i>some jackass</i> who couldn't find a subtler way to deal with his problems!&quot;). It also deprives the Gods of a sizable amount of worship...<br /> <br /> Really, it was a very stupid thing for those Sids to do, which is more implausible than Heaven's reaction to it.<br /> <br /> Seeing that his execution also freed up the Chair for possible Gold possession, I'm also inclined to give it the benefit of the doubt that the Gold Faction may have used some influence to ensure a worse sentence than could have been expected. This would be in keeping with the escalation of their factional rivalry as a Bronze agent had recently killed a Gold Star, so many of them could also see this as payback.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it sticking in this edition because sidereals are literally allowed to do anything they want in creation so long as they aren't purposely fucking over their job. They are exalts and as exalts they not gods have control over how creation is run. However, if he was assassinated by the city god who was mad about it. That would be more in line with how everything works in Yu-shan. however, they can't be executed over it.<br /> <br /> That just smacks of the writer like most people not really knowing how Sidereals operate in Yu-shan. Which is as Operatives who still dictate how creation is run. Yes, they have bosses. Yes those bosses demand things. However, at the end of the day, so long as he's not running counter to fate anomolies he's allowed to do whatever he wants. It's why the Bronze faction was able to dictate the course of creation for over 700 years with the scarlet empress. Yes, she ruled it. The sidereals; however, let her keep her job and made sure her enemies were taken care of.<br /> <br /> The one thing I really don't like about talking about sidereals here is the misconception that Sidereals are JUST Agents. Kejak didn't make the Scarlet Empress the leader of the center of creation because some mandate. He did it because he knew it was what needed to be done to save the world. He works to make sure creation is safe in his own way. And while the Bureau makes sure that things happen as the course sees fit sidereals can easily change it so long as it doesn't effect the loom of fate, which they can actively alter to suit their own needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T15:38:36-07:00","id":512369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512358#post512358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, at the end of the day, so long as he's not running counter to fate anomolies he's allowed to do whatever he wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly untrue. Heaven regulates the lives of its Operatives very closely. The Sidereals aren't allowed to use their pay packets to buy fancy items in Creation! We had a discussion about it in this very thread. They cannot just &quot;do whatever they want,&quot; at least, not without real risk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's why the Bronze faction was able to dictate the course of creation for over 700 years with the scarlet empress. </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Faction did no such thing. They definitely are a force to be reckoned with but they do not &quot;dictate&quot; the course of Creation. They <i>wish</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, she ruled it. The sidereals; however, let her keep her job and made sure her enemies were taken care of. </div> </div> </div>Bull. Shit.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals did not &quot;let&quot; Scarlet keep her job. She got the job on her own merits, and while her relationship with the Bronze Faction has been immensely productive for both parties, she does an excellent job of dealing with her enemies without their help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The one thing I really don't like about talking about sidereals here is the misconception that Sidereals are JUST Agents. </div> </div> </div>Most Sidereal PC's are just going to be agents. You don't get to be one of the people calling the shots until you get promoted up the ranks, which takes centuries and, like any bureaucracy, probably involves waiting patiently for people to die. That is why we talk about them in those terms, because far more people are playing Crimson Banner Executioner than they are playing Holok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kejak didn't make the Scarlet Empress the leader of the center of creation because some mandate. </div> </div> </div>He didn't make her the leader of the center of creation <i>at all.</i> She did that herself. The Empress forced Kejak to come to her and kneel in supplication. THAT is how their relationship began, and her position vis a vis Kejak and his merry band of social engineers did not get weaker over the course of seven centuries of her becoming the most successful and personally powerful monarch in the history of Creation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T18:11:09-07:00","id":512435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512369#post512369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is explicitly untrue. Heaven regulates the lives of its Operatives very closely. The Sidereals aren't allowed to use their pay packets to buy fancy items in Creation! We had a discussion about it in this very thread. They cannot just &quot;do whatever they want,&quot; at least, not without real risk.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ambrosia is a heavenly item and using it to flood the local market with enough Jade to buy out a region is one thing however, they are allowed to muck around creation as they want. They are not gods they don't have godly limitations. They can make gods angry as a result but nothing they do will actively be illegal. There are ways for gods to get back at them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bronze Faction did no such thing. They definitely are a force to be reckoned with but they do not &quot;dictate&quot; the course of Creation. They <i>wish</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bull. Shit.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals did not &quot;let&quot; Scarlet keep her job. She got the job on her own merits, and while her relationship with the Bronze Faction has been immensely productive for both parties, she does an excellent job of dealing with her enemies without their help. </div> </div> </div>She survived because sidereals helped her. She got the job because she had access to the meganuke. If Kejak could have taken that knowledge for himself on how to operate it. We'd have a bunch of puppet dictators. Yes. Sidereals gave her equal quarter however, she wouldn't have even survived if they didn't deem her necessary. They kept her propped up when dozens of other threats would have killed her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most Sidereal PC's are just going to be agents. You don't get to be one of the people calling the shots until you get promoted up the ranks, which takes centuries and, like any bureaucracy, probably involves waiting patiently for people to die. That is why we talk about them in those terms, because far more people are playing Crimson Banner Executioner than they are playing Holok. </div> </div> </div>You can play both if play it right. It's not just about promoting people it's also about dealing in favors half the time. Considering there are only 100 sidereals and thousands of gods you could probably kill to get a promotion for it's not as hard as you'd imagine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He didn't make her the leader of the center of creation <i>at all.</i> She did that herself. The Empress forced Kejak to come to her and kneel in supplication. THAT is how their relationship began, and her position vis a vis Kejak and his merry band of social engineers did not get weaker over the course of seven centuries of her becoming the most successful and personally powerful monarch in the history of Creation. </div> </div> </div>That is how Kejak allowed himself to be put into the position. Again if it wasn't for the fact that she was more useful alive than dead she wouldn't have even survived her first encounter with him. He was what four thousand years old when they first met? She was young and fresh out of training. She's alive because she had a super weapon and because Kejak knew if they worked together they would be an a better position than if they worked against each other. The fact is, the reason sidereals are called invisible masters is because they've helped and had an extremely large hand in forming it. They aren't just agents and people should stop treating them as the only thing they actually do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:48:11-07:00","id":512487,"title":"","content":"Okay quick thing on her Redness' power and how that's related to anything. There was kind of the whole Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion going on at the time, and considering both of those both of those hit Creation out of nowhere (from the perspectives of those it hit) I think it is a fair assumption that the greater scheme most people had at the time was put an end to the apocalypse and try to be on the side who don't die doing it. Plus I swear by the end of 2E it seems like only factions who weren't instrumental in her rise were factions that didn't exist yet. The Empress' ascension was not Kejak and the Sids ensuring she got the job because they could control her. However, Kejak didn't appear as a kneeling supplicant at the order of Her Redness. Kejak appeared that way because the adviser job works best if you get the person to listen to you and most people who declare themselves the rulers of the world like it when you prostrate yourself before them. She did make him wait a few days before actually meeting him though, that was all her.<br /> <br /> Though Epimetheus an impression I'm getting off your end of this is that you think the Sids secretly run creation, that accurate? I mean I could be wrong and it could just be a tone thing giving the wrong impression as a result of your attempt to argue that Sids should be treated as more than goverment spooks, so I thought I would check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:54:41-07:00","id":512489,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out, Epimetheus, that &quot;more useful dead than alive&quot; to the point where you're willing to put thousands of years of pride as &quot;the man who is saving Creation from itself by upholding the Bronze Faction's goals even after we've seen the results&quot; is... a pretty strong position, regardless of whether Kejak could PERSONALLY have punched the Empress' soul out through her pores without really trying.<br /> <br /> Even in Exalted, there are times when facepunching your problems doesn't fix your problems, it just causes more problems. Kejak knows this, and that's why he helped build a freaking religion venerating the Dragon-Blooded so as to pacify vast swathes of Creation with dogma and then empowered the Dragon-blooded who dedicated themselves to that religion to have super special magic powers that even other Dragon-blooded don't have to ensure that they could keep the small gods in line really really well.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am a Celestial Exalt and I can kill you&quot; might work for some Solars, but it causes major problems. It rarely works for Sidereals, if only because Sidereals that are that crass in their methods find that their Charms are generally not sufficient to allow them to live long enough to learn those SMAs that everyone likes to point at as their high essence options.<br /> <br /> Kejak does not facepunch everyone to solve his problems, that's not how he's done things throughout his life. For a guy like Kejak, the direct application of personal violence on his part is a last resort, not a threat he throws around willy nilly. Yes, he COULD kick Ahlat in the crotch until Ahlat did whatever he wanted, probably, but that just makes a lifelong enemy out of Ahlat, everyone associated with Ahlat, and everyone else who might think that they could theoretically be next, and unless Kejak can arrange a full on coup of heaven such that he is a personal dictator, he knows very well he could not get away with that kind of direct, personal action. Not to mention that takes a lot of time out of his day and his paperwork falls behind and there are a lot of people that he would then have to dedicate a great deal of time to facepunching... ugh, such a hassle for a guy who's frankly already tired of life at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:57:58-07:00","id":512491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512487#post512487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though Epimetheus an impression I'm getting off your end of this is that you think the Sids secretly run creation, that accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not him but that's the impression I got from briefly skimming a few pages of the 1e Sidereals book, and from the 4 books that I do own. I think there's even the sentence &quot;But history has not been kind to Sidereal rule.&quot; (in 1e Sidereals)<br /> <br /> I'd welcome <i><b>gentle</b></i> clarification or corrections, though, because they come across as total imcompetent narcissists, if the Age of Sorrows is the best they can do and they actually think they're the best thing ever for Creation and have made it so much better than the 1st Age (or can totally make the world perfect if they can only turn the Solars into their brainwashed puppets). I get the impression that they all think they're literally infallable and have never made mistakes in their lives, and that humanity almost going extinct twice wasn't a mistake. Not gonna lie, it's very hard for me to like them, based on what little info I've had access to.<br /> <br /> If they are not actually almost as responsible as the Deathlords for the world going down the toilet and being moribund, and are not pleased with their hideous screwups, that makes them... less horribly unsympathetic. I actually wish the Usurpation was consistently depicted in shades of grey -- not as the single stupidest, worst thing any human being decided to do in the history of Ever, and obviously so in retrospect.<br /> <br /> Just please be gentle correcting me, I only own 4 books, OK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-12-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:32:32-07:00","id":512509,"title":"","content":"I believe, Erinyes, that the best way to view the Sidereals--and mind you, this is my perception which may not be shared by anyone--is people who are way too smart and clever for their own good, by and large.<br /> <br /> They are the classic image of the smartest guy in the room, who thinks that he should run everything just because he's smart, and that attitude breeds a certain arrogance that starts to feed itself. You start assuming &quot;I'm smarter than you, so my ideas have more merit than yours, and that means your ideas have less merit than mine, so I must be right, and since I'm right, I'm smart, and I'm smart so I'm right...&quot; and it just goes in a circle that doesn't allow for dissenting opinions.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that the Sidereals, when choosing how to save the world, consulted no one outside themselves, because they considered no one else capable of understanding the burden they bore, or capable of making the choices they made, or of comprehending the enormity of the choice itself.<br /> <br /> They truly felt that they AND ONLY THEY understood enough to make the &quot;right&quot; choice, and that even the wisest beings in creation outside the Sidereal Host could not possibly be trusted to act in the best interests of Creation.<br /> <br /> It was not until the decision was made and events were set in motion that they even involved the dragon-blooded, and they used them as catspaws and weapons, not as partners in a struggle for the fate of the world.<br /> <br /> If the Solars were tyrants, the Sidereals were the wise men whose very wisdom led them to foolish action. That they needed to act, one way or another, is clear.<br /> <br /> That they assumed the rest of the world too incompetent or too tainted to trust, also clear.<br /> <br /> That this directly led to the lessening of the world, and that they consulted no one but themselves, that they never truly considered viewpoints other than their own, and that they entirely neglected to consider threats from outside fate--the very threats the Solars themselves were so exceptionally good at holding back--is simply a series of examples of the Sidereals' flaws coming to light.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are absolutely wise, powerful, mystical masters in their way.<br /> <br /> They're just categorically incapable of trusting anyone to do anything unless they manipulate the crap out of the situation until there's no other choice first.<br /> <br /> ...And to be fair, they're not entirely unjustified in that.<br /> <br /> Still makes them kinda douchey though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T21:50:54-07:00","id":512525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512487#post512487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay quick thing on her Redness' power and how that's related to anything. There was kind of the whole Balorian Crusade and Great Contagion going on at the time, and considering both of those both of those hit Creation out of nowhere (from the perspectives of those it hit) I think it is a fair assumption that the greater scheme most people had at the time was put an end to the apocalypse and try to be on the side who don't die doing it. Plus I swear by the end of 2E it seems like only factions who weren't instrumental in her rise were factions that didn't exist yet. The Empress' ascension was not Kejak and the Sids ensuring she got the job because they could control her. However, Kejak didn't appear as a kneeling supplicant at the order of Her Redness. Kejak appeared that way because the adviser job works best if you get the person to listen to you and most people who declare themselves the rulers of the world like it when you prostrate yourself before them. She did make him wait a few days before actually meeting him though, that was all her.<br /> <br /> Though Epimetheus an impression I'm getting off your end of this is that you think the Sids secretly run creation, that accurate? I mean I could be wrong and it could just be a tone thing giving the wrong impression as a result of your attempt to argue that Sids should be treated as more than goverment spooks, so I thought I would check.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of references to it starting from sidereals first edition and along the course of the setting. They don't rule it day to day like the empress did. They did dictate it's course and continue to do so. It's not the gods who make creation what it is today it was the sidereals and dragonblooded as well as every outside factor that couldn't be accounted for.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T21:51:53-07:00","id":512526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512007#post512007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why doesn't this go the other way around, though? Why aren't the Sidereals worried about using political manipulation to get a god executed because the gods friends and allies will close ranks and make an example of the offending party, because &quot;you don't survive in a cutthroat environment like Yu-shan by employing half-measures.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand what you're asking here, I think that they are. That's why I called it the nuclear option...yes, if Ryzala or Ahlat decide to fuck with the Five-Score Fellowship, they can make them regret it, but it will involve expending a great deal of political capital and then having to weather blowbacks and reprisals, from any allies they have if not them themselves. If they have to go that route, it also means that the situation has gotten so far out of control that what amounts to a political scorched earth attack is the best option, which means they're in pretty dire straits indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That might be it, yes. It's just... part of the point of a cutthroat political environment, in my mind, is that the mechanisms of the state can be turned against you even unto the point of death. Having your political rivals killed is a logical endgame and removing the danger of &quot;if you fuck up badly enough you gonna die&quot; removes a lot of the tension and drama. </div> </div> </div>I prefer the &quot;If you fuck up badly enough you gonna die&quot; option to come more from skullduggery and ambushes in the slums, and less &quot;You rolled a 10 on the audit results table.&quot; Reminds me too much of Essence Venom. And hey, I got to page 7 of a Sidereal thread before I had an opportunity to say &quot;fuck Paradox.&quot; <br /> <br /> Fuck Paradox, by the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And hell, that limitation only applies to your personal lifestyle. The rules don't speak to this one way or the other, but I've always assumed if you're on the clock, the normal rules don't apply <i>and</i> you can expense everything. &quot;Ayesha, this Resplendency I'm using really demands that I hire a company of mercs as my personal guards; it isn't believable otherwise, and frankly if I'm going to be spending two months crawling around the jungle that close to Rathess, I'd feel better with the meatshield.&quot; &quot;Yeah, okay, approved. Keep your receipts, tho.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I imagine that's the case. I'd go so far to say that if you were hiring those mercs for Bureau work, you might even be able to pay them out of the department budget instead of your pocket. Or more likely, you pay out of pocket and then the Bureau reimburses you.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one of the questions I asked back in the first Ask the Devs thread over on rpg.net was if the information on Sidereals would give a better overview on the sort of resources they can draw upon, and I was very happy when hatewheel said yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you intended that as a threat, Coik, but I interpreted it as a <i>promise</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img911/7821/c8L26x.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to the Phantom Pain, even though the current shenanigans with Konami mean it'll probably be the last real Metal Gear game we get.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Kejak's relationship with Her Redness, my personal headcanon is that he ended each of his meetings with her by saying &quot;Good night, Scarlet. Good work. Sleep well. I'll most likely kill you in the morning.&quot;<br /> <br /> Probably just me, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T21:52:27-07:00","id":512527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512491#post512491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are not actually almost as responsible as the Deathlords for the world going down the toilet and being moribund, and are not pleased with their hideous screwups, that makes them... less horribly unsympathetic. I actually wish the Usurpation was consistently depicted in shades of grey -- not as the single stupidest, worst thing any human being decided to do in the history of Ever, and obviously so in retrospect.<br /> <br /> Just please be gentle correcting me, I only own 4 books, OK.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is more to do with we are presented as the solars as a whole being insane, wicked, and unimaginable monsters but since they are the player characters it's kept vague when it should be clearer that the usurpation happened for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T03:02:19-07:00","id":512761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512491#post512491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not him but that's the impression I got from briefly skimming a few pages of the 1e Sidereals book, and from the 4 books that I do own. I think there's even the sentence &quot;But history has not been kind to Sidereal rule.&quot; (in 1e Sidereals)<br /> <br /> I'd welcome <i><b>gentle</b></i> clarification or corrections, though, because they come across as total imcompetent narcissists, if the Age of Sorrows is the best they can do and they actually think they're the best thing ever for Creation and have made it so much better than the 1st Age (or can totally make the world perfect if they can only turn the Solars into their brainwashed puppets). I get the impression that they all think they're literally infallable and have never made mistakes in their lives, and that humanity almost going extinct twice wasn't a mistake. Not gonna lie, it's very hard for me to like them, based on what little info I've had access to.<br /> <br /> If they are not actually almost as responsible as the Deathlords for the world going down the toilet and being moribund, and are not pleased with their hideous screwups, that makes them... less horribly unsympathetic. I actually wish the Usurpation was consistently depicted in shades of grey -- not as the single stupidest, worst thing any human being decided to do in the history of Ever, and obviously so in retrospect.<br /> <br /> Just please be gentle correcting me, I only own 4 books, OK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't figure they think they're infallible, mostly because they seem to rarely <i>succeed</i>.<br /> <br /> Seriously, since the Usurpation, Sidereal plans are mostly mentioned in the gameline to say how they go wrong. Culminating in the entirety of the Fellowship getting exterminated in one go in Return of the Scarlet Empress because hey, why not. I have never quite gotten where the omniscient Sidereal ruler meme came from. Sidereals as depicted feel more like people desperately trying to not drown and barely keeping above water for the last seven hundred years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T10:43:02-07:00","id":513048,"title":"","content":"Regarding the changed relationship between Sidereals and the Gods of Yu-Shan: I suspect this is the Devs reacting to a common misconception that Sids can't walk down a heavenly street without every god there hissing and booing them, throwing divine turnips at them and overcharging them for every little thing. The books don't actually support this reading, but it wouldn't be the first time the echo chamber blew things out of proportion. <br /> <br /> It's possible that, in order to win over the fans, the Devs are fixing a problem that isn't really broken, but I hope they read the actual source material clearer than that. In any event, even if the masses of gods now enthusiastically support the Fellowship, that doesn't mean that they won't still have problems with the Gods, esp the ones they work closest with! They still have to produce results, and will get in trouble if they don't, or if they cross the line on what they're allowed to do to carry out their duties. Temporary exile from heaven will probably be something we see a lot of, esp as it allows the Seer to conduct extended activities in Creation with his bosses having Plausible Deniability. <br /> <br /> I think hostility will still exist between gods and viziers, but it will most likely be for personal reasons, some insult or inconvenience that you (or your previous incarnation!) caused a minor or major figure in the Bureaucracy that they intend to return to you, for ex. <br /> <br /> Incidentally, as to the Realm officially executing Dragon-Blooded: Yes, this is a thing that happens. There was an incident where no less than a full *General* and all his senior officers were found guilty of Jade embezzlement and publicly beheaded in front of their own troops!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T10:54:45-07:00","id":513056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512525#post512525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a lot of references to it starting from sidereals first edition and along the course of the setting. They don't rule it day to day like the empress did. They did dictate it's course and continue to do so. It's not the gods who make creation what it is today it was the sidereals and dragonblooded as well as every outside factor that couldn't be accounted for.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just need to point out that there's a pretty big difference between &quot;the Realm&quot; and &quot;Creation&quot;. The former only accounts for the Blessed Isle and *some* of the near Threshold, the parts that are Satrapies. The Bronze Faction has some broad influence over those areas, but doesn't, and can't, micro-manage it all. Plenty of developments occur that they don't see coming, as expected of a large nation run by thousands of Exalted essence-users, and they just have to roll with them as best they can. <br /> <br /> The Sidereals certainly don't have a lot of influence over the other bits of the Threshold, including its nations, the barbarian tribes and the Guild (which is the only thing pretty much tying it all together), which is included in &quot;Creation&quot;. Even the Gold Faction spends too much of its time in political feuds with the Bronze as well as doing its actual official job(s) to actually &quot;run things&quot;. There are just too few Siddies to run everything, esp considering that some of them aren't even active yet, some are still young and in training, and still others don't give a shit about Factions and such, and just want to do their jobs and unwind in Heaven during their off-hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:00:41-07:00","id":513062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512509#post512509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are absolutely wise, powerful, mystical masters in their way.<br /> <br /> They're just categorically incapable of trusting anyone to do anything unless they manipulate the crap out of the situation until there's no other choice first.<br /> <br /> ...And to be fair, they're not entirely unjustified in that.<br /> <br /> Still makes them kinda douchey though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> In a way, it's like the 1% in the Real World. Their privileged backgrounds give them access to the best schools and teachers, as well as pre-existing connections in politics and business. On paper, they absolutely seem like the best choices to run the world!<br /> <br /> But of course, that doesn't mean that they are GOOD people, or even good at what they do...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:03:16-07:00","id":513345,"title":"","content":"Administration is like evolution: the keyword is diversity, not optimisation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T02:33:34-07:00","id":517772,"title":"","content":"Actually, it doesn't surprise me that the occasional Sidereal gets executed, now and then. Sure, Heaven is corrupt as heck, in the <i>Exalted</i> era. But there's still the rule of law (just a very corrupt one).<br /> <br /> If a Sidereal actually gets caught, dead to rights, committing a serious offense, there's not much that Kejak or the other Sidereals can do to help him. Sure, they could close ranks, help him escape . . . but then their entire faction becomes accomplices. Even if they get away with it, that's going to break down the fragile fabric of peace in Heaven. And once that happens, its only a matter of time until there's blood in the streets.<br /> <br /> And with all the other problems going on, the last thing Creation needs is a civil war in Heaven. Better to sacrifice the stupid (or unlucky) Sidereal, and maintain the fiction that there's still a veneer of civility and rules. After all, the unfortunate Sidereal will reincarnate, sooner or later. And the other Sidereal can always settle the score, later, quietly, after the crowds have gone away . . .<br /> <br /> Think of Milady du Winters, from <i>The Three Musketeers</i>. She was a very loyal henchwoman to Cardinal Richelieu, and a talented one to boot. And yet, when she's caught in the act, she's still executed. One word from him, and she'd be spared. But then he'd have to answer dangerous questions about what she was doing . . .<br /> <br /> And du Winters' has a daughter, who's an even <i>more </i>promising agent . . . and now has a very personal reason for wanting the Musketeers dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=512761#post512761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I don't figure they think they're infallible, mostly because they seem to rarely <i>succeed</i>.<br /> <br /> Seriously, since the Usurpation, Sidereal plans are mostly mentioned in the gameline to say how they go wrong. Culminating in the entirety of the Fellowship getting exterminated in one go in Return of the Scarlet Empress because hey, why not. I have never quite gotten where the omniscient Sidereal ruler meme came from. Sidereals as depicted feel more like people desperately trying to not drown and barely keeping above water for the last seven hundred years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its worth remembering that the Sidereals have a huge &quot;Butterfly in China&quot; problem, when it comes to their fortunetelling/scheming. Or rather, they have three - the Malfeans, the Yozi, and the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Sidereals use the <i>stars</i> to predict the future, which map the destinies of all creatures born <i>in Creation</i>. But the Malfeans and Yozi predate Creation, and the Fair Folk are from Elsewhere. So the Sidereals have no way of seeing what those factions are up to, until they unleash their plans on the world. And their plans aren't going to mesh well with those of the Sidereals - the Malfeans, for example, are planning the death of Creation itself.<br /> <br /> So it makes perfect sense for the Sidereals to have big, gaping flaws in their plans. They assumed the Yozi were locked away, that the Malfeans were too dead to try anything, and that the Fae still feared the might of the Realm. So they left those factions out of their plans for a new world order . . . and thus were completely blindsided by the Fae invasion, the rise of the Death Lords, and the appearance of the Infernal and Abyssal Exalted.<br /> <br /> They missed half of the power players! Compounded with incidents like the destruction of the Jade Prison (which freed the Solars), is anyone surprised that the Sidereal plans are a mess right now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:16:20-07:00","id":518279,"title":"","content":"By Malfeans do you the Neverborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:31:19-07:00","id":518287,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Malfeans was what they were called back in 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:24:07-07:00","id":518323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=518287#post518287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Malfeans was what they were called back in 1st edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Why they were called that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:30:43-07:00","id":518327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=518323#post518323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Why they were called that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the writers had yet to really grasp the differences between the Neverborn and the Yozis. It was extremely confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:53:18-07:00","id":518345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=518323#post518323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Why they were called that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because in Werewolf the Apocolypse you had the evil &quot;demon&quot; realm called Malfeas (which served as the inspiration for Malfeas in Exalted). Then in Wraith the Oblivion, you had the Malfeans which were these dead-creepy monsters that hung out near Oblivion and were pretty much copy/pasted into Exalted.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, the idea was that Malfeas had been the general of the Primordials, and the Malfeans were those Primordials who swore their loyalty to him and fought to the death. I never had an issue with it, but some people found the terms incredibly confusing and complained about it, so the authors dropped that name in 2nd edition and the Malfeans only went by the name &quot;Neverborn&quot; which had been one of their titles in 1st edition (like the Yozi being called the Demon Princes).<br /> <br /> Post 2nd edition the term &quot;Malfeans&quot; becomes even more confusing as we suddenly find out Malfeas is actually pretty young and didn't came into being after he made the surrender oaths. Prior to that he was essentially an entirely different being. So the idea of the Neverborn calling themselves Malfeans definitely no longer works, as they would have already died before the being known as Malfeas even existed!<br /> <br /> But you still see the term tossed around occasionally as it's been with the gameline since before day zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T12:18:36-07:00","id":518371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=517772#post517772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it makes perfect sense for the Sidereals to have big, gaping flaws in their plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really only makes sense in 2e paradigm where the primary purpose of Sidereals is for them to die and be thwarted constantly to show how big and scary the threat of the latest released book is. Basically, the point of the Sidereals is the same point as Worf or Jedi...they get beat up and tossed around the room or wiped out casually in order to build heat for the current threat.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't even track, because the primary mechanical effects of being outside Fate is that Sids can't mess with your Willpower, can't compel them and can't transport them. Even if we put that aside and say &quot;Oh, but it's <i>supposed</i> to mean that they can't use their prophecy or affect them with Charms,&quot; than that makes the Sidereals <i>complete fucking idiots</i> for relying on their Charms for centuries despite knowing they're completely unreliable, and it makes the Maidens complete shitheads because they're the ones who gave Sidereals Charms to fight the Enemies of Creation(tm) <i>that don't fucking work against the Enemies of Creation(tm)</i>.<br /> <br /> All in all it's a fucking stupid idea and should be dropped like a ton of bricks onto a lead balloon into a toilet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">I have $10 that says that &quot;lawl hubris&quot; will be used at some point in any replies</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T14:44:01-07:00","id":518442,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the Lotus Massacre was only in Return of the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> We also don't know what's up with the Maidens. They're often said to be crazy and they could very well be writing the epic story about how Creation comes to an End. They may also have simply given the Sidereals the best tools they were able to give. Or what they considered the absolute minimum that could get the job done.<br /> <br /> But yeah, making the Sidereals less incompetent and incapable would also help make them sympathetic and, I'm purely guessing here, a better play experience. Being unable to make prophecy or astrology that includes things outside of Fate is plausible. Having more than a few charms that just plain fail against creatures outside of Fate is... weak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-18-2015, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T18:35:54-07:00","id":518631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=518371#post518371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all it's a fucking stupid idea and should be dropped like a ton of bricks onto a lead balloon into a toilet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear hear! I also hope the whole &quot;closed charmset&quot; is dropped.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:21:01-07:00","id":518672,"title":"","content":"The devs have been adamant that they won't drop it because it would warp the play experience of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> AFAIK they have not said whether the 3E closed charmset will be larger or the same size as before. With the way the 1E charms and scriptures aren't set up for 2E/3E abilities, the 2E charms were reportedly all mucked up, and the other Exalted are getting bigger charmsets in 3E, I think that's at least a good chance of longer scriptures (re-written for the 3E abilities) and larger charmtrees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T21:27:12-07:00","id":518875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=518672#post518672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs have been adamant that they won't drop it because it would warp the play experience of Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goddamnit.<br /> <br /> The problem is that even if they expand the charmset, the other splats will inevitably get new charms in other books, but the Sidereals, of course, will not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T22:10:10-07:00","id":518926,"title":"","content":"Then IMHO I guess it'll probably be better if you and like-minded Sidereal players try to prevail upon them to write longer-than-usual charm-trees, with well-matched scriptures, for their hardback. By which I mean, longer than the charmtrees other Exalted are getting in their hardbacks.<br /> <br /> I suppose they could radically restructure them by giving each ability multiple charm-trees, each with a separate scripture that starts with the charm after the branching off from the common root (if there is a common root). That would establish a theoretical framework for additional trees and scriptures to be added to each ability later, without destroying the overall arrangement. I guess it would require each constellation to have multiple interpretations. I don't know if that would avoid their objection to an open charmset -- whether they object only to messing up the scriptures, or the charmset being expandable at all.<br /> <br /> I dunno, you probably know 23765 times more about Sidereal charms than I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-19-2015, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T23:47:52-07:00","id":519029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xeno426</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=518875#post518875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goddamnit.<br /> <br /> The problem is that even if they expand the charmset, the other splats will inevitably get new charms in other books, but the Sidereals, of course, will not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs have said that having a closed charmset will not stop them adding Sidereal Charms if they're needed; in-universe, the new Charms will always have been there.<br /> <br /> Which is to say the closed charmset is only an in-universe thing, and won't stop there being more Sid Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T00:26:22-07:00","id":519043,"title":"","content":"Multiple Charm trees is what I'm hoping for, honestly, particularly Charm trees aspected to different Maidens. It'd be interesting to see Presence according to Jupiter or Saturn, or Occult according to Mars or Mercury. If we're not going to get an open or semi-open Charmset (and according to a lot of dev commentary, we're quite definitely not), that seems like multiple trees could at least inject some new ideas and perspective into Sidereals. Plus, we know they're thinking about that for Dragon-Blooded.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:05:21-07:00","id":519534,"title":"","content":"That would be stupendous for Dragon-Blooded, but how would that work with Sidereals? Currently, as I understand it, each ability is tied to a single constellation, associated with one astrological college, Division of the Bureau of Destiny, and Maiden. Would there be new constellations (and colleges) added, or abilities no longer associated with colleges, or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:35:59-07:00","id":519551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=519029#post519029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The devs have said that having a closed charmset will not stop them adding Sidereal Charms if they're needed; in-universe, the new Charms will always have been there.<br /> <br /> Which is to say the closed charmset is only an in-universe thing, and won't stop there being more Sid Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there will still be a few balance considerations behind the power and progression of Sidereals Charms when it's assumed that players and characters can't readily develop their own.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if the only problem is the idea that they'll be locked out of evolution in Charm technology, that's been covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T07:45:09-07:00","id":519557,"title":"","content":"I personally like the idea of shortcomings in the prophetic powers of the Sidereals when it comes to things like demons (and would like it to be more apparent in their prophetic Charms), but more in the manner of Sidereals actually seeing visions of things &quot;near&quot; demons becoming hazy (ala Vision of Escaflowne and Dune). The kind of thing that can make for a sense of ominous foreshadowing and let Sidereals pro-actively move against things that can take their plans and visions off of the rails, as well as the idea that things around demons or mighty fae become more obfuscated when the creature has actual plans to draw them under their own auspices, such as the idea that Sidereals lose a handle on the fate of dreams and destiny of souls of those who are consecrated to Makarios (whereas those who are going to have a drink with him are just a bit fuzzy around the edges).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T08:33:58-07:00","id":519622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=519029#post519029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The devs have said that having a closed charmset will not stop them adding Sidereal Charms if they're needed; in-universe, the new Charms will always have been there.<br /> <br /> Which is to say the closed charmset is only an in-universe thing, and won't stop there being more Sid Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if they, or we, come up witha Charm that makes the most sense being between two others, like a new Awareness charm that fits best between Expected Pain and Supernal Awareness? Will a book suddenly say &quot;this charm has always been here, but you now need to buy it if you have SA?&quot; Or if a new charm now contributes to the capstone charm you already bought, do you just get it for free?<br /> <br /> They *could* just rule that all new charms must be either stand-alone or topping an existing tree, but that seems a bit too restrictive. And should Sidereals/Maidens/Players be able to make up new Capstone charms, complete with new Sutras, giving a tree two or more such charms?<br /> <br /> EDIT: And didn't the Sidereal Errata get rid of the idea that Sid charms can't effect creatures outside of Fate? If so, it seems likely that won't be coming back for 3E, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T08:44:04-07:00","id":519627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=519622#post519622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: And didn't the Sidereal Errata get rid of the idea that Sid charms can't effect creatures outside of Fate? If so, it seems likely that won't be coming back for 3E, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It pared down the mechanical considerations, but maintained the idea of a dispensation (the example was how Ligier won't conclude that you were never there if you use Avoidance Kata to dodge him).<br /> <br /> I don't think the idea is out, just that it was a low priority in the herculean effort of Sidereal Errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:13:28-07:00","id":519702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=519534#post519534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be stupendous for Dragon-Blooded, but how would that work with Sidereals? Currently, as I understand it, each ability is tied to a single constellation, associated with one astrological college, Division of the Bureau of Destiny, and Maiden. Would there be new constellations (and colleges) added, or abilities no longer associated with colleges, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were going to do this, I'd break the link between Division and college/constellation and let each Division/Maiden interpret each College differently. So you'd have a Charm tree for Investigation that reflects Jupiter's take on the Key, one for Saturn's take on the Key (&quot;ending&quot; mysteries somehow?), one for Mercury's (focused on the &quot;journey to the truth&quot;), etc. You might have new sutras for these, or you might just have one sutra per ability and talk about how Sidereal Charms reflect cosmic understanding lensed through each Maiden's particular worldview. Whichever works. (You'd probably still have a Division associated primarily with each Constellation, but it always seemed a bit weird to me that Serenity wouldn't have a good solid viewpoint on, say, the Rising Smoke or the Mast.)<br /> <br /> The other hidden benefit of this is that it allows for the possibility of heretical, unorthodox or otherwise hidden knowledge forming the basis of secret Charm trees, known only to factions or even individual elders in the Bureau. Which I at least find interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:21:53-07:00","id":521997,"title":"","content":"About the Out of Fate thing, done well, I think it's totally fine for Sidereals to be confounded by uncanny demons and outsiders who are blurry and confusing glimpses in the Sidereal foresight, and that to combat and work around mighty demons, Sidereals have to use old fashioned Sidereal cleverness, cunning and wisdom and their powers over that which is in Fate. So long as it's presented as a challenge they can do, working against this adversity builds their character, and it helps prevent the community feeling like the setting is stale because the Sidereals can predict everything, while not stopping the Sidereals actually be prophets.<br /> <br /> What is actually the problem is the idea that &quot;Lol blind prophets&quot;*, where the Sidereals are sort of like... *unaware* of this factor, and the Bronze Faction are presumed to be sitting back looking pretty satisfied with themselves that they know everything and Creation is, if diminished, safe forevermore (while the Gold Faction are no better, just hyping themselves up for a glorious age of the return of the Solars, in their pocket, while being kind of blase to the threats outside of Fate out the door).<br /> <br /> That the Sidereals cannot predict, so well, that which has no place in Fate should be a basic foundational part of the Sidereal knowledge, and they should be planning around this and mitigating it since Year Zero, like the intelligence service they are. It should be an acknowledged part of the debates that rage between them around the right path to take, and a nagging concern to those who chose the Path of Bronze. No &quot;lol at the blind, blind prophets. so arrogant, yet so, so blind. fortunately the Solars! are! here! to save the day&quot; that's just cheap heat.<br /> <br /> (I'd also say the some Sidereals could maybe sometimes even be trying to exploit the way Out of Fate defies Fate to beat the Great Prophecy and bring some glory or a better life back to the world, although obviously that's not something they do on the regular, and do judiciously, as every time they invite something out of fate into the world, destiny gets a little more destabilised, and this is sort of the opposite of what they are for).<br /> <br /> *well the &quot;blind prophets&quot; sidebar isn't *literally* &quot;lol blind prophets&quot; at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:46:44-07:00","id":522016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=521997#post521997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where the Sidereals are sort of like... *unaware* of this factor, and the Bronze Faction are presumed to be sitting back looking pretty satisfied with themselves that they know everything and Creation is, if diminished, safe forevermore (while the Gold Faction are no better, just hyping themselves up for a glorious age of the return of the Solars, in their pocket, while being kind of blase to the threats outside of Fate out the door).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this depiction right here (or my impression that they're depicted this way) is why I hate the Sidereals, or at least the Bronze. They aren't honest about trying to destroy the world or make it into Hell, they're pointing at how horrifically atrocious the world is, how it's closer to apocalypse every single day, how many billions have died hideously for their plans, how many atrocities the Dragon-Blooded and Deathlords commit every week ... patting each other on the back for a Job Well Done. They claim to be saving the world but it's blindingly <b><i>obvious</i></b> that they're destroying it instead, and it makes their self-righteousness intolerable. The Gold faction are probably idiots too, but at least they don't like and <b><i>approve</i></b> of the horror show Creation has become.<br /> <br /> They'd be harder to hate if both Factions, and the independents, were ALL willing to openly admit that Creation is not surviving well, that humanity is suffering unacceptable harm, that the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusades were bad things and might happen again -- and if they ALL admitted that they need to get their buts in gear to find real solutions. Just because the Bronze believe that Solars and Lunars aren't a viable solution should not mean they're so obnoxiously stupid and sociopathically callous they believe there are no problems happening at all, or that the Dragon-Blooded have never made mistakes or committed atrocities of their own.<br /> <br /> The Gold Faction say &quot;This is a problem, your Bronze Vision is a nightmare, we have a plan to make it better.&quot; and the canonical Bronze party line (before 5 years ago) seems to be &quot;No, everything is fine, there are no problems and we should never try to improve anything. This mess is <b><i>exactly</i></b> what we wanted.&quot; Their response instead should be &quot;No, our Vision was correct, these problems were caused by beings Outside of Fate. We have a better plan to fix these problems, as usual we're understaffed but we're working on it.&quot; and their plan should be presented as plausible and potentially sufficient. The independents should have their own suggestions that don't fit either faction's plans, or believe the Maidens have a plan that they need to obey. They Sidereals are cursed to be arrogant and self-righteous, but they should not watch Creation die screaming and respond with apathy or satisfaction. Their default should not be horrible callousness, and no Exalted should default to Chumps To Dumb To Live. The Bronze's plan shouldn't be, with OOC knowledge, unambiguously unviable.<br /> <br /> Basically, the debates should not be &quot;Is the post-Contagion status quo good, yes/no?&quot; It should be &quot;Who is to blame for this mess, and what should we do to fix it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-20-2015, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:01:00-07:00","id":522162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522016#post522016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this depiction right here (or my impression that they're depicted this way) is why I hate the Sidereals, or at least the Bronze. They aren't honest about trying to destroy the world or make it into Hell, they're pointing at how horrifically atrocious the world is, how it's closer to apocalypse every single day, how many billions have died hideously for their plans, how many atrocities the Dragon-Blooded and Deathlords commit every week ... patting each other on the back for a Job Well Done. They claim to be saving the world but it's blindingly <b><i>obvious</i></b> that they're destroying it instead, and it makes their self-righteousness intolerable. The Gold faction are probably idiots too, but at least they don't like and <b><i>approve</i></b> of the horror show Creation has become.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er.<br /> <br /> Erinys, I'm often wrong, so I'm a bit hesitant to wade in here... but I think you might be arguing against fanon here, not Sidereals-as-they-are.<br /> <br /> I'm a giant Sidereal fanboy and I've seen very little evidence in the actual books, in either editions, that the Bronze Faction in any way has a mindset of &quot;everything is fine, there are no problems and we should never try to improve anything. This mess is <b><i>exactly</i></b> what we wanted.&quot; Quite the opposite, really. And that's certainly not the canonical Bronze party line.<br /> <br /> The members of the Bronze Faction aren't members of it because they think the current stat of Creation is awesome; they're members of it because they think that this is the best that can be done. Chejop Kejak and the Inner Circle are not portrayed, ever, as self-deluded idiots who think that everything is amazing, they're portrayed as people who are working themselves to death to try and make the world a better place than it currently is and to stop other people from making it worse... by their own standards of &quot;better&quot; and &quot;worse.&quot; Kejak hasn't been propping up the Realm because he thinks all the slavery and racism is super sweet; he's doing it because he doesn't see a workable alternative that he considers to have an acceptable risk/reward tradeoff.<br /> <br /> It is true that the Bronzies often try to convince other factions that everything is cool, they're in control, it is all going according to &amp;c., but that's, you know, politically motivated lying, which the golds are no less guilty of.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their response instead should be &quot;No, our Vision was correct, these problems were caused by beings Outside of Fate. We have a better plan to fix these problems, as usual we're understaffed but we're working on it.&quot; and their plan should be presented as plausible and potentially sufficient. </div> </div> </div>This is actually very close to what it is; it's both &quot;these problems were caused by beings outside of fate&quot; combined with &quot;our Vision is pretty shitty, but we didn't adopt it because it was awesome, we adopted it because the other Visions were even shittier.&quot; They don't deny the existence of problems, and their response to problems is usually &quot;we don't have the resources&quot; or &quot;we're working on <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Their default should not be horrible callousness </div> </div> </div>It's not. People don't play Bronze Faction Sidereals to play people who are either horribly callous or dupes. The writers didn't write them that way, because they knew that would be shit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bronze's plan shouldn't be, with OOC knowledge, unambiguously unviable. </div> </div> </div>And it isn't.<br /> <br /> In-universe, the Bronze Faction's plan has been working pretty fucking well. Creation endures. Most people are born, live out their lives, and die. Many people live and die in horrible conditions, but if the Bronze Faction had no acted everybody in Creation would be the violated mind-slave of the mad, slavering tyrants the Solars were well on their way to turning into. Jenna Moran's &quot;there is no part of you they have not defiled&quot; vision for &quot;what happens if there isn't a Usurpation&quot; would have come to pass. The Realm may not be awesome, but the Realm has millions of people sheltering under its aegis who eat three full meals a day and go to sleep with their family in a warm house. That's what the Bronze Faction has brought to Creation. It's not perfect, but it is better than the alternatives.<br /> <br /> Their response to the Gold Faction is &quot;you want to hand power back to the people who turned into insane god-kings. You're crazy.&quot; That's a reasonable response!<br /> <br /> In fact, I would argue that even OOC, the Bronze Faction plan isn't unambiguously unviable. It is explicitly possible within the setting to play a gang of Bronze Faction PCs who place a successor to the Scarlet Empress on the throne, stabilize the Realm, clean up Heaven, find a way of sidelining or otherwise co-opting the Solars, and basically keep on as they've been keeping on. Their corebooks in both editions present this as an option!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T12:44:33-07:00","id":522328,"title":"","content":"Thanks for helping to clear up my misunderstandings, Mercushio. I appreciate it! Like I said I don't have many books so I get most setting info secondhand. So in summary, what you're saying is that the Sidereals who support the Second Age status quo don't actually believe it's good and it doesn't make them happy, they just believe that there are no other options so they should not try to change it?<br /> <br /> Part of the reason I feel strongly, I think, is that the Realm is a representative of the most extremely oppressive groups in the real world, and the Bronze are a representative of the cynical, cold-hearted bastards who prop the empires up while they know how bad it is, and brainwash the rest of us to not even want anything better. The real world has real alternatives, and I have a hard time believing that Creation has none -- or that anyone with a scrap of human decency or compassion would not look for alternatives.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also don't fully understand your post. What is the Bronze plan then, and how do the books depict it as having any chance to prevent apocalypse, let alone improve things? How can it when the DBs clearly couldn't defend Creation even when they were far more numerous? It still looks much the same as &quot;Your job is to bust the Yozis out of prison so they can brain-rape you forever, luckily your goal is impossible, have fun.&quot;<br /> <br /> I consider the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade the definitive, unambiguous, no-going-back failure of the original Bronze plan. It's obvious to me that the Empress barely pulled the bacon out of the fire, and there is no particular reason to think she or anyone else is likely to pull that off next time. The Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals have not proven themselves sufficient to defend Creation from outside threats. It's clear to me that they cannot, because the world is fraying further into the Wyld and Underworld and they are not keeping up. Even what little they've accomplished in slowing down the inevitable apocalypse has depended on the Lunars doing most of the actual fighting on the Wyld front lines, which is probably not working so well either with the Immaculates killing them (and 1E-2E reportedly made Lunars kinda incompetent). None of the major players except the Sidereals themselves are even paying attention to the threat of the Deathlords. While some Ledaal try to warn the Realm about it, the other Dynasts are too busy carousing, infighting, and Wyld Hunting to care.<br /> <br /> Also, why was the Immaculate religion/society designed to teach that the Dragon-Blooded have an unquestionable right to abuse mortals any way they please? Yes, the Dragon-Blooded are &quot;supposed&quot; to be &quot;gentle&quot; in their oppression, but they're also supposedly born with the moral right to do absolutely anything they want whatsoever, slavery is mandated by the Dragons, and nobody has any right to question them at all. The inflexible caste system inherently encourages abuse, and anyone who lived through the First Age would realise that. Worse, DB society teaches them that it's more important to kill Lunars and backstab other Houses/Gentes than to do anything at all about the Deathlords, Fair Folk, etc. That's not useful for keeping Creation safe. My understanding is that the Bronze Faction got to make the Immaculate religion say anything they wanted when they designed it, so why is this the best they can do? Do they consider Lunars and Solars an even bigger threat than the Deathlords, and why? At least if the Solars (or Yozis!) took over the world would still exist.*<br /> <br /> I also don't really understand the assumption that the Solars inevitably <i><b>will</b></i> go insane again. We know OOC that it's true because of the Curse, but the Bronze just seem to assume it with no evidence, even though the social structure of the First Age that fed the egos of the Solars has been ground into less than dust.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: I don't know if this is clear. I'm stating my confusion and sincerely asking for explanation of where the things I don't understand, not arguing that Mercushio is wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Which is a legitimate reason for a compassionate Infernal to support the Reclamation -- at least as legitimate as the Bronze Vision. The Exalted are failing miserably to keep Creation alive, so they don't deserve to rule it anymore. Even if the Yozis do horrible things to humanity, the Deathlords and Fae would do worse to Creation itself, and the Exalted can't or just plain won't stop them. So move over, Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2015, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:20:14-07:00","id":522364,"title":"","content":"I think the Sidereals get hit especially hard by the idea that Holden has criticised from 2e. The view that the Deathlords or the Yozis are going to come in and roll over the world, so what's the point of worrying about its politics and any of the statecraft behind its kingdoms, or any of the careful, slow work that took? And really, since this is *obvious* why isn't everyone just getting behind the Solars to back them while they fight apocalyptic battles against enormous dangerous super demons right NOW?<br /> <br /> Especially if the fanon where the Sidereals don't even seem to know or feel its important that they can't predict the influence of those Outside Fate comes into play.<br /> <br /> I appreciate a lot of this maybe is fanon, but I do second the idea that, speaking of what I hope for from the 3e presentation, l at least some of the Bronze Faction Sidereals really should be portrayed as self consciously looking to build a better world, rather than be perceived as merely maintainers of the status quo and managers of decline. (Or, god, mucketty muck backroom politicians whose dodgy dealings have no impact outside keeping wealth and power where it is and who are totally unwilling to take the responsibility to improve people's lives that their office commands.)<br /> <br /> I don't think its a realistic or cool way to dichotomise people as either willing to get into lockstep behind, alongside or pulling the strings of risky, extreme golden heroes (Gold Faction) or as people who are just happy maintaining a status quo, without clearly working for anything better and think its the best anything can be. Especially when they have the power of a Celestial Exalt and huge command over and insight into destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:30:58-07:00","id":522379,"title":"","content":"2E definitely depicts the Second Age as an era of obvious and terrifying decline into the Void. I think 1E did, too.<br /> <br /> Then there are issues like the fact that anytime you fight a massive war or have a big massacre, you risk creating a new Shadowland... yet that behavior is common fare for the Realm, and in fact the Dragon-Blooded got busy creating shadowlands immediately after the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522364#post522364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think its a realistic or cool way to dichotomise people as either willing to get into lockstep behind, alongside or pulling the strings of risky, extreme golden heroes (Gold Faction) or as people who are just happy maintaining a status quo, without clearly working for anything better and think its the best anything can be. Especially when they have the power of a Celestial Exalt and huge command over and insight into destiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yess!! There should be Sidereals who have other plans. Viable plans that are neither stupid, nor doomed. But the major Factions should too. The Gold Faction should have concrete ideas about researching (or altering?) Solar psychology and preventing insanity, and there should be a real chance they can discover the Curse. The Bronze Faction should have actual alternatives to what they've tried for the last 1500 years, and the desire and real ability to stop the decline.<br /> <br /> In 2E the Exalted are depicted as the only people who have any particular hope of saving Creation (because the gods are almost all corrupt jerks who don't care, especially the useless Incarnae -- which is another problem because Yu-Shan requires Creation and a lot of them keep their stuff in Creation). But there are only ...<br /> <br /> * DBs who clearly can't protect Creation and have done a lot to break it ...<br /> * Solars and Lunars who could save Creation if everyone got off their backs, but would probably turn around and mess it up afterwards ...<br /> * Abyssals who are forced to destroy the world whether they want to or not ...<br /> * unpredictable Infernals who at best are no better than Solars ...<br /> * and Sidereals, whose <i><b>only</b></i> ideas are to put one of the above on the throne or try to save the world with no help.<br /> <br /> Hopefully in 3E there will be other options that look viable and not-stupid. Exalted are supposed to be able to bend the structure of reality with crazy charms and sorcery (or at least this is what I'm told.) Even in the First Age, they had those monoliths protecting Creation from the Wyld. Why are the Sidereals and Lunars uninterested in rebuilding those? In fact, what moron destroyed them in the first place? Why not do something sorcerous to reinforce the barrier between the Underworld and Creation? Why not try to figure out why the Solars and Lunars go bugnuts, which the Incarnae probably didn't intend?<br /> <br /> What was the Sidereal reaction to the Contagion? The Incarnae and Celestial gods shrugged and left all life to die. The Immaculates concluded that the Lunars caused it. The Sidereals should have tried to figure out what caused it, and encouraged the new Immaculate Order to <b><i>concentrate</i></b> their resources on opposing whoever-it-was. Instead of the Anathema, because the Sidereals know darn well the Lunars didn't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-20-2015, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:43:07-07:00","id":522421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=521997#post521997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Sidereals cannot predict, so well, that which has no place in Fate should be a basic foundational part of the Sidereal knowledge, and they should be planning around this and mitigating it since Year Zero, like the intelligence service they are. It should be an acknowledged part of the debates that rage between them around the right path to take, and a nagging concern to those who chose the Path of Bronze. No &quot;lol at the blind, blind prophets. so arrogant, yet so, so blind. fortunately the Solars! are! here! to save the day&quot; that's just cheap heat.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorite part is that the Sidereals &quot;canonically&quot; have <i>at least</i> one spy informing on goings on in the Underworld, and were still blindsided by Thorns. Apparently the Green Lady was, for five years, too busy playing dress up and wiping her own memory to take five minutes to send in a report:<br /> <br /> &quot;Dear Kejak, Dual Monarch instituted right of <i>prima nocta</i>, which is all kinds of eww. Calendar of Setish found to have little chocolates inside. BTW, probably not important, Deathlords have DEATH ASPECTED SOLARS THEY ARE TRAINING TO HATE AND CONQUER CREATION. Weather remains fair. See attached receipts for reimbursment. Love, GL.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T13:48:08-07:00","id":522453,"title":"","content":"Wait, is that canon?<br /> <br /> It makes them look as useless as the 1E-2E Lunars who accomplished nothing constructive for 1500 years, so the Solars could sweep in and do it for them.<br /> <br /> Also, were the Gold Faction doing anything to move their goals forward before the Jade Prison broke, or just complaining about hypothetical plans to stop the end of the world that they totally couldn't act on because of The Man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-20-2015, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:06:11-07:00","id":522577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522453#post522453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, is that canon?<br /> <br /> It makes them look as useless as the 1E-2E Lunars who accomplished nothing constructive for 1500 years, so the Solars could sweep in and do it for them.<br /> <br /> Also, were the Gold Faction doing anything to move their goals forward before the Jade Prison broke, or just complaining about hypothetical plans to stop the end of the world that they totally couldn't act on because of The Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Green Lady is a complicated matter. She is technically spying on the Deathlords for Yu-Shan, except she is also a spy for the Deathlords against the Sids and the other Deathlords. Essentially in order to keep her cover she created a mess of alternate identities to the point where it is unknown who her actual loyalties are to. Also we're talking full fledged personalities who are actually the person they claim to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:43:29-07:00","id":522603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522453#post522453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, were the Gold Faction doing anything to move their goals forward before the Jade Prison broke, or just complaining about hypothetical plans to stop the end of the world that they totally couldn't act on because of The Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that part kinda bugs me. Why does the Gold Faction endure so long after the Solars basically cease to be a factor? Are they holding out for the handful of Solars that continue to exist and get run down by the Wyld Hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","user":"Xeno426","date":". 05-21-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T15:58:06-07:00","id":522613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xeno426</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522603#post522603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that part kinda bugs me. Why does the Gold Faction endure so long after the Solars basically cease to be a factor? Are they holding out for the handful of Solars that continue to exist and get run down by the Wyld Hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my mind, there really wasn't a Gold faction before the Contagion. Just Ayesha Ura and some drunken elders. After the contagion, some of Sidereals jumped ship to the Gold Faction. The main goal of the Gold Faction was the find and open the Jade Prison*. Secondary goals include gaining the support of gods for when the Jade Prison is open, studying Solars to learn how to best guide them, and research a cure for their madness. Saving the few solar would a moral victory, but not very useful in the long run.<br /> <br /> *This only works if you go with the option of the Gold Faction using the Deathlords as a Cat's paw in opening the Jade Prison. Boy was the Gold Faction surprised when they only got 150 shards instead of the 300 they were expecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T16:03:26-07:00","id":522618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522328#post522328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't really understand the assumption that the Solars inevitably <i><b>will</b></i> go insane again. We know OOC that it's true because of the Curse, but the Bronze just seem to assume it with no evidence, even though the social structure of the First Age that fed the egos of the Solars has been ground into less than dust.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have to assume it with no evidence because they predicted it. When they cast their Great Prophecy they saw many visions; in one of them, the one where they (the sids) did absolutely nothing about the solars and their increasingly alarming behavior, creation was either* destroyed or turned into hell.<br /> Now whether that prediction is as accurate as the bronze faction sidereals think it is, it's another matter (they clearly didn't predict either the Great Contagion or the Balorian Crusade, both extinction level events).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522162#post522162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually very close to what it is; it's both &quot;these problems were caused by beings outside of fate&quot; combined with &quot;our Vision is pretty shitty, but we didn't adopt it because it was awesome, we adopted it because the other Visions were even shittier.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, not all of their visions were shittier, in some of them things were better, i am talking first age better here. The issue is that in the visions they tried to help the solars but their success was guaranteed, they might be able to help** the solars with their insanity and all things would be good, well and <i>golden</i> in the world OR they might fail and the world would be destroyed or turned to hell*. It's just that they <i>choose</i> to do the sure thing instead of taking a gambit.<br /> <br /> *i can't remember which one since it has been some time since i have read it, maybe it was both (2 visions)<br /> <br /> **Cure or manage the insanity, again i am not remembering very well since it has been some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":816,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","user":"leo1925","date":". 05-20-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T16:09:02-07:00","id":522624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522618#post522618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> in one of them, the one where they (the sids) <u>didn't do absolutely nothing</u> about the solars, creation was either* destroyed or turned into hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why didn't the sids choose not to act?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T16:20:34-07:00","id":522628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xeno426</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522624#post522624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why didn't the sids choose not to act?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the double negative, it's a mistake, i edited my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T20:49:04-07:00","id":522886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522379#post522379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . Even in the First Age, they had those monoliths protecting Creation from the Wyld. Why are the Sidereals and Lunars uninterested in rebuilding those? In fact, what moron destroyed them in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said they were destroyed? If we look at (real world) history, they were probably carted off to adorn city plazas and the mansions of rich aristocrats. They're tall, cool looking, and they &quot;bring good luck&quot; - they'd be a must-have accessory for any up-and-comer.<br /> <br /> For a real world example, look at Cleopatra's Needles. They're a serious of monoliths originally raised in ancient Egypt. Today, they're scattered across three continents, in places like Rome, London, and New York City's Central Park.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not do something sorcerous to reinforce the barrier between the Underworld and Creation? Why not try to figure out why the Solars and Lunars go bugnuts, which the Incarnae probably didn't intend? </div> </div> </div>Good question - and I imagine there are a number of Exalted working on that exact problem. However, they may not have the right powers to do so. Each type of Exalted has a pretty strict theme, after all. And with Solars (whose Eclipse caste probably built the first monoliths) being imprisoned and hunted for 15 centuries . . . They'd probably have to completely re-invent/discover a new process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 05-20-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T21:21:37-07:00","id":522908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522886#post522886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said they were destroyed? If we look at (real world) history, they were probably carted off to adorn city plazas and the mansions of rich aristocrats. They're tall, cool looking, and they &quot;bring good luck&quot; - they'd be a must-have accessory for any up-and-comer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same question. What nutjob thought that conspicuous wealth and privilege was more important than Creation not being devoured by the Wyld? And it was either one nutjob who stole all the monoliths, or a conspiracy of hundreds of nutjobs all doing it, and... just like Marama's death-camp project that built a huge shadowland, the Sidereals did ... <b><i>what</i></b> to stop it? Still haven't done boo to put them back even after the Balorian Crusade?<br /> <br /> The Lunars have an excuse for accomplishing so little: everyone except outer-Threshhold barbarians is trying to kill them. But the Sidereals are on top, and successfully reprogrammed most of human society 180 degrees from what it used to be. They're social engineers on par with the Solars. They can clearly do amazing things! If they want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522618#post522618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't have to assume it with no evidence because they predicted it. When they cast their Great Prophecy they saw many visions; in one of them, the one where they (the sids) did absolutely nothing about the solars and their increasingly alarming behavior, creation was either* destroyed or turned into hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a starting point of the already-corrupt First Age Solar Deliberative with nobody bothering to reform it. But that society is as dead as the Neverborn. Why did the Usurpation require that the new society is built on repeating that Usurpation forever, no matter how much the social context changes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522162#post522162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jenna Moran's &quot;there is no part of you they have not defiled&quot; vision for &quot;what happens if there isn't a Usurpation&quot; would have come to pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't something I know about, probably I don't have that book. Can you please summarize what it said about Solar rule? I know the First Age Solars are vaguely supposed to have been worse than the Scarlet Empire, but I don't know of anything concrete that was actually worse. They massacred mortals with exotic weapons and Wyld explosions instead of boring ol' steel and fire, but dead is dead. How is the Scarlet Empire an improvement? They look just as tyrannical to me, but in addition they also can't or won't do jack about the Deathlords and Fae.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted combine crazy, dirt ignorance, and sapient WMD. That should be something terrifying that any right-thinking person hesitates to get behind... but all the alternatives have proven themselves to be much worse. Except the Lunars, nobody's given them a chance I guess.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this is clear. I'm stating my confusion and sincerely asking for explanation, not arguing that Mercushio is definitely wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2015, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T22:16:45-07:00","id":522932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522908#post522908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't something I know about, what book is it in? Probably one I don't have. I know the First Age Solars are vaguely supposed to have been worse than the Scarlet Empire, but I don't know of anything concrete that was actually worse. They massacred mortals with exotic weapons and Wyld explosions instead of boring ol' steel and fire, but dead is dead. How is the Scarlet Empire an improvement? They look just as tyrannical to me, but in addition they also can't or won't do jack about the Deathlords and Fae.<br /> <br /> The Solar Exalted combine crazy, dirt ignorance, and sapient WMD. That should be something terrifying that any right-thinking person hesitates to get behind... but all the alternatives have proven themselves to be much worse. Except the Lunars, nobody's given them a chance I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;He who fights monsters should see to it that he himself does not become a monster.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Life under the Primordials sucked for everyone without a multi-soul existence (and some who did). The Primordials played with human lives like they were nothing and basically fucked with reality for their amusement. Because of this, the gods made Exalts to fight in the Primordial War, to make things suck less for everybody. We have the Glorious First Age after that where everything sucked less and the new bosses (the Solars) weren't as inclined to fuck with reality, in part because they couldn't. Until they started to realize they could. Solar excesses in the First Age started to look like the rule of the Primordials, godly superbeings that used humanity and reality itself for their amusement. When projections say the Solars will become just as bad as the Primordials themselves, any alternative looks preferable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T22:20:21-07:00","id":522933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522618#post522618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, not all of their visions were shittier, in some of them things were better, i am talking first age better here. The issue is that in the visions they tried to help the solars but their success was guaranteed, they might be able to help** the solars with their insanity and all things would be good, well and <i>golden</i> in the world OR they might fail and the world would be destroyed or turned to hell*. It's just that they <i>choose</i> to do the sure thing instead of taking a gambit.<br /> <br /> *i can't remember which one since it has been some time since i have read it, maybe it was both (2 visions)<br /> <br /> **Cure or manage the insanity, again i am not remembering very well since it has been some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall in the Sid book there were 3 prophecy made during the meeting. There was the bronze prophecy* which was basically &quot;What happens if we take the Solars out of power?&quot; That led to a lesser Creation, but it still existed even if it wasn't as good. This was not too popular when done, but you had some who were in favor of the idea since the world still existed and all.<br /> <br /> Then it was the gold prophecy which amounted to, &quot;So what if we point out to the Solars that they're getting kind of horrifyingly insane?&quot; That was tricky because some parts of it implied that if it was pulled off right then the world could reach even greater, but if things went wrong it could get pretty bad and there was a possibility of ending reality in the long run.There were supporters of this partially because it didn't add nightmarish amounts of work to the Sidereal workload, but also because it could potentially handle the problems. Essentially this was supported by your risk takers and those who really really believed that exalts were meant to do the impossible and working with the Solars had previously allowed amazing and near impossible things to happen before.<br /> <br /> At this point you still have a good number of Sidereal's in the undecided camp because of the problems that Bronze would cause, but weren't all that thrilled with the whole prospect of accidentally dooming reality.<br /> <br /> Then there was the dark one which was basically, &quot;What if we don't interfere?&quot; The result was described as taking the madness of the Wyld, the cruelty of Malfeas, and the and the despair of the Underworld cranked them up a few notches and mashed it all together. This was ,shockingly, supported by no one. As a result the Sidereal came to the conclusion that they do something, Bronze won over the most because well Sidereal job one is not dooming reality and it's hard to support the off chance when the risk is &quot;and then everything everywhere dies.&quot;<br /> <br /> *Technically all of them were called The Vision of ____, but I'm being lazy on my typing there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T03:33:23-07:00","id":523069,"title":"","content":"I am aware of the whole &quot;are sidereals heroes or cowards for taking the safe route instead of the risky one?&quot;.<br /> On one hand they are cowards and not worthy of their exalted powers for not trying to do the hard thing for the greater result, on the other hand they are heroes because they took the burden of murdering so many and bringing so much pain to everyone* in order to make absolutely sure that future men would have a world to live in, they took upon themselves and bore a burden that nobody else could bore.<br /> <br /> By the way, why did sidereals murder lunars as well and drove them out of the Realm? Did they predicted that the lunars will be incompetent for 2 iterations of the universe?**<br /> <br /> *i am talking about the Usurpation here.<br /> <br /> **sorry about that, couldn't help myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522908#post522908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a starting point of the already-corrupt First Age Solar Deliberative with nobody bothering to reform it. But that society is as dead as the Neverborn. Why did the Usurpation require that the new society is built on repeating that Usurpation forever, no matter how much the social context changes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you elaborate on that a bit? What do you mean by repeating the Usurpation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":816,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","user":"leo1925","date":". 05-21-2015, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:11:05-07:00","id":523145,"title":"","content":"I mean creating the Immaculate Philosophy and Wyld Hunt. They assumed the crazy was inherent to Solar exaltations, and not a result of Solar society. We know OOC it is, but they had no reason to think so. The Prophecy only showed the Solar Deliberative, in its First Age form, ruining the world.<br /> <br /> They destroyed Solar society. Great! But instead of building a better society and then giving new Solars a chance to grow better than their predecessors with guidance, they built a shittier (equally oppressive) society and locked the Solars away forever. They never made any attempt to find out if the Solars were capable of getting better. Didn't attempt the reform in the first place, didn't attempt reform later after their corrupt Deliberative was gone. They destroyed the most obvious source of the corruption, but didn't bother to stop afterwards and ask if that had been sufficient. They just kept on murdering innocent people, completely unnecessarily as far as any of them could know, and planned to keep doing that for eternity. They had no actual evidence that new Solars, separately raised in a completely different society from the Solar Deliberative, would go crazy at all. They built a worldwide society so single-mindedly obsessed with murdering those innocent people that most Dragon-Bloods are now unwilling to even consider the possibility that Deathlords or Fair Folk are a threat to Creation, even though everybody in Creation knows something resembling them almost destroyed the world.<br /> <br /> Real human beings do not suddenly become serial killers or gangsters or warmongers because they were born evil. The problems in real human society arise out of society and the culture and values people are raised with, not from congenital demon parasites or ancient eldritch curses or the voice of Satan. The Solars are human. The Sidereals knew nothing about the Curse, so they have no rational reason to think the new Solars are any different from the rest of humanity in this regard.<br /> <br /> Even cursed, the Solars don't wake up one day with their entire personality, social background, and cultural value system replaced whole-cloth by a brain upload of their Past Life. For example: Swan did not wake up the day after his Exaltation with a brain upload of Desus replacing his personality and set out to turn Creation into a hellhole. He continues to be a diplomat from Coral or Wavecrest or wherever he came from, who grew up in the Second Age. He's a little more emotionally unstable, but he didn't suddenly forget the society he came from overnight, or suddenly transmogrify into the product of an extinct society he's never seen and probably doesn't remember. Why would he? Past Life memories don't work that way even with the Throwback Flaw, and as Celestial Exalted the Sidereals <i><b>know</b></i> it doesn't work that way. Even when Swan eventually does go batshit insane, he'll be a batshit insane diplomat from Coral or Wavecrest, not a brain upload of somebody who grew up in the First Age -- not that the Sidereals have actual evidence he'll go insane at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2015, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:53:52-07:00","id":523192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522328#post522328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for helping to clear up my misunderstandings, Mercushio. I appreciate it! Like I said I don't have many books so I get most setting info secondhand. So in summary, what you're saying is that the Sidereals who support the Second Age status quo don't actually believe it's good and it doesn't make them happy, they just believe that there are no other options so they should not try to change it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that at all. The Sidereals who support the Second Age status quo, for the most part, don't believe there are &quot;no other options.&quot; Of couse they're aware of other options, every time they see a member of the Gold Faction they are reminded that there are other options. They simply don't think any of those other options have an acceptable risk/reward ratio. And they definitely believe in making things better, but, again, in the context of not accidentally making shit worse as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of the reason I feel strongly, I think, is that the Realm is a representative of the most extremely oppressive groups in the real world, and the Bronze are a representative of the cynical, cold-hearted bastards who prop the empires up while they know how bad it is, and brainwash the rest of us to not even want anything better. The real world has real alternatives, and I have a hard time believing that Creation has none -- or that anyone with a scrap of human decency or compassion would not look for alternatives. </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Faction is deeply moved and motivated by human decency and compassion, but they're also highly utilitarian. They organized the Usurpation because they were motivated by human decency and compassion! People who were cynical, cold-hearted bastards would have decided that being the shadow advisors to triumphant god-kings who used the world as their plaything would be pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem, though, is that a lot of these guys are old and very removed from Creation, so they tend to be more utilitarian than compassionate at times. That's a genuine, real flaw in how they work. The Bronze Faction is prepared to accept a lot of bullshit on the part of the Realm because they look at thousands of slaves being worked to death, and they compare it to the crazy shit the Solars got up to in the First Age and say firmly &quot;this is the lesser evil by far.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't fully understand your post. What is the Bronze plan then, and how do the books depict it as having any chance to prevent apocalypse, let alone improve things? How can it when the DBs clearly couldn't defend Creation even when they were far more numerous? </div> </div> </div>... I don't know what you're talking about here. The Dragon-Blooded absolutely did defend Creation; it was the Dragon-Blooded, not the Sidereals, who threw back the Fair Folk.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I consider the Great Contagion and Balorian Crusade the definitive, unambiguous, no-going-back failure of the original Bronze plan. </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Faction disagrees with you, and with good cause. The Great Contagion and the Balorian Crusade have nothing at all to do with their plan, which was &quot;stop the Solars from wrecking everything, and then rebuild as best we can with them gone.&quot; They would readily admit they can't forsee <i>every</i> threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's obvious to me that the Empress barely pulled the bacon out of the fire, and there is no particular reason to think she or anyone else is likely to pull that off next time. </div> </div> </div>Why isn't there?<br /> <br /> The Empress had the Defense Grid and was willing and able to fire it up and kill some Fair Folk whenever it proved necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals have not proven themselves sufficient to defend Creation from outside threats. </div> </div> </div>Of course they have, owing to the fact that Creation is still there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's clear to me that they cannot, because the world is fraying further into the Wyld and Underworld and they are not keeping up. </div> </div> </div>It is not. You are wrong. The world has been pretty stable for the entirety of the Second Age, with the Wyld held at bay and the Underworld not particularly encroaching on anything more than it usually does. It is only in the last five years things have been going downhill, and those five years do not invalidate seven and a half centuries of stability.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of the major players except the Sidereals themselves are even paying attention to the threat of the Deathlords. </div> </div> </div>You are wrong. The Lunars are very much paying attention to the Deathlords. So is Lookshy and the Confederation of Rivers. So is every major nation in the West.<br /> <br /> <i>So is the Realm.</i><br /> <br /> The Realm just happens to be crippled by an enormous political crisis at the moment. That doesn't mean it isn't paying attention.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, why was the Immaculate religion/society designed to teach that the Dragon-Blooded have an unquestionable right to abuse mortals any way they please? </div> </div> </div>It does no such thing. It doesn't teach this, and it isn't designed to teach this.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Philosophy in fact calls on Dragon-Blooded to not abuse mortals. At all. In any way, shape, or form. It in fact calls on them, as the people in Creation closest to the perfection of the Elemental Dragons, to uplift, inspire, protect, and guide the mortals towards their own enlightenment. They're meant to alleviate poverty and disease and ensure that mortals live lives of peace and plenty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, the Dragon-Blooded are &quot;supposed&quot; to be &quot;gentle&quot; in their oppression, but they're also supposedly born with the moral right to do absolutely anything they want whatsoever </div> </div> </div>No, they don't have that moral right. The Immaculate Philosophy does not teach that it is okay to mistreat mortals! It does teach that mortals do not acquire karmic debt by doing awful things the Dragon-Blooded tell them to do, but that isn't the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> slavery is mandated by the Dragons, </div> </div> </div>I... what? No.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and nobody has any right to question them at all. </div> </div> </div>No <i>mortal</i> has the right to question them, that's true. <i>Other Dragon-Blooded </i>do, and in fact the Immaculate Philosophy <i>requires</i> them to question other Dragon-Blooded who are abusing mortals. There's a Dragon-Blooded signature character (Kasif) who spends his entire life basically doing that and only that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worse, DB society teaches them that it's more important to kill Lunars and backstab other Houses/Gentes than to do anything at all about the Deathlords, Fair Folk, etc. </div> </div> </div>One, most Dragon-Blooded didn't, and still don't, know much about the Deathlords. Pre-Thorns, if you said the word &quot;Deathlord&quot; to a Dragon-Blooded, they'd be like &quot;bzuh?&quot; And even post-Thorns, they don't know that the Deathlords plan is to destroy the world on behalf of the Neverborn. As near as anyone looking at them from the outside can tell, the Deathlords are just supercharged ghosts out to do some conquering, and so far the best they've managed are a few small city-states. They don't <i>seem</i> like an existential threat.<br /> <br /> Two, the Dragon-Blooded regard slaying Fair Folk as a <i>very important part of their job</i>. The Wyld Hunt spends a lot of time doing just that! That's where the &quot;Wyld&quot; part of it comes from! The Fair Folk almost destroyed the world, the Dragon-Blooded remember that well, they take Wyld incursions really, really friggin' seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not useful for keeping Creation safe. My understanding is that the Bronze Faction got to make the Immaculate religion say anything they wanted when they designed it, so why is this the best they can do? Do they consider Lunars and Solars an even bigger threat than the Deathlords, and why? At least if the Solars (or Yozis!) took over the world would still exist.* </div> </div> </div>Deathlords didn't exist when the Immaculate Philosophy was being created.<br /> <br /> Also, no, the Sidereals didn't have a completely free hand; the Immaculate Philosophy, if I recall right, was made in conjunction <i>with</i> the Dragon-Blooded. The Dragon-Blooded Host that took down the Solars wasn't just a tool that did whatever the Sidereals wanted, its leaders had their own needs and wants.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Philosophy is designed to deal with the post-Solar world as it was, and provide a means of stability and social control that would smooth off a lot of the rough edges off the Dragon-Blooded polity. The Sidereals could have tried designing a religion that said &quot;you should all be humble and generous and spend all day and every day serving the mortals, who are just as good as you are&quot; but that religion would have gotten zero traction amongst the Princes of the Earth, who were not made to be humble; they were made to fight and conquer.<br /> <br /> So, okay. You have to take into account both the nature of the Dragon-Blooded and the fact that they're going to be ruling the world now that the Solars and Lunars are gone. Well, fine. The religion will glorify the Dragon-Blooded as spiritually enlightened beings, feeding their ego. It will use this ego-stroking to attempt to inspire them towards goodness and rightouesness, by dangling the &quot;Enlightenment ensures eventual union with the Dragons&quot; carrot in front of them and also employing the &quot;if you don't measure up to these standards, in your next life you will be a mortal, or worse&quot; stick.<br /> <br /> Now, mortals. You don't want mortals rising up all the time. But you also don't want them to be abused all the time either, you staged a whole Usurpation to stop that from happening. So, okay. You build in a lot of stuff about how the Dragon-Blooded rule, and mortals serve, but you also make ruling mortals well part of a requirement for gaining enlightenment. You toss a spiritual palliative towards the mortals in the form of &quot;nothing a Dragon-Blooded can do to you will hurt you karmically, and you will be rewarded in the next life.&quot;<br /> <br /> The payoff for all this social engineering? Stability. The Sidereals value stability. They want there to not really be wars or uprising or revolts and suchly. The Immaculate Philosophy is great for that!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't really understand the assumption that the Solars inevitably <i><b>will</b></i> go insane again. We know OOC that it's true because of the Curse, but the Bronze just seem to assume it with no evidence, even though the social structure of the First Age that fed the egos of the Solars has been ground into less than dust. </div> </div> </div>The Bronxe Faction does not, repeat not, assume the Solars will inevitably go insane again. Many of the Elders were there when the Great Prophecy happened, and they saw the Vision of Gold, and that it had a very real chance of being enacted.<br /> <br /> They feel that the<i> risk </i>that they will is too great to be borne.<br /> <br /> There's a difference.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They built a worldwide society so single-mindedly obsessed with murdering those innocent people that most Dragon-Bloods are now unwilling to even consider the possibility that Deathlords or Fair Folk are a threat to Creation, even though everybody in Creation knows they almost destroyed the world. </div> </div> </div>You keep saying this, and I keep wondering where you get the idea that the Dragon-Blooded don't consider the Fair Folk to be a major threat to creation. Of course they do! They very much do!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:06:39-07:00","id":523322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that at all. The Sidereals who support the Second Age status quo, for the most part, don't believe there are &quot;no other options.&quot; Of couse they're aware of other options, every time they see a member of the Gold Faction they are reminded that there are other options. They simply don't think any of those other options have an acceptable risk/reward ratio. And they definitely believe in making things better, but, again, in the context of not accidentally making shit worse as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is that, if they think the Gold Faction are truly the only other option, then they're idiots. That's the fallacy of the excluded middle, and in this case the two Factions' plans are both very extreme. That the Sidereals have only ever come up with 2 ideas, for ~1500 years, just makes them out to be uncreative idiots. They need to adapt their plans to changes in circumstances and new information. They should consider and talk about and come up with ideas and actually try to make things better! They should realize that the Great Prophecy failed to take creatures Outside of Fate into account. Their strategy should have shifted more than it did in response to the Contagion and Balorian Crusade. They should recognize that the Lunars are necessary to protect the edge of Creation, and at least discuss and debate the idea of peace and alliance with them -- even if peace is sociopolitically unpleasant, it's better than apocalypse! They should look for non-Solar options to prevent another Great Contagion, instead of just repeating what already failed.<br /> <br /> What are Sidereals doing to stop the Dragon-Blooded from being just as bad as the Solars, or prevent apocalypse #3? You said the Bronze are depicted as &quot;working themselves to death&quot; but what are they actually doing, other than propping up Dynast privilege (and their own!) and killing Anathema? The corebooks don't give any clue here. Please elaborate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bronze Faction is prepared to accept a lot of bullshit on the part of the Realm because they look at thousands of slaves being worked to death, and they compare it to the crazy shit the Solars got up to in the First Age and say firmly &quot;this is the lesser evil by far.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you please explain how the Solars were worse than the Realm? I have never had that impression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate Philosophy in fact calls on Dragon-Blooded to not abuse mortals. At all. In any way, shape, or form. It in fact calls on them, as the people in Creation closest to the perfection of the Elemental Dragons, to uplift, inspire, protect, and guide the mortals towards their own enlightenment. They're meant to alleviate poverty and disease and ensure that mortals live lives of peace and plenty.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is the opposite of the way they treat mortals. They commit hideous atrocities every day. The Satrapies are being impoverished and abused horribly to make rich Dynasts richer and give them fun places to rape the natives, and free peasants even in the Realm are oppressed. Let alone the slaves and dispossessed. The Usurpation also involved genocide death camps so awful they punched a giant hole through Creation into the Underworld -- one of the biggest shadowlands on the map. The Immaculate religion is a huge, huge part of Realm society... yet utterly ineffective at stopping any of this. So either it's not well-designed, or those are insincere platitudes painted onto something that's actually designed to do something quite different, or the religion (which the Bronze supposedly still control) has changed drastically from its original non-oppressive form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... what? No.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then ... what does prop up the Realm social structure and slavery as legitimate?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No <i>mortal</i> has the right to question them, that's true. <i>Other Dragon-Blooded </i>do, and in fact the Immaculate Philosophy <i>requires</i> them to question other Dragon-Blooded who are abusing mortals. There's a Dragon-Blooded signature character (Kasif) who spends his entire life basically doing that and only that!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he having any luck? What percentage of Dragon-Bloods actually take his complaints seriously? Is he an abolitionist? It's my impression that he's one of a tiny minority. Certainly, that belief hasn't had much effect, considering how the Realm treats people. I think Lookshy also practices slavery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, no, the Sidereals didn't have a completely free hand; the Immaculate Philosophy, if I recall right, was made in conjunction <i>with</i> the Dragon-Blooded. The Dragon-Blooded Host that took down the Solars wasn't just a tool that did whatever the Sidereals wanted, its leaders had their own needs and wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. So: the slavery and atrocities and constant warfare weren't the Sidereals' idea, the DBs insisted on those parts. And the Sidereals tried to restrain them from behaving like that, but failed. That is less damning. But I still want to know what they're doing about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I don't know what you're talking about here. The Dragon-Blooded absolutely did defend Creation; it was the Dragon-Blooded, not the Sidereals, who threw back the Fair Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>90% of all life died, and then the vast majority of those survivors died, and huge chunks of Creation are just gone. A large fraction of the Dragon-Blooded died, too -- I don't know what proportion, but I thought it was most of them. I don't call that success at all. That's a miserable, pathetic failure, just a hair shy of the end of the world.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals had a responsibility to find out what caused the Great Contagion, and they knew what caused the Balorian Crusade. Those causes are still obviously present and could easily do the same thing again, and again, and again. If the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals, at best, can only save 1-3% each time, how long before nothing is left? To me that looks like a <i><b>much</b></i> worse risk than &quot;The Solars might become oppressive.&quot; In fact the only real difference I see between the Vision of Darkness and the specific way the Bronzes have carried out their vision, is that the Bronze version is draining down into the Void more slowly. But what's 2000 years, on a cosmic scale? Not really much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not. You are wrong. The world has been pretty stable for the entirety of the Second Age, with the Wyld held at bay and the Underworld not particularly encroaching on anything more than it usually does. It is only in the last five years things have been going downhill, and those five years do not invalidate seven and a half centuries of stability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Second Age is an era of continual decline. So, in 762 the shadowlands and Wyld zones hadn't actually gotten any bigger since the Balorian Crusade ended?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are wrong. The Lunars are very much paying attention to the Deathlords. So is Lookshy and the Confederation of Rivers. So is every major nation in the West.<br /> <br /> <i>So is the Realm.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>But what have they ever done about it, in 763 years? Mostly they've killed each other instead. (Although the Lunars also spend a ton of effort fighting off the Fair Folk.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One, most Dragon-Blooded didn't, and still don't, know much about the Deathlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, they aren't necessarily to blame for that ignorance -- they're so clueless they think Lunars did it. But the Sidereals had a responsibility to find out what really caused the Great Contagion, and teach the Dragon-Blooded to regard that cause as a threat. They took on that kind of responsibility when they usurped the throne of Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deathlords didn't exist when the Immaculate Philosophy was being created.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that, but what adjustments were made after the Contagion, to recognize the importance of this new threat?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523192#post523192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You keep saying this, and I keep wondering where you get the idea that the Dragon-Blooded don't consider the Fair Folk to be a major threat to creation. Of course they do! They very much do!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not aware that the Wyld Hunts canonically spend much effort against Fae, that is news to me. They appear to consider Lunars a bigger threat. The Lunars are the primary bulwark keeping the Fair Folk from having another Balorian Crusade, and without them the Dragon-Blooded couldn't hold it back on their own -- the Sword of Creation can stop them from entering the Blessed Isle, but not from dissolving the Threshold. But the Sidereals and Immaculates continue to try to wipe the Lunars out, even though they admit that even Anathema oppose the Fae. There isn't talk of trying to end the counterproductive warfare between Exalted so they can focus on protecting Creation. That's <b><i>stupid</i></b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> This thread is helping me to appreciate the Ratkin from Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:33:53-07:00","id":523366,"title":"","content":"Huh, a Usurpation argument. I... don't think of seen one of these in a while.<br /> <br /> I find they no longer really interest me.<br /> <br /> This though...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Lunars are the primary bulwark keeping the Fair Folk from having another Balorian Crusade, and without them the Dragon-Blooded couldn't hold it back on their own -- the Sword of Creation can stop them from entering the Blessed Isle, but not from wiping out the Threshold.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really good for the setting or the Lunars to hold them up as this great barrier holding back the endless hordes of the Fair Folk, or to undermine the significance of the Realm Defence Grid in the defence of Creation (even if it's implicit that the thing can't sustain the pace that people would expect of it). Hell, it's not even good for the Fair Folk to be portrayed as an endless horde that would be capable of washing over Creation with ease were it not for the Defence Grid and the Lunars (now, the Wyld is a different matter, but it's also held back by more abstract and complex things).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Sidereals and Immaculates continue to try to wipe the Lunars out, even though they admit that even Anathema oppose the Fae. There isn't talk of trying to end the counterproductive warfare between Exalted so they can focus on protecting Creation. That's <b><i>stupid</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically yes. The same way that it's stupid to continue spending precious and limited petrochemicals in fuelling war machines to maintain the pre-eminence of power projection of the United States, but it's the kind of stupidity that is rationally pursued in service to short-sighted goals for the advancement of self-interests, and even then that has less to do with &quot;they're killing the only people who can defend them&quot; and more with &quot;everybody is fighting each other so much that they don't notice that their house is burning down&quot;.<br /> <br /> At the heart of all of this is the dramatic necessity that characters aren't doing the &quot;sensible&quot; thing (which can be defined as the thing most beneficial to the long term survival of everybody), partially to serve better as an existential metaphor and partially to allow the option that player characters are instrumental in the necessary shift.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:45:43-07:00","id":523394,"title":"","content":"But if you build a setting in which <b><i>everybody</i></b> except the PCs are selfish, short-sighted, idiotic assholes, then the world is a very, very dark one and pretty much doomed no matter what the PCs do. Also, PCs raised in a world populated entirely by selfish, short-sighted, idiotic assholes wouldn't grow up to be any better. It's better to write the setting in which people are more complex and some of them actually are well-meaning. Especially when most of them are meant to be groups the PCs can belong to or work for/with.<br /> <br /> Even the U.S. has at least a couple hundred, maybe a few thousand, people who want to change the policy you mentioned. As stupid and selfish as most Americans are, we aren't an entirely monolithic bloc with only one policy. And that's with vastly less access to information and power than the Celestial Exalted have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523366#post523366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, a Usurpation argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the Usurpation I'm talking about, though. It's the Fail strategy afterwards, especially post-Contagion when it should be obvious to every Sidereal that it failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2015, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:36:39-07:00","id":523466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523322#post523322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what have they ever done about it, in 763 years? Mostly they've killed each other instead. (Although the Lunars also spend a ton of effort fighting off the Fair Folk.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Thorns was only 4 years before the default start of the game. Considering Thorns was kind of the inciting event that made it clear the Deathlords were a threat outside of the Underworld there's kind of a point to be made for the other 758 years.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523322#post523322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, they aren't necessarily to blame for that ignorance -- they're so clueless they think Lunars did it. But the Sidereals had a responsibility to find out what caused the Great Contagion, and teach the Dragon-Blooded to regard that cause as a threat. They took on that kind of responsibility when they usurped the throne of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div> They have. Unfortunatly the Dowager is kind of a super powerful psychotic recluse, and the agent sent in to find out may be compromised or may have purposefully developed the most awe inspiring case of DID the world has ever known.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523322#post523322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is the opposite of the way they treat mortals. They commit hideous atrocities every day. The Satrapies are being exploited and abused horribly to make rich Dynasts richer and give them fun places to rape the natives, and free peasants even in the Realm are oppressed. Let alone the slaves and dispossessed. The Usurpation also involved genocide death camps so awful they punched a giant hole through Creation into the Underworld -- one of the biggest shadowlands on the map. The Immaculate religion is a huge, huge part of Dragon-Blood society... yet utterly ineffective at stopping any of this. So either it's not working at all, or those are insincere platitudes painted onto something that's actually designed to do something quite different.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Immaculate religion didn't exist till after the Usurpation. This leaves your argument that X happened during the Usurpation, so what is the Immaculate religion doing about it, kind of hollow like the UN is useless because it did nothing during the Crusades or when the black plague was sweeping Europe.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523322#post523322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that, but what, if any, adjustments were made after the Contagion, to recognize the existence of this new threat? Did the Sidereals ever investigate to find out the what caused the plague? If they did, they didn't tell the Immaculates, who believe the Lunars did it (according to the 1E corebook).</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly what kind of adjustments does one make to deal with a plague where the infection vectors include, air, contact, contact with ley lines that touch an infection point somewhere, and looking at its destiny? Yeah the Sids have looked into it, unfortunately it is part of an amazingly large workload,so things haven't exactly been progressing smoothly on that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523322#post523322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not aware that the Wyld Hunts canonically spend much effort against Fae, that is news to me. They appear to consider Lunars a bigger threat.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh yeah the purpose of the Wyld hunt is to go after threats to Creation. It will hunt demons, gods, rhaksha, behemoth, lunars, solars, abyssals, hell its uncommon but even DBs can do crap to earn themselves the anathema title and get hunted. Lunars just tend to be a more active thing, so they get more hunts against them than the rhaksha who will occasionally just show up in Creation for business.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523322#post523322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunars are the primary bulwark keeping the Fair Folk from having another Balorian Crusade -</div> </div> </div> </div> Well that and the fact that many Rhaksha don't want anything to do with Creation, most of the others are perfectly content to just go into Creation and see sights and do stuff without trying to end it all, the lack of entities like Balor who have the ability to galvanize the rhaksha into another attempt, and that the rhaksha are neither limitless in number nor are all of them particularly keen on risking final death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523322#post523322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Sidereals and Immaculates continue to try to wipe the Lunars out, even though they admit that even Anathema oppose the Fae. There isn't talk of trying to end the counterproductive warfare between Exalted so they can focus on protecting Creation. That's <b><i>stupid</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div> The lunars also spend a fair amount of time slaying DBs, trying to kill Sids whenever the opportunity presents itself, and there are a few that go out and try to destroy the governments organizing the world. Those don't particularly help with the case of everyone just sitting down and trying to talk things out like rational beings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:55:25-07:00","id":523485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523466#post523466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thorns was only 4 years before the default start of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Contagion was 768 years ago. In all that time, did any Sidereals ever try to investigate what caused it, so the next one can be prevented? Did they ever determine the source of this threat and teach the Dragon-Blooded to oppose that source? Evidently not; the official Immaculate party line is that the Lunars caused the Contagion, even though the Sidereals can be absolutely certain that isn't true. Yet the Contagion was obviously a much bigger problem than Lunars had ever been even in the First Age. That's some drastically messed up priorities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523466#post523466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate religion didn't exist till after the Usurpation. This leaves your argument that X happened during the Usurpation, so what is the Immaculate religion doing about it, kind of hollow like the UN is useless because it did nothing during the Crusades or when the black plague was sweeping Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragon-Blooded have been doing those things continuously for 1500 years. What has any Sidereal ever done to stop that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523466#post523466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lunars also spend a fair amount of time slaying DBs, trying to kill Sids whenever the opportunity presents itself, and there are a few that go out and try to destroy the governments organizing the world. Those don't particularly help with the case of everyone just sitting down and trying to talk things out like rational beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunars are also depicted as ineffective idiots. But the ball is mostly in the Sidereal court for continuing to prop up and spread the lies that mandate the war. The Lunars really don't have any option to approach a negotiation table when the world doesn't consider them human people and will never accept surrender no matter what. Have even the Gold Faction bothered to tell the Lunars that not all Sidereals are helping the Immaculates? How would the Lunars ever guess that otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2015, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:06:06-07:00","id":523493,"title":"","content":"Man, and I though<b> <i>I</i> </b>looked for the absolute worst ways to look at an Exalted splat (in my case, Solars)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:20:17-07:00","id":523508,"title":"","content":"I feel a lot of this would be solved if the purpose of the Great Contagion was more ambiguous, and the Deathlords were portrayed as being more interested in wasting resources in pursuit of temporal power over the Underworld.<br /> <br /> As well as the idea that the Deathlords are powerful enough that there would be diminishing returns for trying to pre-emptively strike at them for something they probably can't or won't do again, or punish them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you build a setting in which <b><i>everybody</i></b> except the PCs are selfish, short-sighted, idiotic assholes, then the world is a very, very dark one and pretty much doomed no matter what the PCs do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-interest is not directly equivalent to selfishness. Basically decent and smart people can still do things that perpetuate problematic or destructive systems.<br /> <br /> The future of the setting is unwritten, so whether or not it's possible to save it is something to decide in the course of actual games, not try to mathematically derive from secret truths of the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:25:54-07:00","id":523512,"title":"","content":"Erinys,<br /> <br /> I can't help but notice that your argument is that<br /> <br /> 1) kung fu Fate ninja demigods should have rationalized and conducted their desperate military coup against their mad genius tyrannical god-king oppressors by your ethical standards,<br /> 2) failing to design and implement-by-proxy a world-wide utopian society based on modern ideals in the process of said desperate military coup is inexcusable,<br /> 3) failing to make peace with and integrate the severely aggrieved and angry remnants of the old regime, despite viewing this segment as part of the original problem and necessary to extinguish as part of the coup is stupid, because they could potentially be useful,<br /> 4) plans based on the understanding that something important will be damaged and lessened, but will survive, should be abandoned because &quot;new information&quot; as soon as that important thing is damaged and lessened, but survives,<br /> 4b) the Dragon-Blooded are insufficient to save Creation, as demonstrated by two examples of horrible tragedies that they saved Creation from,<br /> 5) one thousand years or so is plenty of time to unearth any and all plots, regardless of how subtle and thorough the misdirection is, and therefore<br /> 6) the fact that the Age of Sorrows is an Age of Sorrows is a direct result of Sidereal incompetence.<br /> <br /> I'm hardly the biggest fan of the Sidereals, particularly the Bronze, but wow, your take on them makes the whole setting seem so much less grand and epic.<br /> <br /> It doesn't take much adjustment to say &quot;The Sidereals are doing everything they can to preserve Creation the best way they know how, but they're doing so with the methods they have, according to the beliefs and understandings that they have, and from the standpoint <i>we</i> have - a snapshot of a time where everything has gone wrong at once - it appears to not be going well at all, but perhaps this is not entirely fair to them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:58:56-07:00","id":523533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523145#post523145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean creating the Immaculate Philosophy and Wyld Hunt. They assumed the crazy was inherent to Solar exaltations, and not a result of Solar society. We know OOC it is, but they had no reason to think so. The Prophecy only showed the Solar Deliberative, in its First Age form, ruining the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't create the Wyld hunt to hunt down and kill solars, they didn't predict that solars would break out of the Jade Prison*, the wyld hunt was formed to hunt fair folk and lunars**; that's why it has that name Wyld hunt.<br /> <br /> Now that this is out of the way.<br /> Yes i agree with you, they should have tried different things with the solars, things like executing the real crazy ones (either legally or illegally), locking up the worse offenders, forcing them to share power, limiting their number, try to cure them of their insanity etc. The thing is that some and/or all of the above were part of the Vision of Gold***. The Vision of Bronze on the other hand predicted a safe but diminished Creation but it has the requirement of the solars being out of the picture****.<br /> It should be clear now (after 3***** major unpredicted things happened) that the sidereals either can't predict so far ahead or that their predictions are as trustworthy as they thought or the sidereals aren't as good at making their visions happening****** as they thought they could.<br /> I agree with you that the sidereals should realize that the Vision of Bronze is gone now, <b>for good</b>, whether it was the right choice or no; now the solars are back, they are in the picture, they can't have their Vision of Bronze with the Solars out there in Creation doing their thing. Sidereals should get themselves a new plan.<br /> <br /> I agree with you that the sidereals did nothing about the Great Contagion (<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio\">Murcushio</a></b> correct me if i am wrong) and they lock themselves in Heaven sipping celestial wine and at best not watching the people of Creation dying. About the balorian crusade though; they did something, they created (or super-charged or whatever) the destiny of the then young dragon blooded officer which in the future will be known as the Scarlet Empress. Sure you might think that it wasn't enough (i don't think that this was enough, they should have done more) but at least they did <i>something</i>; lunars didn't do anything, at best some of them died heroically(?) and unknowingly gave Scarlet enough time to do her thing, i didn't see Ma-ha-su-chi or Leviathan or any other of the first age survivors making a bee line for the realm defense grid, all they did was fight and some of them died; apparently that's all lunars are good for, <b>dying</b> again and again.<br /> <br /> *the fact that they didn't keep an eye out or post a sentry or something in the Jade Prison is just another issue of sidereal hubris or incompetence (take your pick)<br /> **i still don't understand why they want the lunars out of the picture<br /> ***i think that each Vision actually gave multiple visions showing variations of the same thing based on the sidereals' actions.<br /> ****i still don't know why lunars, ALL lunars needed to be so much in the sidelines for this Vision, i still don't understand why the sidereals needed the lunars out of the picture as well.<br /> ***** 1) Great Contagion 2) Bolorian Crusade 3) The breaking of the Jade Prison and all that followed (abyssals, infernals etc.), now that i think about it; the things might be 4 if you count the disappearance of the empress<br /> ******by enforcing their visions i mean making sure they come true and the interference from beings outside of fate doesn't alter the destiny that they had crafted.<br /> <br /> Now about the Realm dragon blooded and the immaculate philosophy, sure they are wrong but things aren't that bad as you make them out to be, or rather they weren't as bad until now; most of the things you said are happening more and more frequently now that the empress is gone and the realm is in disarray, and the Realm is in disarray because the empress and her sidereal masters created a government that can't function without her. Now with her redness gone there are more dragon blooded that can do what they want, they have more power than they did before, they don't care so much how they are seen, the immaculate order can't do what they could etc.<br /> <br /> PS. I saw somewhere in this thread something about a massive sidereal errata, did that thing happened? (me and my group jumped ship and left exalted before 2.5 happened)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T12:42:45-07:00","id":523580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523533#post523533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't create the Wyld hunt to hunt down and kill solars, they didn't predict that solars would break out of the Jade Prison*, the wyld hunt was formed to hunt fair folk and lunars**; that's why it has that name Wyld hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're right. Mostly -- there were about a dozen Solars still reincarnating. I should have said they created the Jade Prison to prevent Solar reincarnation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523533#post523533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes i agree with you, they should have tried different things with the solars, things like executing the real crazy ones (either legally or illegally), locking up the worse offenders, forcing them to share power, limiting their number, try to cure them of their insanity etc. The thing is that some and/or all of the above were part of the Vision of Gold***. The Vision of Bronze on the other hand predicted a safe but diminished Creation but it has the requirement of the solars being out of the picture****.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Usurpation itself wasn't necessarily a bad idea! The Solar Deliberative was an oppressive tyranny. I think it would have been much better to attempt reform (or even better, curing the insanity) first and only try revolution if that failed, but I don't know the details (which is why I ask questions!). I don't know if they had tried reforms before the Great Prophecy, or if the Vision of Gold specified that if reforms failed they would fail spectacularly and immediately, with no chance to switch to the Bronze plan. The setting is unambiguous in saying that the Solar rule was bad and something had to be done, but mostly seems ambiguous about what the best way to change it was. It's also quite vague to me if the Shogunate was better or worse than the late First Age.<br /> <br /> What isn't ambiguous, to me, is that the Age of Sorrows is horrible. Somebody messed up bigtime. Either they're unable to do better, or not trying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523533#post523533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you that the sidereals should realize that the Vision of Bronze is gone now, <b>for good</b>, whether it was the right choice or no; now the solars are back, they are in the picture, they can't have their Vision of Bronze with the Solars out there in Creation doing their thing. Sidereals should get themselves a new plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just modify the plan. They should have done that in response to the Contagion. They set up the Realm, but it isn't really much different from the Shogunate? Except smaller and with fewer supersoldiers, thus even less effective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523533#post523533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you that the sidereals did nothing about the Great Contagion (<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio\">Murcushio</a></b> correct me if i am wrong) and they lock themselves in Heaven sipping celestial wine and at best not watching the people of Creation dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that -- I don't know what Sidereals did during it. The Celestial gods locked the gates of Heaven and the Incarnae looked away, I think -- I read that secondhand. The thing the Sidereals didn't do <b><i>afterwards</i></b> was make sure it won't ever happen again. It's the whole &quot;Out of Fate, out of mind&quot; problem in their portrayal.<br /> <br /> The Contagion and Balorian Crusade are these huge, pivotal moments that define the Age of Sorrows, and they have to be apocalyptic, but I think maybe they shouldn't have been depicted as wiping out (collectively) 99% of life. That high level of mortality isn't necessary for the Shogunate civilization to collapse, lots of folks to die, and Creation's fabric to be damaged. When the books say the world came so close to oblivion twice, and then protray the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded as thinking that's success, it twists the rest of their narrative into...well, crazyland. They just look insane. Most of my problem with their portrayal would evaporate if the Contagion and Balorian Crusade weren't &quot;99% of Creation died, it could happen again <b><i>any day now</i></b>, and nobody's prepared!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-21-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:07:13-07:00","id":523622,"title":"","content":"I think that the biggest issue is that we don't know enough about the Shogunate (we don't even know how long it lasted), maybe this was the lessened version of Creation that sidereals saw in the Vision of Bronze; but because we don't know things about that time period we don't know how good or bad it was and what was happening during that time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523485#post523485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have even the Gold Faction bothered to tell the Lunars that not all Sidereals are helping the Immaculates? How would the Lunars ever guess that otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure that the Gold faction doesn't talk with lunar elders (part of the whole hubristic/incompetent sidereals <b>and</b> useless lunars), now the cult of the illuminated tries to recruit young lunars but i am not sure what it tells them and how it presents them to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:23:48-07:00","id":523660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523512#post523512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4b) the Dragon-Blooded are insufficient to save Creation, as demonstrated by two examples of horrible tragedies that they saved Creation from</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree with you, but on this point I think you're being unfair. The Empress suddenly showing up and stopping the Crusade does not seem like a reliably repeatable strategy. They lucked out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:31:34-07:00","id":523667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523485#post523485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have even the Gold Faction bothered to tell the Lunars that not all Sidereals are helping the Immaculates? How would the Lunars ever guess that otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a note in MoEP: Sidereals that mentions that Nazri (Chair of the Convention of Fire), and Tammuz (A Lunar Elder) both operate out of the same city. It posits the possibility that the two of them are actually on good terms with each other as a potential plot point for the ST to decide. So it is possible that at least some Lunars are aware that not all Siddies are hostile towards them. Then, of course, there is the (controversial) Silver Faction...who actively think the Lunars would do a better job of being in charge...and the book openly says they trade favors with a few Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:54:19-07:00","id":523689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523660#post523660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I generally agree with you, but on this point I think you're being unfair. The Empress suddenly showing up and stopping the Crusade does not seem like a reliably repeatable strategy. They lucked out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. The Empress showing up unexpectedly when needed has not proven repeatable, because after she showed up, she was, y'know, present. If she's present and a known factor, she doesn't need to show up unexpectedly. After that, the Dragon-Blooded Host continued to prove that it was good enough to preserve Creation against its enemies for the next nearly-800 years, apparently vindicating the Vision of Bronze.<br /> <br /> We, as players, know that the Vision of Bronze overlooked some very important factors operating in the background, but from an in-setting Sidereal perspective, things likely appeared to be moving along as well as could be expected... before the Empress vanished, turmoil erupted in the Realm, the Solars returned, the Deathlords kicked things into high gear, revealing themselves as a major threat and debuted <i>dark Solar servants of all freaking things,</i> the Lunars look ready to pounce at the sudden vulnerability, the Yozis appear to be stirring for some reason we're still just guessing at, and basically the entire creaky old clock that used to keep plugging away with enough TLC just erupted and now it's raining gears and sprockets and springs and lots of little weird metal bits I can't even speculate about but <i>will</i> be held responsible for reassembling, I'd quit my job and drink away my savings if that didn't mean the world would probably die and someone has to do it and I'm the only one who can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:25:01-07:00","id":523706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523689#post523689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no. The Empress showing up unexpectedly when needed has not proven repeatable, because after she showed up, she was, y'know, present. If she's present and a known factor, she doesn't need to show up unexpectedly. After that, the Dragon-Blooded Host continued to prove that it was good enough to preserve Creation against its enemies for the next nearly-800 years, apparently vindicating the Vision of Bronze.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the point.<br /> <br /> If I described the history of Creation up through the Balorian Crusade (ending right before the Scarlet Empress comes into the picture), and you didn't know the world followed narrative conventions, would you expect Creation to have been saved?<br /> <br /> If I randomly generated a million universes that match Creation's history in the broad strokes through the Balorian Crusade, differing only in details not described, what fraction of them do you think would be saved?<br /> <br /> A pretty small fraction, IMO.<br /> <br /> What this means is that the Bronze plan <i>did</i> leave Creation incredibly vulnerable to a certain class of threat. A class of threat the Solar Deliberative probably would have dealt with easily (in fact, it's implied they did handle this sort of stuff without too much difficulty all throughout the High First Age). And that's legitimately on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:32:16-07:00","id":523714,"title":"","content":"Of course, it is entirely possible that the Solars could have been so far gone by the time of the Great Contagion/Balorian Crusade that they would have let the world burn.<br /> <br /> And we are looking at the decision to go with the Vision of Bronze in hindsight. I'm sure the Sidereals - when dealing with a group of limit breaking Solars going on and on about how letting Wyld Monster roam creation was good times - might have thought they were making a best choice. <br /> <br /> Not to mention that the Sidereals were limit breaking themselves when they made that fateful decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-21-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:39:18-07:00","id":523718,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I don't agree with Erinys 100% (in part that would involve reading through a lot of mega ginormo long posts!).<br /> <br /> But I do think that it is fair to say that much of what the Sidereals and Lunars are supposed to know about one another and about the world and to have been able to do to affect the world are products of a time in Exalted's publishing history when it seems that they were envisioned much more as passive NPCs, who were a lot more isolated figures, and much less as dynamic, active characters who were part of large organisations. <br /> <br /> Which early in 1e how they seem more to be presented - Sidereals were more these Gandalf and Traveller in Black esque lone wanderer figures using prophecy and acting as the hands of history based on their own judgement while Lunars were these fractious, excitingly and sexily mad, individualistic warlords. You kind of wouldn't expect knowledge about the Deathlords to necessarily be researched or that widely disseminated among these fractious groups, or for major projects to change the world to be that workable, with characters like that.<br /> <br /> So a lot of this basic plot had to be updated to a time when instead the Sidereals and Lunars are more organised into the Bureau of Fate and Silver Pact and were taking more of an active role in the world.<br /> <br /> And that's why you then get more fallback onto the ideas that they're at war with one another, or that they're overworked government employees. Which as ideas go are maybe not actually that sympathetic, or convincing.<br /> <br /> Plus 2e didn't really work too hard to make the Sidereals sympathetic.<br /> <br /> So maybe it's better instead by now to update what they should know and be able to have done to some extent? I'll have to see how 3e sells it.<br /> <br /> At least that's my view without having read the books a lot recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:46:50-07:00","id":523722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523706#post523706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not the point.<br /> <br /> If I described the history of Creation up through the Balorian Crusade (ending right before the Scarlet Empress comes into the picture), and you didn't know the world followed narrative conventions, would you expect Creation to have been saved?<br /> <br /> If I randomly generated a million universes that match Creation's history in the broad strokes through the Balorian Crusade, differing only in details not described, what fraction of them do you think would be saved?<br /> <br /> A pretty small fraction, IMO.<br /> <br /> What this means is that the Bronze plan <i>did</i> leave Creation incredibly vulnerable to a certain class of threat. A class of threat the Solar Deliberative probably would have dealt with easily (in fact, it's implied they did handle this sort of stuff without too much difficulty all throughout the High First Age). And that's legitimately on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except <i>this</i> is definitely not the point.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals trusted in the Vision of Bronze, which said that Creation would be damaged and lessened, but would survive, under the rule of the Dragon-Blooded, with the discrete assistance of the Sidereals. Now, there was definitely time during the Balorian Crusade/Great Contagion that it looked like that might not be true... and yet, here comes the woman who would become the Empress, claiming the throne, saving Creation and stabilizing Dragon-Blooded control under one central ruler, and suddenly the Sidereals are looking pretty smart. Creation was damaged, lessened... but <i>it survived.</i> Just like the Sidereals had foreseen.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, instances where you're proven right against all odds don't make very good arguments for why you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:50:42-07:00","id":523723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523722#post523722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except <i>this</i> is definitely not the point.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals trusted in the Vision of Bronze, which said that Creation would be damaged and lessened, but would survive, under the rule of the Dragon-Blooded, with the discrete assistance of the Sidereals. Now, there was definitely time during the Balorian Crusade/Great Contagion that it looked like that might not be true... and yet, here comes the woman who would become the Empress, claiming the throne, saving Creation and stabilizing Dragon-Blooded control under one central ruler, and suddenly the Sidereals are looking pretty smart. Creation was damaged, lessened... but <i>it survived.</i> Just like the Sidereals had foreseen.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, instances where you're proven right against all odds don't make very good arguments for why you're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I've misunderstood a part of the lore, the Vision of Bronze couldn't be describing the Realm because the massive Wyld invasion (and possibly the Contagion as well) were outside fate and therefore invisible to their prophecies. The diminished Creation was the Shogunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:04:11-07:00","id":523729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523714#post523714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, it is entirely possible that the Solars could have been so far gone by the time of the Great Contagion/Balorian Crusade that they would have let the world burn.<br /> <br /> And we are looking at the decision to go with the Vision of Bronze in hindsight. I'm sure the Sidereals - when dealing with a group of limit breaking Solars going on and on about how letting Wyld Monster roam creation was good times - might have thought they were making a best choice.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the Sidereals were limit breaking themselves when they made that fateful decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get you, that's why i said that it's a matter of opinion whether the sidereals were cowards or heroes for choosing the Vision of Bronze.<br /> <br /> What we are saying is WHY didn't they adjust their plans when HUGE things are happening, things like the Great Contagion (during which the sidereals did absolutely nothing), the balorian crusade (where the only thing that we know the sids did was to create an uber destiny for one gal) and most important of all the BREAKING of the Jade Prison.<br /> <br /> Seriously now; you have this great plan for a Creation that would be lessened but still there and that great plan of yours needed the solar exalted so out of the picture that you had to murder them and go to extreme measures to make sure that they don't come back and then they <b>do</b> come back. Don't you think that you should re-think and re-evaluate your plan <b>now</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:04:55-07:00","id":523730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523723#post523723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I've misunderstood a part of the lore, the Vision of Bronze couldn't be describing the Realm because the massive Wyld invasion (and possibly the Contagion as well) were outside fate and therefore invisible to their prophecies. The diminished Creation was the Shogunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the Visions were substantially less specific than you suggest.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I cite Sidereal support of the Realm and continued (renewed?) relevance of the Gold and Bronze factions as evidence. They didn't say &quot;welp, we're screwed, back to the drawing board!&quot; They continued on as if nothing had changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","user":"Ren9077","date":". 05-21-2015, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:46:41-07:00","id":523766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>leo1925</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523729#post523729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get you, that's why i said that it's a matter of opinion whether the sidereals were cowards or heroes for choosing the Vision of Bronze.<br /> <br /> What we are saying is WHY didn't they adjust their plans when HUGE things are happening, things like the Great Contagion (during which the sidereals did absolutely nothing), the balorian crusade (where the only thing that we know the sids did was to create an uber destiny for one gal) and most important of all the BREAKING of the Jade Prison.<br /> <br /> Seriously now; you have this great plan for a Creation that would be lessened but still there and that great plan of yours needed the solar exalted so out of the picture that you had to murder them and go to extreme measures to make sure that they don't come back and then they <b>do</b> come back. Don't you think that you should re-think and re-evaluate your plan <b>now</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure some Sidereals did, thus the re-emergence of the gold faction after the formation of the realm. <br /> <br /> I like to compare Sidereal politics to oWOD Garou politics. You are responsible for saving the world. Everything is on the line if you screw up. However people are going to have different opinions on how to go about this. With stakes that high, you are going to make damned sure that your idiot bronze coworker isn't going to screw things up.<br /> <br /> Of course, I always wondered why the Sidereals didn't get together and create another prophecy. I guess they didn't have enough living Sidereals to draw another prophecy at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T16:21:41-07:00","id":523778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523766#post523766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, I always wondered why the Sidereals didn't get together and create another prophecy. I guess they didn't have enough living Sidereals to draw another prophecy at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>What time? After the destruction of the Jade Prison? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T16:34:19-07:00","id":523782,"title":"","content":"During the great contagion<br /> <br /> (Sorry, my previous post was on my phone.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-21-2015, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T21:38:21-07:00","id":523976,"title":"","content":"I guess that by then the Bronze Faction was so entrenched that no-one dared to argue there was something wrong with the original prophecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T00:26:00-07:00","id":524140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523723#post523723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I've misunderstood a part of the lore, the Vision of Bronze couldn't be describing the Realm because the massive Wyld invasion (and possibly the Contagion as well) were outside fate and therefore invisible to their prophecies. The diminished Creation was the Shogunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Vision simply showed that, if the Sidereal Exalted murdered the Solars and locked their Essences away, Creation would survive albeit diminished. It never said that there wouldn't be disasters or that Creation would never be in danger or come close to destruction - only that it would be diminished but survive. And so far, through the Usurpation, through the Great Contagion, through the Balorian Crusade that's been true.<br /> <br /> Things have changed though now during the Time of Tumult - the Solar Exaltations have been freed, so the Bronze Vision (which required that the Solar Exaltations be locked away) no longer applies.<br /> <br /> While the Sidereal could come together for a new Prophecy, that's not terribly likely. Something like that would require all (or at least almost all) of the Sidereal working together to pull off, and there's far too much animosity between the factions for that to happen. Just getting the Sidereal together to perform a new Prophecy, nevermind getting them to agree to work together towards a single outcome would be an epic endeavor, and any Sidereal or group of Sidereal who succeeded in doing so would find themselves in a position similar to Chejop at the end of the High First Age - at the helm of the Five Score Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> This is the sort of task and position that PC's might find themselves in, and probably the primary reason why the Sidereal aren't canonically getting together to perform a new prophecy; because this is something cool that would be awesome for the PC's to do, rather than something for NPC's to undertake while the PC's sit back and watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:25:22-07:00","id":524171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522908#post522908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said they were destroyed? If we look at (real world) history, they were probably carted off to adorn city plazas and the mansions of rich aristocrats. They're tall, cool looking, and they &quot;bring good luck&quot; - they'd be a must-have accessory for any up-and-comer</div> </div> </div> </div>Same question. What nutjob thought that conspicuous wealth and privilege was more important than Creation not being devoured by the Wyld? And it was either one nutjob who stole all the monoliths, or a conspiracy of hundreds of nutjobs all doing it, and...</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says the looters even knew what the Monoliths were really for? One noble thought the artwork looked cool, so had several shipped home (<i>a la</i> the Elgin Marbles). One local cult, horrified to have an Anathema artifact in their presence, smashed theirs (like ISIS is doing in Syria). A nearby town, in need of fresh stone for a construction project, carved theirs up (think &quot;Italy&quot;). A wannabe sorcerer, convinced the Monoliths contained mystical secrets, carted one off to his workshop . . .<br /> <br /> In the real world, we're actually looking at ancient monoliths (and other ruins) for guidelines on how to mark nuclear waste. You need something that will stand for 10,000 years - without constant maintenance (since you can't guarantee your civilization will be around that long). And one thing we've learned is that - if people can steal or destroy an artifact - they usually will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> . . .But the Sidereals are on top, and successfully reprogrammed most of human society 180 degrees from what it used to be. They're social engineers on par with the Solars. They can clearly do amazing things! If they want to. . . </div> </div> </div>That's part of the problem - the Sidereals <i>aren't</i> on par with the Solars. And they were never meant to be. The Solars were the ones Exalted to lead, to rule. Its why their aura banners are so drastic - they're <i>supposed </i>to be noticed, to be followed. Solars were generals and knight-errants, healers and scholars, diplomats and spies. And they had the charms to back it up.<br /> <br /> Sidereals, on the other hand, were diviners and fortune tellers, advisors and assassins. In their own way, they are just as powerful as the Solars (possibly more so), but they were &quot;built&quot; to hold a supporting role. When the gods created the Exaltations, the assumption was that the Solars would always be around, and (as the Exalts of the king of the gods), always in charge. So there was no point in giving anyone else strong leadership or diplomatic powers.<br /> <br /> So that's a big part of the reason the Sidereals have run into so much difficulty. The Dawn Caste was built to crush problems like the Balorian Crusade. It would have been the Twilight Caste's job to cure the Great Contagion. The Night Caste is supposed to be spying on the Yozi and Malfeans. And the Eclipse Caste could broker a deal between the Gold Faction and the Lunars.<br /> <br /> With the Solars dead, locked away, or in hiding, there's a huge &quot;skill gap&quot; in the Celestial Exalted community. Things are not getting done - and haven't been for centuries. Some of which the Sidereal and Lunar know nothing about. And even if they did, they don't have the power to cover for the missing Solars.<br /> <br /> Yet, can they trust the returning ones?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a starting point of the already-corrupt First Age Solar Deliberative with nobody bothering to reform it. . . .<br /> <br /> This isn't something I know about, probably I don't have that book. Can you please summarize what it said about Solar rule? I know the First Age Solars are vaguely supposed to have been worse than the Scarlet Empire, but I don't know of anything concrete that was actually worse. They massacred mortals with exotic weapons and Wyld explosions instead of boring ol' steel and fire, but dead is dead. How is the Scarlet Empire an improvement? They look just as tyrannical to me, but in addition they also can't or won't do jack about the Deathlords and Fae. . . </div> </div> </div>What tends to get overlooked is that the Solars weren't merely &quot;crazy' - they were one keg or bad breakup from destroying all of Creation. And their Deliberative wasn't corrupt in the usual sense (as in taking bribes) - any sense of &quot;separation of powers&quot; or &quot;checks and balances&quot; had been completely destroyed. So there was no &quot;legal&quot; means to stop them.<br /> <br /> The Solar castes were meant to complement each other, to form a unified whole, with some support from the other Celestial Exalted. And in the early days, that was true. But once they were in power, with all the wealth and resources of Creation behind them . . . Instead, they scorched the earth, as if five suns had suddenly appeared in the sky.<br /> <br /> As the centuries wore on, the vanity and indifference of the Unconquered Sun mixed with the Great Curse, egging the Solars to ever greater extremes. Dawn Castes were raising armies to settle barroom disputes. Twilights competed to see who could build the most destructive doomsday device. Eclipse members conned demon princes into serving as their footstools for all eternity. In short, at every turn, the Solars were courting massive, Creation-wide destruction.<br /> <br /> And no one cared! Sure, the other Exalted realized there was a problem, but then the Zenith Caste would turn on their leadership and public speaking charms . . .and all those issues would just &quot;go away&quot;. A couple days later, the other Exalts would shake it off, and remember that they'd disagreed . . . but by then, it'd be too late.<br /> <br /> That's why the Bronze Faction won out. If the Gold Faction approached the Solars, and couldn't find enough who agreed with them, the Sidereal would never get another chance to fix the problem. The corrupted Solars would be forewarned, and the Sidereal would be (effectively) brainwashed by the Solars again, with Night Caste spies following them <i>ad infinitum</i> . . .<br /> <br /> But if the Bronze Faction could pull off a quick enough coup, kill enough Solars fast enough . . . Well, remember the truism - the best enemy wizard is a dead one. They can't caste a spell on you, if they're dead and buried.<br /> <br /> I assume that's also their reasoning, too, for why the Bronze Faction doesn't embrace the newly returned Solars. When they find out the truth about the Usurpation (and the Solars definitely have the skills to do so), will they forgive the Sidereal? And what if these new Solars end up as destructively insane as the old ones? You can't pull the same trick twice! Better to kill &amp; re-imprison them, and try to find some other way to deal with the Fae and Deathlords.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: And if the Bronze Faction discovers that the Abyssal and Infernal Exalted are simply &quot;modified&quot; Solars, that will only confirm their bias. The Solars are the root of all their problems, and the only good one is a dead one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit Two:</u></i> Oh, and the Scarlet Empire is &quot;better&quot; in the sense that its leaders <i>aren't</i> doing the mystical equivalent of an egg toss . . . with armed nuclear warheads. They're just oppressive and taking bribes. Creation can survive that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 05-22-2015, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T02:35:46-07:00","id":524193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523976#post523976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that by then the Bronze Faction was so entrenched that no-one dared to argue there was something wrong with the original prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. The original issue of the Bronze and Gold factions were probably more academic for most of the time between Usurpation and the return.I mean there were less than 20 Solars running around, so the upper limit of damage and benefits they could cause was much more limited even ignoring the fact that the Lunars and Dragonbloods were not really going to help them anymore.This is just my hypothesis, but I imagine for that time period the factions probably looked at Solars in a case by case on whether or not a Solar's ability could be useful for solving an issue vs how much damage could it inflict if decides to cut loose and try to break everything it can, is this one likely to become an extreme danger in the near future, and how hard will it be to remove if it gets entrenched. This of course goes out the window once the Solar numbers exceed the Sidereal numbers because you several variables alter rather highly like odds of Solars meeting up and joining forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T03:30:37-07:00","id":524223,"title":"","content":"@One Vorlon<br /> I think that you are overstating things about the first age solars, first of all it was most likely <i>some</i> or even <i>most</i> of the solars who were batshit crazy and not all, secondly if things were <i>that</i> bad then Creation would have been destroyed.<br /> <br /> Anyway the issue here is the sidereals now, even with the return of the solars; we don't see the sidereals trying to rebuilt the Jade Prison, nor do we see them trying to get solars in one place to get them killed in mass, or do anything <i>differently</i> about the solars than they were doing with the handful of solars that were free from the time after the Usurpation. At least the Gold faction <i>tries</i> to enact their original plan, albeit a little differently than they would in the first age because the circumstances are different.<br /> <br /> On the solars seeking revenge on the sids, that reminds of a game i played a long time ago:<br /> It was a game set a decade after the disappearance of the empress and deep in the east (away from Realm's power) a city was built by a circle of solars and it was advertised in the scavenger lands* and in the east as a haven for celestial exalted, so celestial exalted starting flocking there; by the time we, the PCs (2 solars, 1 lunar and 1 sidereal), went there there were ~20 solars, ~15 lunars and even 4 abyssals** (and a couple of sidereal allies but those almost never appeared in the deliberative).<br /> The issue is that 5 solars who built the city had a secret plan*** for the sidereals, after the realm was toppled and the creation was theirs again they planned to pass judgement on the sidereal host, even without Heaven's sanction, for their crimes against the solars and lunars and against creation; and there was even talk of trying to built a Jade Prison for the sidereals if such a thing was possible.<br /> <br /> So yes i agree that if the solars (somehow) learn what the sidereals did, they would be super pissed and will be out for blood.<br /> <br /> *that's where the circle has began<br /> **it's very weird how those got there but i will put it in a spoiler tag to avoid a wall of text<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">when the 4 abyssals (1 dusk, 1 midnight and 2 daybreaks) from the north, who thought that they had killed their deathlord, came to the city and asked to be included as celestial exalted; the deliberative had to vote whether to allow them in or no; most of them wanted to help one of the daybreak who was saying that he wanted their help to turn into a solar (the fact that he was able to use a couple of solar charms convinced most of the celestial exalted for his sincerity), some of them wanted to learn about their necromantic power, some of them wanted another uber warrior (the dust caste), and most of them wanted the information the abyssals could provide for the deathlords and the underworld. So they ended up voting them in almost unanimously </div></div> </div> </div><br /> ***ok, maybe it wasn't all 5 of them who had the plan, but at least the 3 of them did","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:06:27-07:00","id":524511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524140#post524140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bronze Vision simply showed that, if the Sidereal Exalted murdered the Solars and locked their Essences away, Creation would survive albeit diminished. It never said that there wouldn't be disasters or that Creation would never be in danger or come close to destruction - only that it would be diminished but survive. And so far, through the Usurpation, through the Great Contagion, through the Balorian Crusade that's been true.</div> </div> </div> </div>99% of all life died. The Shogunate failed. Nobody in their right mind who cared about the survival of Creation could have called it success. If the Bronze did, and made no change in their strategy, it's inexcusable. Nobody here has mentioned anything they did to find out why it happened, or to prevent the next apocalypse from wiping out 100% of life. If they've done nothing, that's the most damning of all. Preventing the next Great Contagion should be more important than everything else they've done for 768 years, certainly more important than proving a political point that they're infallible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524171#post524171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Solars dead, locked away, or in hiding, there's a huge &quot;skill gap&quot; in the Celestial Exalted community. Things are not getting done - and haven't been for centuries. Some of which the Sidereal and Lunar know nothing about. And even if they did, they don't have the power to cover for the missing Solars.<br /> <br /> Yet, can they trust the returning ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>But why are &quot;bring back the Solars&quot; and &quot;pretend the Great Contagion didn't happen&quot; the <i><b>only</b></i> two options? If the &quot;Silver Faction&quot; is canon that's only three ideas. Why haven't 100 supra-geniuses had any other ideas in 1500 years?<br /> <br /> They should not be portrayed as idiots -- as thinking the Great Contagion was no big deal and preventing the next one is unimportant -- as taking no effort anymore to prevent the Dragon-Blooded from becoming just as terrible as the First Age Solars. <i>If any books have portrayed them doing differently, somebody please say what.</i> Otherwise I think it's rather bad writing and that 3E should depict them better -- not succeeding since the Age of Sorrows still sucks, but <i><b>trying</b></i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524171#post524171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says the looters even knew what the Monoliths were really for?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the First Age Exalted would have known. Did no Sidereal or Lunar or elder Dragon-Blood ever do anything to save them? On the whole rim of Creation, is there even one single Monolith left? That's a heck of a lot of neglect from the &quot;protectors of Creation.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-22-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:44:33-07:00","id":524548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524511#post524511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Bronze did, and made no change in their strategy, is inexcusable. Nobody here has mentioned anything they did to even find out why it happened, or to prevent the next apocalypse from wiping out 100% of life. If they have done nothing, that's the most damning of all. Preventing the next Great Contagion should be more important than everything else they've done for 768 years, certainly more important than proving a political point that they're infallible.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Sarcastic assertion that the Sidereals used up their non-Solar &quot;Affect History Once and Only Once&quot; coupon with the Usurpation*<br /> *Thinly veiled accusation that the gameline only cares about history Solars are directly involved in*<br /> *Assorted cursing*<br /> *Strange metaphor about a starling that seems completely irrelevant to rest of post*<br /> *More cursing; at least three instances of &quot;fuck&quot; in one sentence*<br /> *Sarcasm lampshading Isator's inevitable reply*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T09:49:17-07:00","id":524551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524548#post524548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Sarcastic assertion that the Sidereals used up their non-Solar &quot;Affect History Once and Only Once&quot; coupon with the Usurpation*<br /> *Thinly veiled accusation that the gameline only cares about history Solars are directly involved in*</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I mean yeah, more or less. I think that's possibly why it was written this way. But if the Lunars can be rewritten to have a significant impact on history in 3E, the Sidereals should be rewritten to not be ... crappy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T10:39:19-07:00","id":524569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524551#post524551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I mean yeah, more or less. I think that's possibly why it was written this way. But if the Lunars can be rewritten to have a significant impact on history in 3E, the Sidereals should be rewritten to not be ... crappy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't view sidereals as crappy, i view them as delusional pricks who want to be the man on top but don't actually have the abilities to be the man on top and they aren't realizing that they don't have what it takes to rule the world.<br /> <br /> Ok that's the whole view i have about the sidereals but it's a pretty major part, i prefer to view them full of hubris than full of incompetence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T10:46:54-07:00","id":524572,"title":"","content":"They can be narrow-minded, hubristic, stubborn, biased, fallible jerks who pay too little attention to the wellbeing of mortals or their own madness ... but still smart, canny, competent, and able to think up new ideas when new problems arise. Their plans should be plausibly worthwhile even from an OOC perspective. They can be unequal to their self-appointed thrones without obvious incompetence/apathy. Their flaw doesn't need to be &quot;Out of Fate, out of mind.&quot; It can be subtler.<br /> <br /> They should be at least as competent as well-educated, highly-intelligent mortals.<br /> <br /> As for delusional -- all Cursed Exalted are presumably delusional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-22-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T12:43:59-07:00","id":524651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524171#post524171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Eclipse Caste could broker a deal between the Gold Faction and the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like quite a sad idea, that the Gold Faction and Lunars literally couldn't ever work together without an Eclipse to put them together. They couldn't use their own genius and humanity to find a solution.<br /> <br /> Which is generally sort of illustration of general a theme with the wider post I quoted this from. You can argue that the Sidereals may have had difficulty dealing with the commanding heights like the Great Contagion, and they really don't have enough to surmount them, no matter how they approach the problem (now, I think that's a little bit more of a predictable and thus boring Creation than I have interest in, but hey).<br /> <br /> It seems a lot harder to argue that they couldn't in theory have done a lot better than they did, from what we know about how capable they're meant to be. And that they wouldn't really be expected to. Even if you're willing to disregard this and put a lot of leeway in interpretation to maintain the default setting.<br /> <br /> Whether they were built to take a &quot;supporting role&quot; or not, that doesn't prevent them trying to know and getting somewhere with the powers and capabilities we know they have, and making progress over time, rather than being trapped in stasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:18:42-07:00","id":524737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=522613#post522613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my mind, there really wasn't a Gold faction before the Contagion. Just Ayesha Ura and some drunken elders. After the contagion, some of Sidereals jumped ship to the Gold Faction. The main goal of the Gold Faction was the find and open the Jade Prison*. Secondary goals include gaining the support of gods for when the Jade Prison is open, studying Solars to learn how to best guide them, and research a cure for their madness. Saving the few solar would a moral victory, but not very useful in the long run.<br /> <br /> *This only works if you go with the option of the Gold Faction using the Deathlords as a Cat's paw in opening the Jade Prison. Boy was the Gold Faction surprised when they only got 150 shards instead of the 300 they were expecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Open the Jade Prison: Good Idea<br /> <br /> Help the Deathlords Open the Jade Prison: Bad Idea<br /> <br /> So since I can't PM you WonderandAwe...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -