v> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The opening of the Jade Prison is centuries after the events of Hero.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T15:37:07-07:00","id":524831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524651#post524651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems like quite a sad idea, that the Gold Faction and Lunars literally couldn't ever work together without an Eclipse to put them together. They couldn't use their own genius and humanity to find a solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that they're incapable of it more that the situation has been allowed to fester and decay. I mean the Lunars who survived the Usurpation would have taught the next gen that Sids are lying manipulative backstabbers with an emphasis that its probably best to just kill the Sid if you aren't positive you need it. Which probably means any Sids who did try and explain what happened did not go as well as they had hoped. Cycle of violence and so on and so forth. Probably the reason you would need an Eclipse in the mix is to enable it to happen. A somewhat neutral 3rd party that can rein in the conflict if it talks start to go bad, and it probably wouldn't hurt to make sure that those talking are actually willing to talk things out. I mean Gold faction Sid only means that the individual is pro-solar not that they aren't very in favor of killing all the Lunars and there's always the risk that the Lunar is in favor of killing all the Sids as well. And I think we can all agree that negotiations tend to end poorly for peace if both sides are absolutely in favor of slaughtering each other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T16:30:13-07:00","id":524908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=523466#post523466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have. Unfortunatly the Dowager is kind of a super powerful psychotic recluse, and the agent sent in to find out may be compromised or may have purposefully developed the most awe inspiring case of DID the world has ever known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nalak you responded to one of my questions with this, but unfortunately I don't understand the sentence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What is DID? Can you please rephrase what you were trying to explain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T17:55:04-07:00","id":524956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524908#post524908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalak you responded to one of my questions with this, but unfortunately I don't understand the sentence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What is DID? Can you please rephrase what you were trying to explain?</div> </div> </div> </div>DID= Dissociative Identity Disorder. Multiple personality disorder basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T20:48:40-07:00","id":525060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524572#post524572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can be narrow-minded, hubristic, stubborn, biased, fallible jerks who pay too little attention to the wellbeing of mortals or their own madness ... but still smart, canny, competent, and able to think up new ideas when new problems arise. Their plans should be plausibly worthwhile even from an OOC perspective. They can be unequal to their self-appointed thrones without obvious incompetence/apathy. Their flaw doesn't need to be &quot;Out of Fate, out of mind.&quot; It can be subtler.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think everyone agrees the Blind Seers sidebar in 1st edition was one of the worst things ever published in the gameline. Holden certainly had a few memorable rants about it back when he was still posting as HLS. I think it's safe to say that the whole, &quot;Out of Fate, out of mind,&quot; will no longer be an assumption about Sidereals in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T21:50:21-07:00","id":525124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=525060#post525060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think everyone agrees the Blind Seers sidebar in 1st edition was one of the worst things ever published in the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Worst things ever published in the gameline&quot; has some heavyweights like V'neef Risa and Zeal in competition for that crown, don't forget. Though Blind Prophets is definitely top five.<br /> <br /> I actually just went back and re-read that sidebar, and it was like stepping into the Wayback Machine and visiting the oh-so-distant era of 2003. Perhaps the earliest known manifestation of &quot;Umm, errr, Sidereals kinda break the plot...what do we do about it?&quot; which, of course, ultimiatly culminated in the Lotus Massacre, an event that I have waxed poetic about many a time, singing nothing but the highest praise for such masterful storytelling.<br /> <br /> Man, what shit that was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Holden certainly had a few memorable rants about it back when he was still posting as HLS. </div> </div> </div>Know if they're saved anywhere? I think those would be interesting to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T22:50:25-07:00","id":525171,"title":"","content":"Stuff like V'neef Risa or Zeal are annoying, but they're kind of small single issues. Risa is one Dragon Blooded with a terrible backstory, and Zeal is a broken, high Essence Charm that isn't likely to pop up in standard gameplay anyway. The Blind Seers sidebar shat all over an entire splat, turning them into a bunch of incompetent blithering morons in a way that nothing else in the gameline has come close to doing (the, &quot;Infernals dare one another to rape Lilun&quot; is the only thing that can really compare, and that was just a throwaway line rather than a whole sidebar hammering the point home). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=525124#post525124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Know if they're saved anywhere? I think those would be interesting to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely they've vanished into the mists by this point; that was quite awhile ago. I wish I could find some of them though - they were rather funny and vitriolic enough to make Malfeas blush. His rants on the Blind Seers and Dean Shomshak were, what I would call, &quot;vintage Holden.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T04:38:27-07:00","id":525340,"title":"","content":"Can anyone post that sidebar about sidereals from 1st edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T06:59:10-07:00","id":525438,"title":"","content":"Nope! But I'll gladly summarize: &quot;Blind Prophets&quot; spends two long paragraphs explaining all we've been talking about here, how the Sids cannot see certain things outside of Fate and were blindsided by events stemming from there. But then, it goes into how theGreat Curse was responsible, and the Hubris it inflicts Seers with literally keeps them from realizing this very blindness exists. Sidereals, according to it, quite literally cannot even conceive of the notion that they or their plans might be wrong, despite blatant evidence to the contrary. Therefore, the master manipulators (as it calls them) can't see all the manipulations in Creation that cause major events threatening it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T08:13:32-07:00","id":525465,"title":"","content":"And this was in what book of 1st edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T08:31:18-07:00","id":525493,"title":"","content":"Exalted: The Sidereals, pg. 64","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T12:46:13-07:00","id":525796,"title":"","content":"Blind Seers is emblematic of a problem that Exalted has struggled with since the beginning, which is that things that require subtlety and nuance are instead taken way too far.<br /> <br /> Like, it makes total and complete sense that the way the Great Curse manifests within the Sidereals is via hubris, arrogance, and an inability to admit to themselves that they done fucked up. That makes sense for them, because it perverts their intended purpose in the grand scheme of things into something ultimately pretty horrific, as a good curse should. Great! Good stuff.<br /> <br /> It also makes sense that the Sidereals didn't see the Great Contagion and other major disasters coming because those disasters originate outside Fate and despite working really hard it, the entire Sidereal toolkit isn't designed with that in mind. So far, so good. Things make sense, and this is a good reason the Sidereals haven't seen this shit coming and stopped it, so we still have a setting.<br /> <br /> Really, what makes an otherwise serviceable sidebar completely break down are a bare two sentences:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their arrogance and hubris have blinded them to <b>even the possibility</b> that their prognostications may be in error or that there are things of which they are not aware </div> </div> </div>And<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It simply <b>doesn't occur</b> to them that they could be wrong. </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine in both cases.<br /> <br /> And that's shitty. That's a shitty curse. It precludes a lot of interesting possibilities, it makes the Sidereals less awesome, and in fact it contradicts greatly other parts of their splatbook, where it is pointed out that the Sidereals are very concerned and work very hard to gather information on shit they <i>know</i> they are ignorant about. It also makes them seem like idiots <i>within the setting</i>, which should never, ever be the case.<br /> <br /> Because you know what? It is true that there should be some Sidereals in whom their version of the Great Curse manifests as a stubborn, arrogant refusal to admit that they could be wrong and who meddle with things they don't understand because they're 100% convinced they do understand them, because they're so wise and powerful and control the world. Oh, sure, when pressed they'll admit they've fucked up in the past. But they won't really believe it. It was always somebody <i>else's</i> fault. <i>Their</i> plan was perfect. That should, certainly, be a thing.<br /> <br /> But there should also be Sidereals who are so consumed by doubt about ever having enough information, about knowing enough about everything, that it wraps them up in bureacratic paralysis, and they order study after fact-finding mission after reconnaissance report after committee meeting after analysis after analysis after analysis after <i>analysis</i> until the time when they should have acted, could have made a real difference, could have saved the world, has long since passed them by.<br /> <br /> It should <b>also</b> be a thing that there are Sidereals who for the most part have a realistic understanding of their own strengths and weaknesses, and carefully balance acting decisively with holding back until they're sure, but occasionally they get... nudged. They step back, and examine their plan, and think <i>Maybe I am wrong.</i> And the Great Curse slithers up to their ear and whispers <i>No, you're totally right and super awesome</i>. Sometimes they listen to that voice and don't scrap a plan they really should have.<br /> <br /> Those should all three be things! They make the Sidereals nuanced and interesting while still preserving the fact that the Great Curse has its hands around their hearts.<br /> <br /> All it would have taken to make that sidebar a thoroughly unremarkable information dump is just the tiniest bit of nuance. Instead, whoever wrote it got super overexcited.<br /> <br /> It's not the only time that had happened. &quot;The Gods are actually metaphysically incapable of ever respecting any Dragon-Blooded, ever&quot; is perhaps the masterpiece of that genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:00:47-07:00","id":525880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=525796#post525796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, it makes total and complete sense that the way the Great Curse manifests within the Sidereals is via hubris, arrogance, and an inability to admit to themselves that they done fucked up. That makes sense for them, because it perverts their intended purpose in the grand scheme of things into something ultimately pretty horrific, as a good curse should. Great! Good stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this, my opinion is that it's OK, but a little narrow.<br /> <br /> Compare the Solars - their Great Curse leads them to tyranny and misrule, yes, it subverts their role as champions and leaders. But the way it does so is through a number of different routes, through the twisting of the four virtues in a bunch of different ways depending on the individual. Wrath, depression, bitterness, pride, anger, paranoia, alienation, paralysis, contempt, fear, cruelty, and so on - the whole human suite.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice if the Sids had a bunch of different Compassion, Conviction, Valor, Temperance related curses that led to the place that they were supposed to go, to being advisors who give corrupt advice or make hubris fueled errors, ultimately, as a broad effect of what happens when these individual curses come together over time without that being spelled out mechanically.<br /> <br /> I think another advantage (beyond for its own sakes) of going through that idea of their role as advisors becoming corrupted through multiple routes and multiple emotions is it prevents that one note picture of Sidereals as just arrogant as forming.<br /> <br /> Just my feeling on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:02:50-07:00","id":526250,"title":"","content":"Ugh, long hard day at work, leg aches, and stupid keyboard is still gummed up, so for once I'mnot gonna take the time to correct my text,so sorry in advance.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=524511#post524511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They should not be portrayed as idiots -- as thinking the Great Contagion was no big deal and preventing the next one is unimportant -- as taking no effort anymore to prevent the Dragon-Blooded from becoming just as terrible as the First Age Solars. <i>If any books have portrayed them doing differently, somebody please say what.</i> <br /> &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. 1E Sid-book introduces the Convention on Plague, which became really important after the GC, and a big part of it is explicitly discovering the cause of the GC adn preventing another outbreak. 2E has the Convention on Deathlords, headed by Chehjop himself, which has a Sub-Convention called the Convention on Udr; thanks to recent info from Ragara Bhagwei, headmaster of the Heptagram, they have the first solid lead on where the GC came from in centuries, and are putting together a team (preferably young Gold Factioners, AKA your PCs) to go investigate the Dowager's swamp. This is all top secret, and it's noted that the Plague Convention would go apeshit if they learned they were cut out of the loop...<br /> <br /> So, someone's doing something about it. But honestly,it's a bit like 9/11: After that went down, folks went &quot;Do whatever you can to prevent this fromhappening again!&quot; And the gov put security measures in place. And some folks were like &quot;It's not enough! Do more!!&quot; And, at a certain point, you've really doneall you can do. You only have so many people, who can only work so many hours in a day. And guess what, your other issues andproblems aren't going away or putting themselves on hold, so you still have to deal withall that, too! <br /> <br /> Now imagine you only have about 70-80 agents to organize and apply to everything.<br /> <br /> Yes, The GC was just about the worst thingever. But, unless you've got actionable intel that's it's resurging *right now*...it can wait. It really has to, we've got Deathlords actually *moving into Creation*, Fae and Demon incursions left and right, Lunars leading barbarian hordes all over the place, and oh yeah, the frickin' Solars are back, on top of it all! Sadly, even CK can only juggle so many balls at once...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:11:50-07:00","id":526259,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, where are people getting the idea that the Jade Obelisks shielding Creation's borders were deliberately destroyed/moved? The Wyld Compass says that they're still there. The FA Lawgiversdidn't bother moving them when expanding the world's borders, but when the Fair Folk invaded, the border fell back to that point and stuck. Some were destroyed by powerful invading Fae, but a great many survive. They weigh about 100 tons, so they're pretty hard to move, and there are many tribesand communities that live near them in the zones of stability they create; when Wyld Storms blow through, vastly different groups of beastmen, barbarians andWyld mutants huddle around them, watching each other very carefully!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:37:48-07:00","id":526325,"title":"","content":"It was asked: Was the reign of the Solars really that bad, such that the worst excesses of the Scarlet Dynasty are worth propping up? <br /> <br /> I imagine every now and then, an Elder who lived through that time is asked this by a younger Seer. He looks them right in the eye,and says &quot;I know what you're thinking. That we are exaggerating how bad things were to justify our secret control. Or we're just delusional or outright lying. I understand why you might think this, and applaud you for being skeptical. But you'll just have to take my word for it when I tell you: Yes. Yes, it really was just. That. Bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it was. DotFA is set before things got really bad and became a dystopia, so details are still sketchy, but one book tells us that, by the time of the Usurpation, something like one in every 100 mortals living on the Blessed Isle knew someone who had been murdered or molested in some way by a Solar. Out of the millions of people living there, that's horrifying!<br /> <br /> Before they acted, the Sids discovered a conspiracy of mortals who were going to attempt to overthrow theirrulers; they covered it up, not because they felt they could use them for the Usurpation,but because they were genuinely afraid of what would happen to all those people when they were found out!<br /> <br /> Even in the Dreams time, we see Solars who do such things as mutate the humans living in their principalities into new races of inhuman creatures against their wills. And there are laws protecting mortals, specifically Accords against mutating,mutilating or otherwise altering their souls (which is well beyond DB capacity), which many solars were willing to break, either openly if they ruled a Tributary, or covertly, which some others covered up because they didn't want the Deliberative telling THEM what not to do. <br /> <br /> Don't forget, the Soalrs also invented teh Soulbreaker Orbs. In a world where the soul is a verifiable thing, guaranteed to survive any amount of violence to the body so someone can start over witha fresh life, think of how horrible such a thing is! No wonder that Lookshy deploying one against the REalm troops is considered oneof the most unforgivably heinous war crimes of the Second Age...<br /> <br /> Then there's the Agony Organ, a torture device that applied pain to wrench a single perfect note from the mortals inserted into it; the Solar who created it played long symphonies of complex melodies composed of the agonized screams of his victims...Apparently, a big hit among his fellow Lawgivers! Now, can you imagine a Dynast openly trying to get away with some shit like that??<br /> <br /> On a larger scale, Solars were fucking around with the Sidereals,gods and heaven in other ways. Not only were they imprisoning Spirits for minor &quot;offenses&quot; (like sorcerously binding that Elemental Dragon under An-Teng and binding a Spirit insidethe Brass Leviathan, both just because those spirits didn't want to hang with those Solars), and experimenting on the Pattern Spiders (only stopping when the Maidens themselves asked them to), but when the Sids warned them that the large amounts ofEssence they were using was having unforseen effects on the Loom of Fate, their reaction was to deliberately *increase* the amounts of Essence they were applying, just to see what would happen!<br /> <br /> If the worst started to happen, many didn't care, as they were planning to reshapethe entire world into a more pleasing shape, anyway. Something round, perhaps, or maybe cubical? Seriously,there were entire political cliques centering around what shape they should force the world into! And don't even get me started on Operation: Wyldhand...<br /> <br /> One of the creators once stated that the Usurpation went down because the Solars were increasingly coming to the same answer to the question, What need have we for Man and Gods?: None.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:50:57-07:00","id":526328,"title":"","content":"Why dothe Sids act as though all Solars will go bad? Because when they did forecasts back in the FA, they sawthat *every single Solar* eventually went crazy...except for one, the Queen of (what is now) Whitewall. and they killed her, too, because they couldn't make exceptions at that point. Interesting thought, if she (and her successor) were somehow immune to the GC for whatever reason...<br /> <br /> Arguably, the Sids were right not to take the Gold Path, as they were also twisted by the Curse, and couldn't really remove the mote from their brother's eye without clearing their own eyes out first! Their reformation attempt would almost certainly have been doomed to failure. Maybe. One of the books mentions that the Maidens were present (thogiving no sign of approval or disapproval) at the Great Prophecy; there was a fan theory awhile back, based on the fact that the Maiden of Secrets is one of two beings who knows aboutthe GC, that if the Sids had chosen the impossible Gold way, then she would have divulged that knowledge to them (possibly moved by Samsara,which wasn't a thing back then), enabling them to eventually cure all the Exalted, and raise a new, even greater Age as the Gold Prophecy described!<br /> <br /> Had moreto say here,but can't recall where Iwas going with it. Oh well, posting it anyway...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T03:36:09-07:00","id":526514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=525493#post525493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted: The Sidereals, pg. 64</div> </div> </div> </div>WOW!!!!<br /> So this thing was on the sidereals almost* from the start.<br /> So what's the point of us discussing sidereal motives and process after that? The sidereals are incompetent pricks full of hubris, and have been almost from the start of their (game) history. Mystery solved.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *i say almost because it could be around since 1E core book or the player companion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T04:10:01-07:00","id":526526,"title":"","content":"People who have not read the book should keep the usual hyperbole in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T04:24:48-07:00","id":526531,"title":"","content":"The Blind Seer sidebar actually made me in favour of Sidereals getting a limit track in 2e since the logic of a lot of people was &quot;we don't know when Sidereals have their actions influenced by the Great Curse, therefore we'll assume it's a 24/7 thing&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T08:19:01-07:00","id":526668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So what's the point of us discussing sidereal motives and process after that? The sidereals are incompetent pricks full of hubris, and have been almost from the start of their (game) history. Mystery solved. </div> </div> </div>Because Blnd Seers was contradicted in much of the rest of the canon (and not just a little contradicted, a lot contradicted) and superseded by 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=526531#post526531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blind Seer sidebar actually made me in favour of Sidereals getting a limit track in 2e since the logic of a lot of people was &quot;we don't know when Sidereals have their actions influenced by the Great Curse, therefore we'll assume it's a 24/7 thing&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why we can't have nice things, because they were literally the only type of Exalt who the developers allowed to have a completely player-driven experience with their Great Curse interaction, and people fucked it up left, right, and center.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T11:13:07-07:00","id":526847,"title":"","content":"Hand-of-Omega, thank you for answering the questions I've been asking. You cleared up a lot of the things that prompted me to enter this thread and ask the initial questions I asked.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=526250#post526250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. 1E Sid-book introduces the Convention on Plague, which became really important after the GC, and a big part of it is explicitly discovering the cause of the GC adn preventing another outbreak.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this was actually something they started soon after the Contagion, not in the past 5 years? And have continued doing and still consider <b><i>important</i></b>? But, they haven't found enough evidence yet to get to the cause so they don't have the info to make concrete plans to prevent future outbreaks?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=526259#post526259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, where are people getting the idea that the Jade Obelisks shielding Creation's borders were deliberately destroyed/moved?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know ultimately where, I only learned of the Obelisks on this forum so I can only go by what others post about them, as vanished wonders. Or somebody wrote something that I misinterpreted to mean that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T11:24:17-07:00","id":526851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=526847#post526847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand-of-Omega, thank you for answering the questions I've been asking. You cleared up a lot of the things that prompted me to enter this thread and ask the initial questions I asked.<br /> So this was actually something they started soon after the Contagion, not in the past 5 years? And have continued doing and still consider <b><i>important</i></b>? But, they haven't found enough evidence yet to get to the cause so they don't have the info to make concrete plans to prevent future outbreaks?</div> </div> </div> </div>NP. The Plague Convention had been around since forever, but really only got important after the Contagion, yes. Very much so, yes. And yes.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:53:12-07:00","id":527117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=526847#post526847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand-of-Omega, thank you for answering the questions I've been asking. You cleared up a lot of the things that prompted me to enter this thread and ask the initial questions I asked.<br /> So this was actually something they started soon after the Contagion, not in the past 5 years? And have continued doing and still consider <b><i>important</i></b>? But, they haven't found enough evidence yet to get to the cause so they don't have the info to make concrete plans to prevent future outbreaks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that the Great Contagion was the result of a deeply reclusive Deathlord pulling it out of a literal hole in the universe and unleashing it. She maybe told the Neverborn, her colleagues, and perhaps a tiny handful of trusted servants. The Great Contagion itself is so deadly that Sidereals who examined it too closely on the Loom actually contracted it; <i>that's</i> how contagious it is.<br /> <br /> Given that, it is really not surprising that the Sidereals have had trouble tracking it back to its source. They have poor penetration into the Underworld to begin with and their penetration into the inner councils of the Deathlords is basically nonexistent.<br /> <br /> As for planning on how to prevent future outbreaks... I don't think you <i>can</i>. Damn near everything in Creation currently is the descendant of someone or something that was immune to the Contagion, so planning against that specific disease hitting again isn't all that useful. But let's assume that someone creates Great Contagion 2.0, which does the same thing as the first one did. How, precisely, do you contain something that virulent once it is out in the wild?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T17:55:24-07:00","id":527212,"title":"","content":"Oh man are we discussing the Usurpation and the Contagion as they relate to Sidereals again? Alright let me get this warning for what you're about to read out of the way, given numerous problems that have happened when the game approached it badly:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/lWvKN2p.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why? It's the same problem the game has had with a lot of other things; it's taken a decent idea and portrayed it without nuance.<br /> <br /> The core concept of hubris is pretty central to Sidereals; even if you think that everything they did was 100% totally awesomely correct, the specter of it hangs over everything they do. When you're the secret masters making decisions for everyone in the world based on your Objectively Correct Analysis of the Inevitable Truths You've Foreseen, the doubt that you might be overestimating your own abilities or overstepping your right to make choices for other people hangs over everything you do. The Usurpation is just the most obvious example; simply <i>being a Sidereal</i> involves making decisions for other people, constantly. It's a big part of what a Sidereal is and what it means to manipulate Fate.<br /> <br /> This is sort of core to their story, so the game was never intended to say &quot;the Great Prophecy was absolutely totally reliable and 100% correct with no chance that it allowed any other options&quot; (obviously.) Nobody gets to know that they made the Objectively Right Decision. But it's stumbled repeatedly on how exactly to portray this uncertainty.<br /> <br /> Problem 1: If the prophecy isn't reliable enough for the Sidereal's decisions to make sense, then you make them look like doofs. Honestly I think that this is the easiest problem to solve, which is why I'm baffled that the game has repeatedly stumbled over it -- I think they wanted to tie it into some sort of mechanics for how Sidereal prophecy works? But it's not really hard. What I would say is that prophecy (even flawless prophecy) involves interpretation, which is inevitably subjective and flawed and never completely correct. The Sidereals are the absolute best people in the world at interpreting prophecy, and pretty much all of them got together to interpret this big prophecy, so their interpretation is as good as it was likely to get. But it's not perfect. And they knew that, and decided that that uncertainty was acceptable given the seriousness of the problem they faced.<br /> <br /> Problem 2: If you approach it badly, you end up with an irritatingly oversimplified Trolley Car Problem choice. This is my problem with most of the discussions people have had about it so far and the Bronze Prophecy / Gold Prophecy way that the game eventually went to resolve the problem. All of Creation is tied to the tracks with a trolley heading towards it, and you can pull a lever to redirect it to 300 Solars and their magical empire... no. That's dumb. The choice wasn't made in some sort of rarified vacuum of Freshman Philosophy logic. It involved deeply personal bonds of fear and love and loyalty, temptations of power and sentiment, their responsibility to Creation and its people (and what exactly it meant), and so on. Each individual Sidereal had their own reasons to end up with the answer they did.<br /> <br /> The Great Contagion (and the idea that the Sidereals didn't see it coming) does serve at least one important purpose in dragging their decision-making out of that Trolley Car Problem space by making it clear that they did not and could not see everything. It sort of pulls the rug out from under you if you tried to approach it in the simplest way possible.. but it doesn't really make it <i>that</i> much more interesting if you stop there. It's ultimately just a cheap twist, used like that, so I think that it sort of overstayed its welcome and became stale as The One Problem With the Usurpation. (I mean, you can lump the other outside-fate stuff the Sidereals didn't foresee into here, it doesn't change anything.) &quot;Maybe you didn't see everything&quot; is <i>one</i> thorny issue raised by the Usurpation, but hardly the only one, and the important question isn't really whether they did or not -- because the game obviously requires that their visions and ability to interpret them have limits -- but the human feelings and loyalties and ambitions and fears that drove them to decide that what they'd foreseen and the reading they'd managed was accurate <i>enough</i>.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, it doesn't really matter whether their prophecies are 99% accurate or 98% accurate, or whether the exact reason for the flaws is because of Fate or because they chose to ignore an alternative or whatever -- those are distractions, we already know what they decided. What matters (and the reason why those flaws are necessary) is why they made the decision they did. That's what really characterizes Sidereals. The Usurpation happened a long time ago, so the details are really only important in terms of history; but the kinds of human bonds Sidereals wrestle with when they're forced to decide whether to interfere in a fate that would kill <i>this</i> guy or <i>that</i> guy, depending on their choice? That's what's really matters.<br /> <br /> Asking whether the Gold Faction or the Bronze Faction are right or not (or whether the details of the Contagion or whatever <i>prove</i> one side was objectively correct) is silly. I mean, we can argue over it, sure, but if you can find something in the book that seems to make it 100% clear what the right decision is, that just means you've found something that shouldn't have been printed. I <i>think</i> that, on the balance, the game is generally meant to portray the Usurpation as a failure on the part of the Sidereals (as part of a tragedy where all the Exalted failed.) The backstory is meant to show all the Exalted in the past ages having somehow fallen short of their full potential so that you, in the present, can look beyond them and do better. And -- to the extent that there's a default right or wrong way for characters to approach the setting, which obviously isn't really a thing, but to the extent that the writers inevitably have assumptions like that -- I'm pretty sure that &quot;get stuck on this old decision, keep repeating old squabbles forever&quot; means you're probably screwing things up somewhere. The game is at least a bit more upbeat than <i>that</i>.<br /> <br /> (You might consider exactly when and where they failed, though. The First Age shouldn't have gotten to the point where the Great Prophecy was even necessary; and the Sidereals bear some responsibility for that, too. Maybe if they'd seen the direction things were headed in sooner, they could have repaired the world's fate without taking such desperate measures? The Usurpation itself attracts a lot of attention because it's the crux where everything came to a head, but ultimately it was the result of over three-thousand years of accumulated bad choices by the Exalted as a whole. Even if the Usurpation was necessary, fixating on that choice tends to miss the bigger picture.)<br /> <br /> But that's all very subjective, and my point is you're not going to find an answer to that kind of question by analyzing the details of the game's history, by trying to read too much into the mechanics of Fate or the Contagion or anything like that. It's more useful to think of the kind of overarching backstory Creation's history is meant to give you -- imperfect but hopeful, with generations of Exalted past who were heroic and larger than life and who earnestly fought for their ideals but whose actions ultimately fed into a tragedies that gave us the Age of Sorrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-24-2015, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:00:37-07:00","id":527216,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the Contagion hitting was one of the biggest selling points of the Gold Faction for a long time... the idea that the peerless physicians of the Solar Host &quot;would have found a way&quot;.<br /> <br /> And they're probably right, since the best medics in the universe have always been Solars. Dragon-blooded medicine looks a lot more like battlefield triage, in a lot of ways, though vastly more effective obviously. Lunar Medicine focuses a lot more on curing the LUNAR than it does anyone else, and even if the Lunar could protect a small group of people Lunars don't really seem to do vast-scale effects well, they focus more on the personal. Sidereal Medicine is wonky as hell.<br /> <br /> The Alchemicals probably could've figured it out, if they were around at the time, though whether they could've done so in time might be debatable. An Infernal solution to the problem might look worse than the Contagion itself. Abyssals would've obviously had less interest in solving the issue but theoretically could've found some way to kill the heck out of the Contagion, maybe. Probably a way that also killed everyone afflicted by it. Which wouldn't necessarily be better.<br /> <br /> But the Solars, presumably, who're by far the best at vast-scale far-reaching effects that draw upon their peerless skill and unfathomable might to envelop the world in their golden solutions, probably would've been able to do the job. At least in time to stop it from hitting 90% of everybody. Presumably it'd've involved the Wyld somehow, since a Solar researcher who discovered the origin of the Contagion (as some Solar Circle of heroes may well have done, in this case I'm referring to the Well of Udr and not the Dowager herself) could've theorized that infinite entropic possibility might be countered by infinite creative possibility.<br /> <br /> But that's just a theory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd like to specify of course that none of this necessarily speaks to the Solars being &quot;automatically better&quot; than everyone else, for those who might be inclined to think so.<br /> <br /> Just that in this case, they really were the best option for dealing with the problem at hand, and that they were, for obvious reasons, not available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5771,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","user":"Krata Lightblade","date":". 05-24-2015, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:41:31-07:00","id":527228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=527212#post527212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? It's the same problem the game has had with a lot of other things; it's taken a decent idea and portrayed it without nuance.<br /> <br /> The core concept of hubris is pretty central to Sidereals; even if you think that everything they did was 100% totally awesomely correct, the specter of it hangs over everything they do. When you're the secret masters making decisions for everyone in the world based on your Objectively Correct Analysis of the Inevitable Truths You've Foreseen, the doubt that you might be overestimating your own abilities or overstepping your right to make choices for other people hangs over everything you do. The Usurpation is just the most obvious example; simply <i>being a Sidereal</i> involves making decisions for other people, constantly. It's a big part of what a Sidereal is and what it means to manipulate Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aquillion, I don't just want to &quot;like&quot; this paragraph. I want to meet it's eyes as we both reach for the same book in the library, ask it out to ice cream, learn about all of it's hopes and dreams over a tumultuous two year courtship that I almost completely fuck up because of ill-advised flirting with one of Coik's comments, and then propose to it using my grandmother's heirloom engagement ring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problem 1: If the prophecy isn't reliable enough for the Sidereal's decisions to make sense, then you make them look like doofs. Honestly I think that this is the easiest problem to solve, which is why I'm baffled that the game has repeatedly stumbled over it -- I think they wanted to tie it into some sort of mechanics for how Sidereal prophecy works? </div> </div> </div>I sort of feel like at this point, it might be a good idea of the devs just completely went nuclear on this issue and were very, very explicit that the Great Prophecy isn't mechanically modellable, that gathering the entire Five-Score Fellowship in one place at one time to preform their greatest feat of prognostication ever did <i>not</i> just involve mass spamming of &quot;Of Things Desired and Feared&quot; by old people with a shit-ton of Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Asking whether the Gold Faction or the Bronze Faction are right or not (or whether the details of the Contagion or whatever <i>prove</i> one side was objectively correct) is silly. </div> </div> </div>Mm, it depends on the context of the question, I think.<br /> <br /> The clear <i>intent</i> of the materiel is that we don't know which faction is right. We <i>can't</i> know. The whole point is for individual PCs to come to that decision on their own, or to reject both choices. It's part of the personal journey of both individual Sidereals and their society as a whole.<br /> <br /> However, in order for that journey to have meaning, it means the setting has to support both choices as potentially valid. There is, of course, no pleasing everybody. But for a lot of people, verisimilitude is a huge deal, and they dislike it if the setting is nominally neutral towards something when the facts at hand seem to point clearly to a correct answer. It is often the case that when a person says &quot;Well, Gold/Bronze is clearly and obviously right here&quot; it says more about <i>them</i> than the faction in question, but in the context of &quot;Does the setting support factional uncertainty to an acceptable degree?&quot; the question of which faction is right is useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that's all very subjective, and my point is you're not going to find an answer to that kind of question by analyzing the details of the game's history, by trying to read too much into the mechanics of Fate or the Contagion or anything like that. It's more useful to think of the kind of overarching backstory Creation's history is meant to give you -- imperfect but hopeful, with generations of Exalted past who were heroic and larger than life and who earnestly fought for their ideals but whose actions ultimately fed into a tragedies that gave us the Age of Sorrows. </div> </div> </div>See, I agree with what you're saying here, but I feel it worth noting that for many people, and I include myself here, it is difficult to get to where the setting is meant to take you if it feels like the road leading there is badly constructed. We analyze the setting history and the mechanics thereof because that's how we relate to the setting, and if the road doesn't seem like it should logically lead to the destination it is supposed to we get... itchy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T18:54:02-07:00","id":527234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/506852-sidereals-how-much-is-forgotten?p=527228#post527228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The clear <i>intent</i> of the materiel is that we don't know which faction is right. We <i>can't</i> know. The whole point is for individual PCs to come to that decision on their own, or to reject both choices. It's part of the personal journey of both individual Sidereals and their society as a whole.<br /> <br /> However, in order for that journey to have meaning, it means the setting has to support both choices as potentially valid. There is, of course, no pleasing everybody. But for a lot of people, verisimilitude is a huge deal, and they dislike it if the setting is nominally neutral towards something when the facts at hand seem to point clearly to a correct answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's also necessary for all the books to be equally ambiguous about it. I don't know whether this is part of the problem that lead to my confusion, but <i><b>hypothetically</b></i> if an issue is supposed to be ambiguous yet some books present facts that entirely support one side, and other books present facts that entire support another side, then a reader is left feeling like the road makes no sense, depending on what books they have on hand, unless they happen to get a book from each camp. That's fine in the World of Darkness where every book is written from an obviously first-person, in-character perspective, and readers should assume they're full of bias and ignorance. It isn't fine in Exalted because the books mostly have an omniscient narrator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}